INSERT INTO _s463ea VALUES
(45375,'S','1-adam-eve',3,10,'1-adam-eve',3,10,$n$Jubilees 3:29 — *And He sent out of the Garden of Eden all flesh that was in the Garden of Eden, and all flesh was scattered according to its kinds, and according to its types to the places which had been created for them.* The same primeval record of the expulsion that frames the gate-scene of 1 Adam and Eve 3:10 — one history of the driven-out, kept in both books.$n$,$n$And again, when Adam was by the gate of the garden, and saw the cherub with a sword of flashing fire in his hand, and the cherub grew angry and frowned at him, both Adam and Eve became afraid of him, and thought he meant to put them to death. So they fell on their faces, trembled with fear.$n$,false),
(45376,'S','1-adam-eve',3,15,'1-adam-eve',3,15,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The "Word of Yahuah" who comes to Adam and Eve and raises them up (1 Adam and Eve 3:15) is the Word who would be made flesh and dwell among men.$n$,$n$And the Word of Yahuah (Lord) came to Adam and Eve, and raised them up.$n$,false),
(45377,'S','1-adam-eve',3,14,'1-adam-eve',3,14,$n$Psalms 91:11 — *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* The Angel Elohim sends "to keep the garden" (1 Adam and Eve 3:14) is the same mercy that gives His angels charge to keep His own.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) had pity on them, and showed them mercy, and sent His Angel to keep the garden.$n$,false),
(45378,'S','1-adam-eve',3,10,'1-adam-eve',3,10,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The cherub "with a sword of flashing fire" at the gate (1 Adam and Eve 3:10) is the very cherub and flaming sword Yahuah set to keep the way of the tree of life.$n$,$n$And again, when Adam was by the gate of the garden, and saw the cherub with a sword of flashing fire in his hand, and the cherub grew angry and frowned at him, both Adam and Eve became afraid of him, and thought he meant to put them to death. So they fell on their faces, trembled with fear.$n$,false),
(45379,'S','1-adam-eve',3,9,'1-adam-eve',3,9,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The covenant Elohim makes with the lifted-up Adam (1 Adam and Eve 3:9) is fulfilled when the Son is manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$,$n$And as Adam went to it he feared, trembled and fell down; but Elohim (God) in His mercy lifted him up, and then made this covenant with him.$n$,false),
(45380,'S','1-adam-eve',3,9,'1-adam-eve',3,9,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The mercy that lifts the fallen Adam and seals a covenant (1 Adam and Eve 3:9) carries the same promise — Satan bruised under foot shortly.$n$,$n$And as Adam went to it he feared, trembled and fell down; but Elohim (God) in His mercy lifted him up, and then made this covenant with him.$n$,false),
(45381,'S','1-adam-eve',3,7,'1-adam-eve',3,7,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The covenant made "by the tree where Eve took of the fruit" (1 Adam and Eve 3:7) is the seed-promise spoken over the serpent at that same fall.$n$,$n$But before that, Elohim (God) had made this covenant with our father, Adam, in the same terms, before he came out of the garden, when he was by the tree where Eve took of the fruit and gave it to him to eat.$n$,false),
(45382,'S','1-adam-eve',3,2,'1-adam-eve',3,2,$n$Hebrews 1:2 — *Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds;* The Word promised to save "when the five and a half days are fulfilled" (1 Adam and Eve 3:2) is the Son who in the last days speaks and by whom the worlds were made.$n$,$n$Yes, the Word that will again save you when the five and a half days are fulfilled."$n$,false),
(45383,'S','1-adam-eve',3,6,'1-adam-eve',3,6,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour appointed to a fixed term in 1 Adam and Eve 3:6 is the Lamb foreordained before the foundation of the world.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) in his mercy for Adam who was made after His own image and likeness, explained to him, that these were 5,000 and 500 years; and how One would then come and save him and his descendants.$n$,false),
(45384,'S','1-adam-eve',3,6,'1-adam-eve',3,6,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "5,000 and 500 years" until One comes to save (1 Adam and Eve 3:6) is the fulness of time at which the Son was sent forth.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) in his mercy for Adam who was made after His own image and likeness, explained to him, that these were 5,000 and 500 years; and how One would then come and save him and his descendants.$n$,false),
(45385,'S','1-adam-eve',3,1,'1-adam-eve',3,1,$n$Colossians 1:16 — *For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:* The Word "that created you" in 1 Adam and Eve 3:1 is the One by whom all things were made.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) said to Adam, "I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen.$n$,false),
(45386,'S','1-adam-eve',3,2,'1-adam-eve',3,2,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The Word who "will again save you" (1 Adam and Eve 3:2) is the Word made flesh to come and save what was fallen.$n$,$n$Yes, the Word that will again save you when the five and a half days are fulfilled."$n$,false),
(45387,'S','1-adam-eve',3,1,'1-adam-eve',3,1,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* This is exactly the Word "that created you" of 1 Adam and Eve 3:1 — the Maker of Adam is the Saviour of Adam.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) said to Adam, "I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen.$n$,false),
(45388,'S','1-adam-eve',3,1,'1-adam-eve',3,1,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word Elohim promises to send Adam is the One who was with Elohim from the beginning, naming the Logos at the very first day outside Eden in 1 Adam and Eve 3:1.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) said to Adam, "I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen.$n$,false),
(45404,'S','1-adam-eve',5,8,'1-adam-eve',5,8,$n$1 Timothy 2:15 — *Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety.* As Eve fears to stand *one and alone* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:8, Sha'ul holds out the woman's saving hope through the seed and the faith she keeps.$n$,$n$But if You do not bring him back to life, then, O Elohim (God), take away my own soul, that I be like him, and leave me not in this dungeon, one and alone; for I could not stand alone in this world, but with him only.$n$,false),
(45405,'S','1-adam-eve',5,13,'1-adam-eve',5,13,$n$Genesis 2:24 — *Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh.* Eve's plea that she and Adam *die the same day* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:13 is the one-flesh bond of Eden refusing to be sundered even by death.$n$,$n$But if You will not give him life, then take me, even me, like him; that we both may die the same day."$n$,false),
(45406,'S','1-adam-eve',5,7,'1-adam-eve',5,7,$n$Romans 5:17 — *For if by one man's offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by one, Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ).* The life and standing Eve begs for Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 5:7 is the reign-in-life that grace secures over the fall.$n$,$n$Don't take away his soul right now; but let him live that he may stand after the measure of his repentance, and do Your will, as before his death.$n$,false),
(45407,'S','1-adam-eve',5,6,'1-adam-eve',5,6,$n$2 Corinthians 7:10 — *For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death.* Eve's prayer that Adam be raised *that he may cry and repent* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:6 is exactly the sorrow-unto-life Sha'ul distinguishes from the world's sorrow-unto-death.$n$,$n$O Elohim (God), look at this Your servant fallen in this manner, and bring him back to life, that he may cry and repent of his transgression which he committed through me.$n$,false),
(45408,'S','1-adam-eve',5,9,'1-adam-eve',5,9,$n$Jubilees 3:5 — *And Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and he slept, and He took for the woman one rib from amongst his ribs, and this rib was the origin of the woman from amongst his ribs, and He built up the flesh in its stead, and built the woman.* The restored books keep one primeval history: Jubilees tells the same making of woman that Eve recites in 1 Adam and Eve 5:9-10.$n$,$n$For You, O Elohim (God), caused him to fall asleep, and took a bone from his side, and restored the flesh in the place of it, by Your divine power.$n$,false),
(45409,'S','1-adam-eve',5,11,'1-adam-eve',5,11,$n$Genesis 2:23 — *And Adam said, This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.* Eve's cry that *I and he are one* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:11 echoes Adam's first word over her in Eden.$n$,$n$O Yahuah (Lord), I and he are one, and You, O Elohim (God), are our Creator, You are He who made us both in one day.$n$,false),
(45410,'S','1-adam-eve',5,9,'1-adam-eve',5,9,$n$Genesis 2:21 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof.* This is the very act Eve recounts to Yahuah in 1 Adam and Eve 5:9, the bone taken from Adam's side and the flesh restored.$n$,$n$For You, O Elohim (God), caused him to fall asleep, and took a bone from his side, and restored the flesh in the place of it, by Your divine power.$n$,false),
(45411,'S','1-adam-eve',5,5,'1-adam-eve',5,5,$n$Romans 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned.* The fall from light into darkness Eve laments in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 is the entrance of sin and death that Sha'ul traces back to Eden.$n$,$n$For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison.$n$,false),
(45412,'S','1-adam-eve',5,5,'1-adam-eve',5,5,$n$1 Timothy 2:14 — *And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression.* Sha'ul's verdict matches Eve's own self-judgment in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 that she alone brought Adam down.$n$,$n$For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison.$n$,false),
(45413,'S','1-adam-eve',5,4,'1-adam-eve',5,4,$n$Genesis 3:13 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the woman, What is this that thou hast done? And the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.* Eve's plea that Yahuah forgive and not remember her sin in 1 Adam and Eve 5:4 unfolds the confession first wrung from her at the tree.$n$,$n$Then she got up, spread her hands toward Elohim (God), appealing to Him for mercy and pity, and said, "O Elohim (God), forgive me my sin, the sin which I committed, and don't remember it against me.$n$,false),
(45414,'S','1-adam-eve',5,5,'1-adam-eve',5,5,$n$Genesis 3:6 — *And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat.* This is the very deed Eve confesses in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 when she says she alone caused Adam to fall from the garden.$n$,$n$For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison.$n$,false),
(45415,'S','1-adam-eve',6,10,'1-adam-eve',6,10,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Against the curse held over the hardened in 1 Adam and Eve 6:10 stands the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$,$n$But, if on the contrary, they still continue hardened in their transgression, they shall be under a curse forever."$n$,false),
(45453,'S','1-adam-eve',8,2,'1-adam-eve',8,2,$n$1 Corinthians 13:12 — *For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known.* Adam who once could "see things far away" now sees "only near at hand" — the darkened glass of a fallen race awaiting restored sight.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) Yahuah (Lord) said to Adam, "When you were under subjection to Me, you had a bright nature within you, and for that reason could you see things far away. But after your transgression your bright nature was withdrawn from you; and it was not left to you to see things far away, but only near at hand; after the ability of the flesh; for it is brutish."$n$,false),
(45517,'S','1-adam-eve',13,12,'1-adam-eve',13,12,$n$Ephesians 5:8 — *For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in Yahusha (Lord): walk as children of light:* Those Elohim made to do their work in the day's light are called to walk as the children of light He willed from the first.$n$,$n$Strengthen your heart, and be not afraid. This darkness is not a punishment. But, O Adam, I have made the day, and have placed the sun in it to give light; in order that you and your children should do your work.$n$,false),
(45529,'S','1-adam-eve',13,3,'1-adam-eve',13,3,$n$*But when he transgressed My commandment, I deprived him of that bright nature, and he became dark.* (1 Adam and Eve 13:3). *How art thou fallen from heaven, O Lucifer, son of the morning! how art thou cut down to the ground, which didst weaken the nations!* (Isaiah 14:12). Isaiah speaks of one who fell from heaven, called the son of the morning, and cut down to the ground. In 1 Adam and Eve, Elohim (God) tells Adam of an angel who once carried a bright light and lost it by breaking the commandment, so that he became dark. The two verses describe the same fall from two sides: Isaiah names the height and the cutting down, and Elohim (God) names what was taken from him. Both say that the one who fell had been bright before he transgressed.$n$,$n$But when he transgressed My commandment, I deprived him of that bright nature, and he became dark.$n$,true),
(45537,'S','1-adam-eve',14,4,'1-adam-eve',14,4,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Yahuah's "But I will" save you (14:4) is the manifested Son destroying the very works of Satan whose hand held Adam.$n$,$n$But I will. When I shall come down from heaven, and shall become flesh of your descendants, and take on Myself the infirmity from which you suffer, then the darkness that covered you in this cave shall cover Me in the grave, when I am in the flesh of your descendants.$n$,false),
(45542,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$1 Peter 1:19 — *But with the precious blood of Messiah (Christ), as of a lamb without blemish and without spot:* — the suffering for salvation promised in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is purchased by the spotless blood of the Lamb.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45543,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The salvation Adam mourns over in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is exactly this — the Son manifested to suffer and undo the works of the serpent.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45544,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The suffering Elohim foretold in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is the bruised heel of the woman's seed crushing the serpent's head.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45545,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* — the same Elohim who spake to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 with the word of His coming suffering.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45546,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* — Adam hears in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 of a salvation already foreordained before the world, manifest only in the last times.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45547,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The promise of 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 — that Elohim should suffer — is kept when the Word takes flesh to suffer for our salvation.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45548,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Elohim who in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 told Adam He should suffer for their salvation is the eternal Word, the Logos who speaks with Adam outside the garden.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45549,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The barred return of 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 ends here, when the way to the tree of life is opened again at the fulfillment of the days.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45550,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* — the fulfillment of the days decreed in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is the appointed coming of the seed of the woman.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45551,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The flaming sword is why Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 may not return until the days decreed are fulfilled.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45552,'S','1-adam-eve',15,1,'1-adam-eve',15,1,$n$Genesis 3:23 — *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.* This is the very expulsion 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 weeps over, the LORD's word that they should not return to the garden.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve cried and sorrowed by reason of Elohim's (God's) word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation.$n$,false),
(45568,'S','1-adam-eve',17,2,'1-adam-eve',17,2,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The serpent that became Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 17:2 is the devil who sinned from the beginning, whose works the Son of Elohim came to destroy.$n$,$n$But as they went near it, before the western gate, from which Satan came when he deceived Adam and Eve, they found the serpent that became Satan coming at the gate, and sorrowfully licking the dust, and wiggling on its breast on the ground, by reason of the curse that fell on it from Elohim (God).$n$,false),
(45574,'S','1-adam-eve',18,5,'1-adam-eve',18,5,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The contrast is sharp: in 1 Adam and Eve 18:5 a true angel of Yahuah delivers Adam and Eve, where elsewhere Satan only counterfeits the angelic to deceive them.$n$,$n$But Elohim (God) sent an angel who threw the serpent away from them, and raised them up.$n$,false),
(45575,'S','1-adam-eve',18,7,'1-adam-eve',18,7,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word silencing the serpent's deceiving speech in 1 Adam and Eve 18:7 foreshadows the Son manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$,$n$This time, however, you will be mute, and you and your race will speak no more; because, the first time My creatures were ruined because of you, and this time you tried to kill them."$n$,false),
(45576,'S','1-adam-eve',18,6,'1-adam-eve',18,6,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* The same Word who made the serpent and gave it speech now removes it in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6-7 — the Maker disposing of His own creature.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to the serpent, and said to it, "The first time I made you slick, and made you to go on your belly; but I did not deprive you of speech.$n$,false),
(45577,'S','1-adam-eve',18,6,'1-adam-eve',18,6,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes to the serpent and pronounces judgment in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6 is the eternal Word of the prologue.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to the serpent, and said to it, "The first time I made you slick, and made you to go on your belly; but I did not deprive you of speech.$n$,false),
(45578,'S','1-adam-eve',18,6,'1-adam-eve',18,6,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The Word's sentence against the serpent in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6 is the same bruising of Satan the gospel promises.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to the serpent, and said to it, "The first time I made you slick, and made you to go on your belly; but I did not deprive you of speech.$n$,false),
(45579,'S','1-adam-eve',18,4,'1-adam-eve',18,4,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The serpent that still tries to kill though already cursed in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 is the murderer from the beginning.$n$,$n$"O Adam, because of you and of Eve, I am slippery, and go on my belly." Then with its great strength, it threw down Adam and Eve and squeezed them, and tried to kill them.$n$,false),
(45580,'S','1-adam-eve',18,4,'1-adam-eve',18,4,$n$Genesis 3:14 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:* The serpent's own words in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 — slippery, going on its belly — are Eden's curse confessed from its own mouth.$n$,$n$"O Adam, because of you and of Eve, I am slippery, and go on my belly." Then with its great strength, it threw down Adam and Eve and squeezed them, and tried to kill them.$n$,false),
(45581,'S','1-adam-eve',18,4,'1-adam-eve',18,4,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The serpent that threw down and squeezed Adam and Eve to kill them in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 is the same devouring adversary the apostle names.$n$,$n$"O Adam, because of you and of Eve, I am slippery, and go on my belly." Then with its great strength, it threw down Adam and Eve and squeezed them, and tried to kill them.$n$,false),
(45582,'S','1-adam-eve',18,1,'1-adam-eve',18,1,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The blood-red serpent that swells to kill in 1 Adam and Eve 18:1 is that same old serpent named at the end of the war.$n$,$n$When the accursed serpent saw Adam and Eve, it swelled its head, stood on its tail, and with eyes blood-red, acted like it would kill them.$n$,false),
(45583,'S','1-adam-eve',18,2,'1-adam-eve',18,2,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The serpent running straight for Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 18:2 is the very enmity Yahuah set in Eden being acted out from the first day outside the garden.$n$,$n$It made straight for Eve, and ran after her; while Adam standing by, cried because he had no stick in his hand with which to hit the serpent, and did not know how to put it to death.$n$,false),
(45596,'S','1-adam-eve',20,2,'1-adam-eve',20,2,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word's stripping the serpent of its ability to hurt in 20:2 foreshadows the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$,$n$But Elohim (God) said to Adam and Eve, "From now on, don't be afraid, I will not let it come near you; I have driven it away from you, from this mountain; neither will I leave in it the ability to hurt you."$n$,false),
(45609,'S','1-adam-eve',21,6,'1-adam-eve',21,6,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins "from the very beginning" is the very one assaulting the first parents at 21:6 — and the Son is manifested to undo his work.$n$,$n$And she said, "I don't wish to live after him; for all that he did to himself was through me."$n$,false),
(45621,'S','1-adam-eve',22,5,'1-adam-eve',22,5,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Satan who deceived Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 22:5 is the enemy from the beginning whose works the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$,$n$And Adam cried and said, "O Yahuah (Lord), do not cut me off for this, neither punish me with heavy plagues, nor yet repay me according to my sin; for we, of our own will, transgressed Your commandment, and ignored Your law, and tried to become gods like you, when Satan the enemy deceived us."$n$,false),
(45631,'S','1-adam-eve',23,9,'1-adam-eve',23,9,$n$*And Adam began to make more requests of Elohim (God). * ORIGINAL OF THE LORD'S PRAYER SAID TO BE USED ABOUT 150 YEARS BEFORE OUR Yahuah (God): Our Father, Who art in Heaven, be gracious unto us, O Yahuah (Lord) our Elohim (God), hallowed be Your Name, and let the remembrance of Thee be glorified Heaven above and upon earth here below. Let Your kingdom reign over us now and forever. The Holy Men of old said remit and forgive unto all men whatsoever they have done unto me. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil thing; for Thine is the kingdom and Thou shalt reign in glory forever and forevermore, AMEN.* (1 Adam and Eve 23:9). *And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever. Amen.* (Matthew 6:13). Adam keeps asking Elohim (God) for more, and the prayer he prays ends on the same petitions Yahusha (Jesus) gives his disciples: do not lead us into temptation, deliver us from the evil, for the kingdom is Yours. The wording is not identical, since Adam's version says the evil thing and has a longer opening, but the shape is the same: a plea for rescue and a confession that the kingdom belongs to Yahuah (the Lord) alone. The first man prays it after the fall, and Matthew records the same cry for those who follow Yahusha (Jesus) now.$n$,$n$And Adam began to make more requests of Elohim (God). * ORIGINAL OF THE LORD'S PRAYER SAID TO BE USED ABOUT 150 YEARS BEFORE OUR Yahuah (God): Our Father, Who art in Heaven, be gracious unto us, O Yahuah (Lord) our Elohim (God), hallowed be Your Name, and let the remembrance of Thee be glorified Heaven above and upon earth here below. Let Your kingdom reign over us now and forever. The Holy Men of old said remit and forgive unto all men whatsoever they have done unto me. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil thing; for Thine is the kingdom and Thou shalt reign in glory forever and forevermore, AMEN.$n$,true),
(45644,'S','1-adam-eve',24,6,'1-adam-eve',24,6,$n$Hebrews 1:3 — *Who being the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high;* The Word who counts the days until He brings Adam back to the garden (1 Adam and Eve 24:6) is the Son who by Himself purges sins — the same Logos who comforts Adam now seated on high.$n$,$n$And now, behold, I have accepted your offering, O Adam, but the days of the covenant in which I have bound you are not fulfilled. When they are fulfilled, then will I bring you back into the garden.$n$,false),
(45645,'S','1-adam-eve',24,7,'1-adam-eve',24,7,$n$Jubilees 6:14 — *And for this law there is no limit of days, for it is for ever. They shall observe it throughout their generations, so that they may continue supplicating on your behalf with blood before the altar; every day and at the time of morning and evening they shall seek forgiveness on your behalf perpetually before Yahuah (God) that they may keep it and not be rooted out.* The standing order "when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:7 is Jubilees' perpetual blood-supplication before the altar — the same covenant of continual offering across the restored library.$n$,$n$Now, therefore, strengthen your heart; and when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering, and I will be favorable to you."$n$,false),
(45646,'S','1-adam-eve',24,6,'1-adam-eve',24,6,$n$Galatians 4:5 — *To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.* The return "into the garden" promised when the days of the covenant are fulfilled (1 Adam and Eve 24:6) is this redemption and adoption — the bound exile of Adam undone in Messiah.$n$,$n$And now, behold, I have accepted your offering, O Adam, but the days of the covenant in which I have bound you are not fulfilled. When they are fulfilled, then will I bring you back into the garden.$n$,false),
(45647,'S','1-adam-eve',24,5,'1-adam-eve',24,5,$n$Matthew 26:28 — *For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.* The blood the Word promises to make "forgiveness of sins" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:5 is the blood Messiah names at the table — shed for the remission Adam was first promised.$n$,$n$And as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it.$n$,false),
(45648,'S','1-adam-eve',24,5,'1-adam-eve',24,5,$n$*And as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it.* (1 Adam and Eve 24:5). *And almost all things are by the law purged with blood; and without shedding of blood is no remission.* (Hebrews 9:22). Adam has shed his blood on an altar and sought forgiveness through it, and the Word of Elohim (God) answers that He will make His own blood the forgiveness of sins. Hebrews states the same necessity plainly: under the law almost everything is cleansed with blood, and without the shedding of blood there is no remission. The law is not set aside here; it is the very ground the promise to Adam stands on, and the one who comes in the flesh of Adam's descendants, Yahusha (Jesus), answers it with His own blood.$n$,$n$And as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it.$n$,true),
(45649,'S','1-adam-eve',24,5,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$Hebrews 9:12 — *Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us.* The Word's pledge "I will offer My blood" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is fulfilled when Messiah enters by His own blood — the once-for-all forgiveness promised to Adam.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45650,'S','1-adam-eve',24,4,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$Genesis 8:20 — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD); and took of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl, and offered burnt offerings on the altar.* The "altar of the earth" the Word promises in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is the same earthen altar the fathers build, Noah's after the flood standing in the line that began with Adam's.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45651,'S','1-adam-eve',24,4,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* That the Word can promise His own blood to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 shows the Lamb was foreordained before the foundation — manifest in the last days, but pledged at the first.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45652,'S','1-adam-eve',24,4,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "days of the covenant" the Word counts to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 close in this fulness of time, the Son made of a woman of Adam's seed.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45653,'S','1-adam-eve',24,4,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The promise "I become flesh of your descendants" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is the incarnation John records — the Word taking the flesh of Adam's own line.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45654,'S','1-adam-eve',24,4,'1-adam-eve',24,4,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is this same eternal Word — the Logos addressing the man He had formed.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die. And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth.$n$,false),
(45655,'S','1-adam-eve',24,1,'1-adam-eve',24,1,$n$Leviticus 17:11 — *For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls: for it is the blood that maketh an atonement for the soul.* The law Sinai will write was already the unspoken ground of Adam's act in 1 Adam and Eve 24:1 — atonement by blood upon the altar, kept before ever it was commanded.$n$,$n$Then the merciful Elohim (God), good and lover of men, looked at Adam and Eve, and at their blood, which they had held up as an offering to Him; without an order from Him for so doing. But He wondered at them; and accepted their offerings.$n$,false),
(45656,'S','1-adam-eve',24,3,'1-adam-eve',24,3,$n$Jubilees 6:3 — *And he placed the fat thereof on the altar, and he took an ox, and a goat, and a sheep and kids, and salt, and a turtle-dove, and the young of a dove, and placed a burnt sacrifice on the altar, and poured thereon an offering mingled with oil, and sprinkled wine and strewed frankincense over everything, and caused a goodly savour to arise, acceptable before Yahuah (God).* Jubilees' goodly savour rising acceptable before Yahuah echoes the sweet savor of 1 Adam and Eve 24:3 — the same primeval altar-mercy carried across the restored library.$n$,$n$He smelled the sweet savor of their offering, and showed them mercy.$n$,false),
(45657,'S','1-adam-eve',24,3,'1-adam-eve',24,3,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake; for the imagination of man's heart is evil from his youth; neither will I again smite any more every thing living, as I have done.* Noah's sweet savour at the post-flood altar is word-for-word the sweet savor Yahuah smells over Adam's offering in 1 Adam and Eve 24:3, mercy meeting the lifted blood.$n$,$n$He smelled the sweet savor of their offering, and showed them mercy.$n$,false),
(45658,'S','1-adam-eve',24,1,'1-adam-eve',24,1,$n$Genesis 4:4 — *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering:* The respect Yahuah shows Abel's blood-offering is the same wondering acceptance He shows Adam and Eve's blood in 1 Adam and Eve 24:1, the way of approach kept from the first day outside Eden.$n$,$n$Then the merciful Elohim (God), good and lover of men, looked at Adam and Eve, and at their blood, which they had held up as an offering to Him; without an order from Him for so doing. But He wondered at them; and accepted their offerings.$n$,false),
(45663,'S','1-adam-eve',25,7,'1-adam-eve',25,7,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The covenant 'that He would save him at the end of the days' (25:7) is kept when the same Word takes flesh.$n$,$n$And the Word of Elohim (God) came to him, and blessed him, and comforted him, and covenanted with him, that He would save him at the end of the days determined for him.$n$,false),
(45669,'S','1-adam-eve',25,1,'1-adam-eve',25,1,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The self-slaughter Adam imagines (25:1) is a work of the devil, and the promised Son comes precisely to undo it.$n$,$n$But Elohim (God) knew that Adam believed he should frequently kill himself and make an offering to Him of his blood.$n$,false),
(45674,'S','1-adam-eve',26,11,'1-adam-eve',26,11,$n$*Yes, rather, bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My covenant is come.* (1 Adam and Eve 26:11). *And so, after he had patiently endured, he obtained the promise.* (Hebrews 6:15). Elohim (God) tells Adam to bear long and calm his soul until the days of the covenant are fulfilled, and the next verse says He will come and save him. Hebrews says Abraham obtained the promise in just this way, by patiently enduring. The promise does not come by hurry; it comes at the time Elohim (God) has set, to the one who waits for it. Adam is told to wait, and Abraham is shown having done it.$n$,$n$Yes, rather, bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My covenant is come.$n$,true),
(45676,'S','1-adam-eve',26,11,'1-adam-eve',26,11,$n$James 5:7 — *Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of Yahusha (Lord). Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain.* The "bear long... until the time of My covenant is come" of 1 Adam & Eve 26:11 is the same patient waiting for the coming of Yahusha (Lord).$n$,$n$Yes, rather, bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My covenant is come.$n$,false),
(45680,'S','1-adam-eve',26,15,'1-adam-eve',26,15,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "When, however, the covenant is fulfilled" of 1 Adam & Eve 26:15 is the fulness of time when the promised Son of the woman is sent.$n$,$n$When, however, the covenant is fulfilled, then shall I show you and your descendants mercy, and bring you into a land of gladness, where there is neither sorrow nor suffering; but abiding joy and gladness, and light that never fails, and praises that never cease; and a beautiful garden that shall never pass away."$n$,false),
(45692,'S','1-adam-eve',27,13,'1-adam-eve',27,13,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The angel stripping Satan to his *own hideous form* in 1 Adam and Eve 27:13 foreshadows the Son manifested to undo his works.$n$,$n$Then the angel went from Adam and seized Satan at the opening of the cave, and stripped him of the pretense he had assumed, and brought him in his own hideous form to Adam and Eve; who were afraid of him when they saw him.$n$,false),
(45702,'S','1-adam-eve',28,10,'1-adam-eve',28,10,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's plot to wipe off their name from the earth at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 is his strike at the heel, but the head-crushing Seed is already promised.$n$,$n$But when they came to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it, the Devil drew near to Adam and Eve, and made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone.$n$,false),
(45703,'S','1-adam-eve',28,10,'1-adam-eve',28,10,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The Devil who draws near to throw Adam and Eve down and kill them at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 is the roaring lion seeking to devour the seed.$n$,$n$But when they came to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it, the Devil drew near to Adam and Eve, and made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone.$n$,false),
(45704,'S','1-adam-eve',28,10,'1-adam-eve',28,10,$n$Matthew 4:8 — *Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;* As Satan covets to wipe off Adam's name so the earth remains his alone at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10, he likewise offers the kingdoms of the world he claims to own.$n$,$n$But when they came to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it, the Devil drew near to Adam and Eve, and made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone.$n$,false),
(45705,'S','1-adam-eve',28,10,'1-adam-eve',28,10,$n$Matthew 4:6 — *And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of Elohim (God), cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.* The devil who marches the first Adam up a high mountain to throw him down at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 tempts the second Adam to the very same fall.$n$,$n$But when they came to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it, the Devil drew near to Adam and Eve, and made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone.$n$,false),
(45706,'S','1-adam-eve',28,6,'1-adam-eve',28,6,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The words that sink into the hearts of Adam and Eve at 1 Adam and Eve 28:6 are the devil's work, which only the manifested Son undoes.$n$,$n$These words sank into the heart of Adam and Eve.$n$,false),
(45707,'S','1-adam-eve',28,5,'1-adam-eve',28,5,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The garden Satan promises to reopen at 1 Adam and Eve 28:5 was sealed by the flaming sword, so his offer is a lie at the very threshold.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) has sent us to take you and bring you to the border of the garden northwards; to the shore of the clear sea, and bathe you and Eve in it, and raise you to your former gladness, that you return again to the garden."$n$,false),
(45708,'S','1-adam-eve',28,5,'1-adam-eve',28,5,$n$Genesis 3:5 — *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* Satan's false promise of restoration at 1 Adam and Eve 28:5 is the same overreaching lie he used in the garden, offering by deceit what is not his to give.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) has sent us to take you and bring you to the border of the garden northwards; to the shore of the clear sea, and bathe you and Eve in it, and raise you to your former gladness, that you return again to the garden."$n$,false),
(45709,'S','1-adam-eve',28,7,'1-adam-eve',28,7,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Adam's trial at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7 is one stroke of the enmity Yahuah set between the serpent and the seed of the woman.$n$,$n$Yet Elohim (God) withheld His Word from Adam, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Eve was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail.$n$,false),
(45710,'S','1-adam-eve',28,7,'1-adam-eve',28,7,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The deceiver testing Adam at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7 is the liar who has murdered by falsehood from the beginning.$n$,$n$Yet Elohim (God) withheld His Word from Adam, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Eve was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail.$n$,false),
(45711,'S','1-adam-eve',28,7,'1-adam-eve',28,7,$n$Genesis 3:4 — *And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die:* The lie that overthrew Eve in the garden is named again at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7, where Yahuah waits to see whether Adam will be overcome as she was.$n$,$n$Yet Elohim (God) withheld His Word from Adam, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Eve was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail.$n$,false),
(45712,'S','1-adam-eve',28,1,'1-adam-eve',28,1,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The host Satan gathers in 1 Adam and Eve 28:1 are the angels cast down with him, and his trade is the deceiving of the whole world.$n$,$n$But when the crafty Satan saw them, that they were going to the garden, he gathered together his host, and came in appearance on a cloud, intent on deceiving them.$n$,false),
(45713,'S','1-adam-eve',28,2,'1-adam-eve',28,2,$n$2 Corinthians 11:3 — *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ).* As Adam and Eve mistake the deceiver for angels of Elohim at 1 Adam and Eve 28:2, Sha'ul warns the same subtilty still corrupts the mind.$n$,$n$But when Adam and Eve saw him thus in a vision, they thought they were angels of Elohim (God) come to comfort them about having left the garden, or to bring them back again into it.$n$,false),
(45714,'S','1-adam-eve',28,1,'1-adam-eve',28,1,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The crafty Satan who comes on a cloud at 1 Adam and Eve 28:1 is the same adversary Sha'ul unmasks, working by counterfeit glory.$n$,$n$But when the crafty Satan saw them, that they were going to the garden, he gathered together his host, and came in appearance on a cloud, intent on deceiving them.$n$,false),
(45715,'S','1-adam-eve',29,7,'1-adam-eve',29,7,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The golden rods laid up to shine in Adam's cave-night in 1 Adam and Eve 29:7 are the first of the treasure kept against the Saviour's coming — the very gold the magi at last bring to the child.$n$,$n$This did Elohim (God) in His wisdom in order that these golden rods, being with Adam in the cave, should shine forth with light in the night around him, and put an end to his fear of the darkness.$n$,false),
(45716,'S','1-adam-eve',29,6,'1-adam-eve',29,6,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The Michael sent to comfort Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:6 is the great prince Daniel sees standing for the children of the covenant — the same guardian from the first man to the last trouble.$n$,$n$And Elohim (God) considered Adam's thought, and sent the angel Michael as far as the sea that reaches India, to take from there golden rods and bring them to Adam.$n$,false),
(45717,'S','1-adam-eve',29,6,'1-adam-eve',29,6,$n$Jude 1:9 — *Yet Michael the archangel, when contending with the devil he disputed about the body of Moses, durst not bring against him a railing accusation, but said, Yahuah (Lord) rebuke thee.* The angel Michael whom Elohim sends to fetch the golden rods in 1 Adam and Eve 29:6 is the same archangel Jude names contending against the devil — Yahuah's appointed servant against the enemy of Adam's race.$n$,$n$And Elohim (God) considered Adam's thought, and sent the angel Michael as far as the sea that reaches India, to take from there golden rods and bring them to Adam.$n$,false),
(45718,'S','1-adam-eve',29,4,'1-adam-eve',29,4,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The Satan who seeks to deceive Adam and his seed in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 is the very serpent John names as the deceiver of the whole world.$n$,$n$Then came the Word from Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "Know you and understand concerning this Satan, that he seeks to deceive you and your descendants after you."$n$,false),
(45719,'S','1-adam-eve',29,4,'1-adam-eve',29,4,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* Peter's charge to watchfulness is the practical form of the Word's first-day warning to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 — know and understand this Satan who seeks your destruction.$n$,$n$Then came the Word from Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "Know you and understand concerning this Satan, that he seeks to deceive you and your descendants after you."$n$,false),
(45720,'S','1-adam-eve',29,4,'1-adam-eve',29,4,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The Word's warning that Satan seeks to deceive Adam and his descendants in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 unmasks the enemy's one tactic — the false light Paul exposes.$n$,$n$Then came the Word from Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "Know you and understand concerning this Satan, that he seeks to deceive you and your descendants after you."$n$,false),
(45721,'S','1-adam-eve',29,4,'1-adam-eve',29,4,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word that comes to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 to counsel and warn him is the Logos John names — the same who was with Elohim from the beginning now walking with the first man.$n$,$n$Then came the Word from Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "Know you and understand concerning this Satan, that he seeks to deceive you and your descendants after you."$n$,false),
(45722,'S','1-adam-eve',29,1,'1-adam-eve',29,1,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* John names the very work Elohim begins to undo when He curses Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 29:1 — the devil who sins from the beginning meets the Son manifested to destroy his works.$n$,$n$But when the merciful Elohim (God) saw that Satan wished to kill Adam with his many tricks, and saw that Adam was meek and without guile, Elohim (God) spoke to Satan in a loud voice, and cursed him.$n$,false),
(45723,'S','1-adam-eve',29,2,'1-adam-eve',29,2,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* As Satan and his hosts flee the rebuke in 1 Adam and Eve 29:2, Paul names the end of that same war — the serpent bruised under the feet of the redeemed.$n$,$n$Then he and his hosts fled, and Adam and Eve remained standing on the top of the mountain, from there they saw below them the wide world, high above which they were. But they saw none of the host which time after time were by them.$n$,false),
(45724,'S','1-adam-eve',29,1,'1-adam-eve',29,1,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The loud curse Elohim speaks over Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 29:1 is the garden-curse still in force, the serpent striking at the seed of the woman.$n$,$n$But when the merciful Elohim (God) saw that Satan wished to kill Adam with his many tricks, and saw that Adam was meek and without guile, Elohim (God) spoke to Satan in a loud voice, and cursed him.$n$,false),
(45725,'S','1-adam-eve',30,3,'1-adam-eve',30,3,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim whose order moves the angels and the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 30:3 is the Logos who was in the beginning, soon to restore the light Adam lost.$n$,$n$The cherub then said, "Well." And Gabriel went in and took the incense.$n$,false),
(45726,'S','1-adam-eve',30,2,'1-adam-eve',30,2,$n$Exodus 30:34 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* The sweet-smelling incense Yahuah commands brought for Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 30:2 is the same holy frankincense He later commands for the tabernacle's perfume.$n$,$n$Then the angel Gabriel went down by Elohim's (God's) order to the garden, and told the cherub as Elohim (God) had commanded him.$n$,false),
(45727,'S','1-adam-eve',30,8,'1-adam-eve',30,8,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The spring of water that comforts the mourners in 1 Adam and Eve 30:8 anticipates the river of life that flows from the throne in the City.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to the angels, "Dip them in the spring of water; then take them and sprinkle their water over Adam and Eve, that they be a little comforted in their sorrow, and give them to Adam and Eve.$n$,false),
(45728,'S','1-adam-eve',30,9,'1-adam-eve',30,9,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's seeking to make an end of Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 30:9 is the serpent striking at the seed; Yahuah's comfort keeps the seed He swore to preserve.$n$,$n$And the angels did as Elohim (God) had commanded them, and they gave all those things to Adam and Eve on the top of the mountain on which Satan had placed them, when he sought to make an end of them.$n$,false),
(45729,'S','1-adam-eve',30,7,'1-adam-eve',30,7,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The Tree of Life in the garden of 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 is the same Yahuah planted in the midst of Eden at the beginning.$n$,$n$And the angels brought these things to Elohim (God), by the Tree of Life, in the garden.$n$,false),
(45730,'S','1-adam-eve',30,7,'1-adam-eve',30,7,$n$Revelation 22:2 — *In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* The Tree of Life beside which the angels stand in 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 stands again, unbarred, in the restored City.$n$,$n$And the angels brought these things to Elohim (God), by the Tree of Life, in the garden.$n$,false),
(45731,'S','1-adam-eve',30,7,'1-adam-eve',30,7,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The cherub who guards the Tree in 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 is the same guardian set at the east of Eden after the expulsion.$n$,$n$And the angels brought these things to Elohim (God), by the Tree of Life, in the garden.$n$,false),
(45732,'S','1-adam-eve',30,10,'1-adam-eve',30,10,$n$Genesis 3:17 — *And unto Adam he said, Because thou hast hearkened unto the voice of thy wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of which I commanded thee, saying, Thou shalt not eat of it: cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;* The myrrh that is a token of sorrow in 1 Adam and Eve 30:10 answers the sorrow pronounced over the ground at the fall.$n$,$n$And when Adam saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he was rejoiced and cried because he thought that the gold was a token of the kingdom from where he had come, that the incense was a token of the bright light which had been taken from him, and that the myrrh was a token of the sorrow in which he was.$n$,false),
(45733,'S','1-adam-eve',30,6,'1-adam-eve',30,6,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The gold, incense, and myrrh gathered from the borders of the garden in 1 Adam and Eve 30:6 are the very gifts borne to Bethlehem.$n$,$n$The golden rods were from the Indian sea, where there are precious stones. The incense was from the eastern border of the garden; and the myrrh from the western border, from where bitterness came over Adam.$n$,false),
(45734,'S','1-adam-eve',30,10,'1-adam-eve',30,10,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The three tokens given to Adam at 1 Adam and Eve 30:10 are the same three the magi lay before the Saviour — kept from the garden against His coming.$n$,$n$And when Adam saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he was rejoiced and cried because he thought that the gold was a token of the kingdom from where he had come, that the incense was a token of the bright light which had been taken from him, and that the myrrh was a token of the sorrow in which he was.$n$,false),
(45758,'S','1-adam-eve',33,14,'1-adam-eve',33,14,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* When Adam is given *to know it was Satan* in 1 Adam & Eve 33:14, the deceiver's work is unmasked — the very works the Son of Elohim was manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$But Adam grieved, and gave her to know it was Satan. He then took her and they both returned to the cave.$n$,false),
(45772,'S','1-adam-eve',34,14,'1-adam-eve',34,14,$n$*Then You drew a rib out of my side, and created it after my own likeness and image. Then I awoke; and when I saw her and knew who she was, I said, 'This is bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh; from now on she shall be called woman.'* (1 Adam and Eve 34:14). *And Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and he slept, and He took for the woman one rib from amongst his ribs, and this rib was the origin of the woman from amongst his ribs, and He built up the flesh in its stead, and built the woman.* (Jubilees 3:5). Adam recalls that he slept, that a rib was drawn from his side, and that he woke to see the woman and name her. Jubilees tells the same event from the other side: Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused the deep sleep, took one rib, and built the woman from it. The two accounts agree on the sleep and the rib, and each says what the other leaves out: Adam speaks as the one who slept and woke, and Jubilees speaks of the hand that built her.$n$,$n$Then You drew a rib out of my side, and created it after my own likeness and image. Then I awoke; and when I saw her and knew who she was, I said, 'This is bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh; from now on she shall be called woman.'$n$,true),
(45776,'S','1-adam-eve',34,11,'1-adam-eve',34,11,$n$*And if You had punished me as You said, with death, I should have died that very moment.* (1 Adam and Eve 34:11). *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned:* (Romans 5:12). Adam looks back on the day he ate and marvels that he was not struck dead on the spot, as the command had said he would be. Paul traces the same line: by one man sin entered into the world, and death came through sin. What Adam says of himself in his own telling, the apostle says of him for all who came after, that the death spoken over the tree reached everyone through the one who ate.$n$,$n$And if You had punished me as You said, with death, I should have died that very moment.$n$,true),
(45781,'S','1-adam-eve',34,5,'1-adam-eve',34,5,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam's confession of being made from earth's dust sets the very contrast Sha'ul draws against the heavenly Man.$n$,$n$Then You spread Your hand and created me out of one element, that of dust of the earth; and You brought me into the garden at the third hour, on a Friday, and informed me of it in the cave.$n$,false),
(45808,'S','1-adam-eve',37,10,'1-adam-eve',37,10,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The mercy Adam pleads in 1 Adam & Eve 37:10 is the seed-war's end — the Son manifested to undo the serpent's hour.$n$,$n$But now, O Yahuah (Lord), behold, we have endured all these days, and have borne sufferings. Make these forty-three days an equivalent for the one hour in which we transgressed."$n$,false),
(45821,'S','1-adam-eve',38,5,'1-adam-eve',38,5,$n$Hebrews 8:6 — *But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.* The covenant Adam is told to endure for in 1 Adam and Eve 38:5 is the better covenant the coming Mediator establishes.$n$,$n$I will not deny your request, neither will I disappoint your hope; therefore, endure until the fulfillment of the covenant I made with you."$n$,false),
(45822,'S','1-adam-eve',38,5,'1-adam-eve',38,5,$n$2 Corinthians 1:20 — *For all the promises of Elohim (God) in him are yea, and in him Amen, unto the glory of Elohim (God) by us.* The hope the Word promises not to disappoint in 1 Adam and Eve 38:5 is sure because all His promises are Yea and Amen in the Son.$n$,$n$I will not deny your request, neither will I disappoint your hope; therefore, endure until the fulfillment of the covenant I made with you."$n$,false),
(45823,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$*"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2). *And he lacked seventy years of one thousand years; for one thousand years are as one day in the testimony of the heavens and therefore was it written concerning the tree of knowledge: “On the day that you eat thereof you will die.” For this reason he did not complete the years of this day; for he died during it.* (Jubilees 4:30). Elohim (God) tells Adam that the fruit of the Tree of Life is held back until the 5500 years are fulfilled, and then he and Eve and their righteous descendants will eat and live forever. Jubilees shows how the heavens count such spans: a thousand years are as one day, and Adam, lacking seventy years of a thousand, died within the day of the command about the tree. The long wait Adam is given is counted in these days of the heavens.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,true),
(45824,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$*"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2). *But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.* (2 Peter 3:8). Elohim (God) promises Adam the fruit of the Tree of Life only when the 5500 years are fulfilled, a span counted in thousands. Peter tells his beloved not to be ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with Yahuah (the Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day. That is the scale on which Elohim (God) speaks when He tells Adam to wait: what looks to Adam like a very long delay is a few days to the one who made him, and the promise is held to its appointed day.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,true),
(45825,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$*"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2). *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* (Revelation 22:14). Elohim (God) promises Adam, Eve and their righteous descendants that they will eat of the Tree of Life and live forever when the time is fulfilled. The last chapter of Revelation says who has the right to that tree: those who do His commandments, who then enter the city through its gates. The righteous descendants of Adam are the ones who keep the commandments, so the promise at the beginning and the blessing at the end are one promise, and the commandments are the way to it.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,true),
(45826,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$Revelation 2:7 — *He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God).* The deferred fruit of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is the overcomer's reward when paradise is restored.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45827,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$Genesis 3:22 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said, Behold, the man is become as one of us, to know good and evil: and now, lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever:* The Word's "not now" in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 echoes the barring of fallen Adam from the tree of life.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45828,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The fruit Adam asks for in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is this same Tree of Life set in the midst of Eden.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45829,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The fulfilled 5500 years of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is the fulness of time when the promised Son is sent.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45830,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour pledged for the end of the 5500 years in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 was already foreordained before the world was.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45831,'S','1-adam-eve',38,1,'1-adam-eve',38,1,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* The Word speaking to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 38:1 is the first of those manifold speakings to the fathers fulfilled at last in the Son.$n$,$n$After these things the Word of Elohim (God) came to Adam, and said to him:--$n$,false),
(45832,'S','1-adam-eve',38,2,'1-adam-eve',38,2,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The 5500-year promise of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is fulfilled when this same Word takes flesh to save Adam's seed.$n$,$n$"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.$n$,false),
(45833,'S','1-adam-eve',38,1,'1-adam-eve',38,1,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word who comes to speak with Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 38:1 is the eternal Logos, with Elohim and Elohim from the beginning.$n$,$n$After these things the Word of Elohim (God) came to Adam, and said to him:--$n$,false),
(45845,'S','1-adam-eve',40,2,'1-adam-eve',40,2,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam’s animal body of earth that must be fed in 1 Adam & Eve 40:2 is the earthy first man, set against the heavenly Second.$n$,$n$But when you came to live in this strange land, your animal body could not survive on earth without earthly food, to strengthen it and to restore its powers."$n$,false),
(45855,'S','1-adam-eve',41,5,'1-adam-eve',41,5,$n$Jubilees 3:16 — *And he tilled (the garden), and was naked and knew it not, and was not ashamed, and he protected the garden from the birds and beasts and cattle, and gathered its fruit, and ate, and put aside the residue for himself and for his wife and put aside that which was being kept.* The garden-fruit Adam once gathered freely is the same garden he now stands outside of, fasting, in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5.$n$,$n$"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink.$n$,false),
(45856,'S','1-adam-eve',41,8,'1-adam-eve',41,8,$n$Genesis 4:26 — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* The praying and calling on Yahuah in 1 Adam and Eve 41:8 is the first keeping of the way of the seed, before ever the law was given.$n$,$n$And they stood and prayed before Yahuah (Lord), and asked Him to look at them this once, to forgive them, and to grant them their request.$n$,false),
(45857,'S','1-adam-eve',41,1,'1-adam-eve',41,1,$n$Genesis 3:7 — *And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.* The fig Adam and Eve lift onto the rods and incense in 1 Adam and Eve 41:1 is the very leaf of their first shame, now offered up to Yahuah.$n$,$n$Then Adam took the fig, and laid it on the golden rods. Eve also took her fig, and put it on the incense.$n$,false),
(45858,'S','1-adam-eve',41,13,'1-adam-eve',41,13,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* Adam's cry for mercy under the curse in 1 Adam and Eve 41:13 rests on the seed-promise that crushes the serpent at last.$n$,$n$Of Your mercy, O Elohim (God), save me from these plagues and trials, and bring me into another land different from this, if You will not let me live in Your garden." * This is substantiated by Genesis 3:7 whereby the leaves of the fig tree were large enough that Adam and Eve could fashion garments from them.$n$,false),
(45859,'S','1-adam-eve',41,6,'1-adam-eve',41,6,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* Adam grieves in 1 Adam and Eve 41:6 that Yahuah has not fed him of the Tree of Life — for the way to it is kept by the flaming sword.$n$,$n$For Elohim (God) has not fed us with the Tree of Life, in order that we may not live. Therefore, we will ask him to give us some of the Water of Life, and to quench our thirst with it, rather than with a drink of water of this land."$n$,false),
(45860,'S','1-adam-eve',41,12,'1-adam-eve',41,12,$n$Genesis 3:19 — *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* Adam's parched, dying flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is this very curse worked out in his body.$n$,$n$But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live.$n$,false),
(45861,'S','1-adam-eve',41,12,'1-adam-eve',41,12,$n$Psalms 36:8 — *They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.* The river of Yahuah's pleasure is the same Water of Life Adam thirsts after in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12.$n$,$n$But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live.$n$,false),
(45862,'S','1-adam-eve',41,6,'1-adam-eve',41,6,$n$Revelation 22:17 — *And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.* The freely-given Water Adam asks for in 1 Adam and Eve 41:6 is held open at last to every thirst.$n$,$n$For Elohim (God) has not fed us with the Tree of Life, in order that we may not live. Therefore, we will ask him to give us some of the Water of Life, and to quench our thirst with it, rather than with a drink of water of this land."$n$,false),
(45863,'S','1-adam-eve',41,12,'1-adam-eve',41,12,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The Water of Life Adam mourns in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 flows again, unbarred, at the end of the seed-war.$n$,$n$But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live.$n$,false),
(45864,'S','1-adam-eve',41,12,'1-adam-eve',41,12,$n$John 7:37 — *In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.* Adam's parched cry in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is the very thirst Yahusha answers with Himself.$n$,$n$But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live.$n$,false),
(45865,'S','1-adam-eve',41,12,'1-adam-eve',41,12,$n$John 4:14 — *But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.* The Water of Life Adam begs for in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is the gift the Messiah Himself names and gives.$n$,$n$But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live.$n$,false),
(45866,'S','1-adam-eve',41,5,'1-adam-eve',41,5,$n$Jubilees 3:12 — *And when she had completed these eighty days we brought her into the Garden of Eden, for it is holier than all the earth besides, and every tree that is planted in it is holy.* The garden Adam now prays toward in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 is, by Jubilees' witness, the holiest ground on earth — and he is shut outside it.$n$,$n$"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink.$n$,false),
(45867,'S','1-adam-eve',41,5,'1-adam-eve',41,5,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The Water of Life Adam seeks in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 flows from beside the tree of life he has been barred from.$n$,$n$"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink.$n$,false),
(45868,'S','1-adam-eve',41,5,'1-adam-eve',41,5,$n$Genesis 2:10 — *And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.* The river Adam names in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 is Eden's own four-headed river, remembered from outside the gate.$n$,$n$"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink.$n$,false),
(45878,'S','1-adam-eve',42,8,'1-adam-eve',42,8,$n$*For My blood shall be the Water of Life to you at that time, and not to just you alone, but to all your descendants who shall believe in Me***; that it be to them for rest forever."* (1 Adam and Eve 42:8). *He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.* (John 7:38). The Word of Elohim (God) tells Adam that the Water of Life he seeks will come when His blood is shed, and that it is for Adam's descendants who believe in Him, for rest forever. Yahusha (Jesus) says that whoever believes on Him, as the scripture has said, will have rivers of living water flowing from within. The water promised to Adam's line in the first days is the same water offered to the one who believes in Yahusha (Jesus), and it comes through His blood.$n$,$n$For My blood shall be the Water of Life to you at that time, and not to just you alone, but to all your descendants who shall believe in Me***; that it be to them for rest forever."$n$,true),
(45889,'S','1-adam-eve',43,10,'1-adam-eve',43,10,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The plot to put their souls to death in 1 Adam and Eve 43:10 is the devil's work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$O Eve, if Elohim (God) will bring us into a strange land other than this, in which we find consolation, it must be to put our souls to death, and blot out our name from the face of the earth.$n$,false),
(45896,'S','1-adam-eve',44,8,'1-adam-eve',44,8,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The fire that separates Adam and Eve from the cave and afflicts them in 1 Adam and Eve 44:8 echoes the flaming sword that bars the way back to the garden.$n$,$n$Then they both began crying because of the fire that separated them from the cave, and that came towards them, burning. And they were afraid.$n$,false),
(45897,'S','1-adam-eve',44,9,'1-adam-eve',44,9,$n$Genesis 3:19 — *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* Adam's lament that "our nature is altered" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:9 unfolds the curse spoken in Eden that bound man to the ground and to death.$n$,$n$Then Adam said to Eve, "See this fire of which we have a portion in us: which formerly yielded to us, but no longer does so, now that we have transgressed the limit of creation, and changed our condition, and our nature is altered. But the fire is not changed in its nature, nor altered from its creation. Therefore it now has power over us; and when we come near it, it scorches our flesh."$n$,false),
(45898,'S','1-adam-eve',44,6,'1-adam-eve',44,6,$n$1 Enoch 54:1 — *And I looked and turned to another part of the earth, and saw there a deep valley with burning fire.* The fire that surrounds the cave but cannot reach the seed in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 foreshadows the valley of burning fire prepared for Satan's hosts that Enoch beheld.$n$,$n$Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.$n$,false),
(45899,'S','1-adam-eve',44,6,'1-adam-eve',44,6,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour by whom the seed is kept from the forty-sixth day outside the garden in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 was foreordained before the world's foundation.$n$,$n$Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.$n$,false),
(45900,'S','1-adam-eve',44,6,'1-adam-eve',44,6,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The enemy driven off at the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 will at the last be bruised wholly under the feet of the redeemed.$n$,$n$Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.$n$,false),
(45901,'S','1-adam-eve',44,6,'1-adam-eve',44,6,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's fleeing in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 is one defeat in the enmity Yahuah set between the serpent and the seed of the woman.$n$,$n$Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.$n$,false),
(45902,'S','1-adam-eve',44,5,'1-adam-eve',44,5,$n$Jubilees 10:8–9 — *And the chief of the spirits, Mastêmâ, came and said: “Yahuah (God), Creator, let some of them remain before me, and let them hearken to my voice, and do all that I shall say to them; for if some of them are not left to me, I shall not be able to execute the power of my will on the sons of men; for these are for corruption and leading astray before my judgment, for great is the wickedness of the sons of men.” And He said: “Let the tenth part of them remain before him, and let nine parts descend into the place of condemnation.”* The same divine patience that leaves the enemy his hosts "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 lets a remnant of Mastema's spirits remain in Noah's day.$n$,$n$Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world."$n$,false),
(45903,'S','1-adam-eve',44,5,'1-adam-eve',44,5,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The destruction withheld by mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 is appointed for the end, when the Son is manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$,$n$Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world."$n$,false),
(45904,'S','1-adam-eve',44,5,'1-adam-eve',44,5,$n$2 Peter 3:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.* The delayed judgment "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 is Yahuah's longsuffering, not slackness.$n$,$n$Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world."$n$,false),
(45905,'S','1-adam-eve',44,5,'1-adam-eve',44,5,$n$Romans 2:4 — *Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of Elohim (God) leadeth thee to repentance?* The mercy and patience that spare Satan "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 are this forbearance and longsuffering of Yahuah.$n$,$n$Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world."$n$,false),
(45906,'S','1-adam-eve',44,4,'1-adam-eve',44,4,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The Satan rebuked at the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is the same old serpent who deceiveth the whole world.$n$,$n$Therefore the angel tolerated him, without saying one bad word, until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.$n$,false),
(45907,'S','1-adam-eve',44,4,'1-adam-eve',44,4,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The one who first deceived and now seeks to destroy in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is the murderer and liar from the beginning.$n$,$n$Therefore the angel tolerated him, without saying one bad word, until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.$n$,false),
(45908,'S','1-adam-eve',44,4,'1-adam-eve',44,4,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The Word's charge that Satan "once before you deceived My servants" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 names the disguising deceiver Paul warns of.$n$,$n$Therefore the angel tolerated him, without saying one bad word, until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.$n$,false),
(45909,'S','1-adam-eve',44,4,'1-adam-eve',44,4,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is this same Logos who was Elohim from the beginning.$n$,$n$Therefore the angel tolerated him, without saying one bad word, until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.$n$,false),
(45910,'S','1-adam-eve',44,2,'1-adam-eve',44,2,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The same flaming cherubic guard set over Eden's way now guards the cave-of-treasures in 1 Adam and Eve 44:2.$n$,$n$And Satan kept on bringing trees and throwing them into the fire, until the flames of the fire rose up on high, and covered the whole cave, thinking, as he did in his own mind, to consume the cave with much fire. But the angel of Yahuah (Lord) was guarding it.$n$,false),
(45911,'S','1-adam-eve',44,1,'1-adam-eve',44,1,$n$Exodus 3:2 — *And the angel of Yahuah (LORD) appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.* As the bush burned unconsumed, so the angel keeps the cave unconsumed in the fire of 1 Adam and Eve 44:1.$n$,$n$Yet Adam and Eve were standing and looking at the fire, and unable to come near the cave from their dread of the fire.$n$,false),
(45912,'S','1-adam-eve',44,2,'1-adam-eve',44,2,$n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The guarding angel of 1 Adam and Eve 44:2 is one of these ministers of flame, mastering the very fire Satan kindled.$n$,$n$And Satan kept on bringing trees and throwing them into the fire, until the flames of the fire rose up on high, and covered the whole cave, thinking, as he did in his own mind, to consume the cave with much fire. But the angel of Yahuah (Lord) was guarding it.$n$,false),
(45917,'S','1-adam-eve',45,11,'1-adam-eve',45,10,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The deliverance promised "until My coming" was foreordained before the foundation, manifest in these last times for the children of Adam.$n$,$n$Then you will see the burning of his fire, that will be burning around you and likewise your descendants. You will not be delivered from it until My coming; just like you cannot go into your cave right now because of the great fire around it; not until My Word comes and makes a way for you on the day My covenant is fulfilled.$n$,false),
(45921,'S','1-adam-eve',45,9,'1-adam-eve',45,9,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The plague of fire "that will be burning around you" is the work of the devil the Son came to destroy.$n$,$n$Elohim (God) also said to Adam, "See this fire kindled by Satan around your cave; see this wonder that surrounds you; and know that it will encompass about both you and your descendants, when you obey his command; that he will plague you with fire; and that you will go down into hell after you are dead.$n$,false),
(45947,'S','1-adam-eve',47,6,'1-adam-eve',47,6,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Adam's plea for forgiven sin in 1 Adam and Eve 47:6 leans on the manifested Son who undoes the devil's works.$n$,$n$And they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain.$n$,false),
(45948,'S','1-adam-eve',47,6,'1-adam-eve',47,6,$n$*And they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain.* (1 Adam and Eve 47:6). *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). Adam and Eve stand and pray to Elohim (God) to forgive them, and then sleep under the mountain. Genesis marks the line of Seth, and the days of his son Enos, as the time when men began to call upon the name of Yahuah (the LORD). The prayer of Adam and Eve is the same calling, already on their lips: forgiveness sought from Elohim (God) by name, and carried down by the holy seed.$n$,$n$And they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain.$n$,true),
(45960,'S','1-adam-eve',48,3,'1-adam-eve',48,3,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's murderous design against Adam from the first days outside Eden is the devil who sins from the beginning, whose works the Son came to destroy.$n$,$n$He then said to them, "You know that this Adam, whom Elohim (God) created out of the dust, is the one who has taken our kingdom, come, let us gather together and kill him; or hurl a rock at him and at Eve, and crush them under it."$n$,false),
(45966,'S','1-adam-eve',49,9,'1-adam-eve',49,9,$n$Matthew 28:6 — *He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where Yahusha (Lord) lay.* The third-day rising foretold to Adam is announced at the open rock — risen as He said, the place where He lay now empty, salvation made sure for Adam's descendants.$n$,$n$But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam, and to your descendants, to believe in Me. But, O Adam, I will not bring you from under this rock until three days and three nights have passed."$n$,false),
(45968,'S','1-adam-eve',49,9,'1-adam-eve',49,9,$n$*But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam, and to your descendants, to believe in Me. But, O Adam, I will not bring you from under this rock until three days and three nights have passed."* (1 Adam and Eve 49:9). *And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures:* (1 Corinthians 15:4). The Word of Elohim (God) tells Adam that on the third day He will rise again, and that it will be salvation to Adam and to his descendants who believe in Him. Paul gives the gospel in the same order: He was buried, and He rose again the third day according to the scriptures. Adam heard it first, under the rock, long before it happened, and Paul's phrase according to the scriptures reaches back to that beginning.$n$,$n$But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam, and to your descendants, to believe in Me. But, O Adam, I will not bring you from under this rock until three days and three nights have passed."$n$,true),
(45973,'S','1-adam-eve',49,6,'1-adam-eve',49,6,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The works of the devil that buried Adam under the stone are the very works the Son was manifested to destroy, foretold in this same chapter's promise of the third-day rising.$n$,$n$It came from Satan, who had promised you the Godhead and majesty. It is he who threw down this rock to kill you under it, and Eve with you, and thus to prevent you from living on the earth.$n$,false),
(45983,'S','1-adam-eve',50,7,'1-adam-eve',50,7,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 50:7 is this eternal Logos, Elohim Himself, walking with the first man.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) and said to him, "O Adam, take Eve and come to the seashore where you fasted before. There you will find skins of sheep that were left after lions ate the carcasses. Take them and make garments for yourselves, and clothe yourselves with them. * Chapter XLVI, verse 1, says "Satan blew into the fire ... so that their bodies were singed". At this time, the garments that Yahuah (Lord) had given them in Genesis 3:21 were burned off so that Adam and Eve were again naked.$n$,false),
(45987,'S','1-adam-eve',50,5,'1-adam-eve',50,5,$n$Genesis 3:7 — *And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.* Standing stained and naked and unable to do the work in 1 Adam and Eve 50:5 reopens the garden's first nakedness, where human handiwork could not truly cover.$n$,$n$So they went out of the cave, and came to the northern border of the garden, and they looked for something to cover their bodies with*. But they found nothing, and knew not how to do the work. Yet their bodies were stained, and they were speechless from cold and heat.$n$,false),
(45991,'S','1-adam-eve',50,3,'1-adam-eve',50,3,$n$Psalm 130:1 — *Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O Yahuah (LORD).* Adam and Eve praying through the whole night and begging for mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 50:3 is this very cry de profundis from the first generation outside Eden.$n$,$n$But Adam and Eve rose again and prayed to Elohim (God) in the cave the whole of that night, and begged for mercy from Him.$n$,false),
(46001,'S','1-adam-eve',51,5,'1-adam-eve',51,5,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The serpent who deceived and stripped Adam in 51:5 is the one whose works the Son came to destroy.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam and Eve, and said to them, "This is he who was hidden in the serpent, and who deceived you, and stripped you of the garment of light and glory in which you were.$n$,false),
(46029,'S','1-adam-eve',53,3,'1-adam-eve',53,3,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word driving the lions from Adam and Eve (53:3) is the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to them, and drove away the lions from them.$n$,false),
(46036,'S','1-adam-eve',54,10,'1-adam-eve',54,10,$n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The fiery angels coming down to Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 54:10 are the flaming-fire ministers of Yahuah.$n$,$n$Then, again, other angels came down close to the place where Adam and Eve were. They were divided between joy and sorrow.$n$,false),
(46037,'S','1-adam-eve',54,11,'1-adam-eve',54,11,$n$Hebrews 1:14 — *Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?* The angels glad over Adam's hoped-for return in 1 Adam and Eve 54:11 are ministering spirits sent for the heirs of the promised salvation.$n$,$n$They were glad, because they thought that Elohim (God) was favorable to Adam, and wished him to return to the garden; and wished to restore him to the gladness he once enjoyed.$n$,false),
(46038,'S','1-adam-eve',54,10,'1-adam-eve',54,10,$n$Hebrews 1:7 — *And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire.* The cherub of flaming sword and the descending angels of 1 Adam and Eve 54:10 are these flame-of-fire ministers.$n$,$n$Then, again, other angels came down close to the place where Adam and Eve were. They were divided between joy and sorrow.$n$,false),
(46039,'S','1-adam-eve',54,8,'1-adam-eve',54,8,$n$Matthew 28:4 — *And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men.* The keepers becoming as dead men at the angel is the very terror that lays Adam and Eve as dead in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8.$n$,$n$When Adam and Eve saw the cherub coming towards them with a flaming sword of fire in his hand, they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead.$n$,false),
(46040,'S','1-adam-eve',54,9,'1-adam-eve',54,9,$n$Matthew 28:2 — *And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of Yahuah (Lord) descended from heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.* The heavens and earth shaking with the descending cherubim in 1 Adam and Eve 54:9 answers the earthquake and the descending angel at the tomb.$n$,$n$At that time the heavens and the earth shook; and another cherubim came down from heaven to the cherub who guarded the garden, and saw him amazed and silent.$n$,false),
(46041,'S','1-adam-eve',54,8,'1-adam-eve',54,8,$n$Daniel 10:9 — *Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground.* Daniel face-down and strengthless mirrors Adam and Eve fallen on their faces as dead in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8.$n$,$n$When Adam and Eve saw the cherub coming towards them with a flaming sword of fire in his hand, they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead.$n$,false),
(46042,'S','1-adam-eve',54,8,'1-adam-eve',54,8,$n$Revelation 1:17 — *And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:* Adam and Eve falling as dead before the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8 is the same collapse of flesh before glory that fells John.$n$,$n$When Adam and Eve saw the cherub coming towards them with a flaming sword of fire in his hand, they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead.$n$,false),
(46043,'S','1-adam-eve',54,5,'1-adam-eve',54,5,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The enmity the stayed sword preserves in 1 Adam and Eve 54:5 ends with Satan crushed under the seed it kept alive.$n$,$n$And the sword of the cherub seemed to shoot flames a distance away from it. But when he raised it over Adam and Eve, the flame of the sword did not flash forth.$n$,false),
(46044,'S','1-adam-eve',54,6,'1-adam-eve',54,6,$n$Psalm 103:13 — *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him.* The favor the cherub perceives toward Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 54:6 is the Father's pity on His dust-made children.$n$,$n$Therefore the cherub thought that Elohim (God) was favorable to them, and was bringing them back into the garden. And the cherub stood wondering.$n$,false),
(46045,'S','1-adam-eve',54,6,'1-adam-eve',54,6,$n$Lamentations 3:22 — *It is of the LORD'S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.* The cherub's wonder that Elohim is favorable in 1 Adam and Eve 54:6 is exactly the un-consuming mercy of Yahuah.$n$,$n$Therefore the cherub thought that Elohim (God) was favorable to them, and was bringing them back into the garden. And the cherub stood wondering.$n$,false),
(46046,'S','1-adam-eve',54,5,'1-adam-eve',54,5,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The flame that will not flash forth in 1 Adam and Eve 54:5 is the first mercy that keeps the seed of the woman alive against the serpent.$n$,$n$And the sword of the cherub seemed to shoot flames a distance away from it. But when he raised it over Adam and Eve, the flame of the sword did not flash forth.$n$,false),
(46047,'S','1-adam-eve',54,4,'1-adam-eve',54,4,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The gate barred by the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 54:4 is the same way to the tree of life the Lamb opens at the end to the keepers of the commandments.$n$,$n$When Adam and Eve came to the eastern border of the garden--thinking in their hearts that the cherub was not watching--as they were standing by the gate as if wishing to go in, suddenly came the cherub with a flashing sword of fire in his hand; and when he saw them, he went forth to kill them. For he was afraid that Elohim (God) would destroy him if they went into the garden without His order.$n$,false),
(46050,'S','1-adam-eve',54,2,'1-adam-eve',54,2,$n$Genesis 3:23 — *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.* The sending-forth is why Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 54:2 can only walk the outside border of the garden they once kept.$n$,$n$And they walked in that condition to the southern border of the garden. And they began to go up that border until they came to the eastern border beyond which there was no more land.$n$,false),
(46051,'S','1-adam-eve',54,3,'1-adam-eve',54,3,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* This is the original of the cherub and flaming sword that meet Adam at the eastern gate in 1 Adam and Eve 54:3-4.$n$,$n$And the cherub who guarded the garden was standing at the western gate, and guarding it against Adam and Eve, lest they should suddenly come into the garden. And the cherub turned around, as if to put them to death; according to the commandment Elohim (God) had given him.$n$,false),
(46052,'S','1-adam-eve',55,16,'1-adam-eve',55,16,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The promise Adam is helped to await (55:16) is the manifesting of the Son to destroy the works of the very Satan warring against him.$n$,$n$Then all the angels rejoiced and praised Elohim (God), and asked Him not to destroy Adam this time, for his having sought to enter the garden; but to bear with him until the fulfillment of the promise; and to help him in this world until he was free from Satan's hand.$n$,false),
(46069,'S','1-adam-eve',56,13,'1-adam-eve',56,13,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The deceiver's renewed assault in 1 Adam & Eve 56:13 is the work the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$,$n$Then Adam came out of the cave, thinking he was one of Elohim's (God's) angels that was come to give him some good counsel.$n$,false),
(46084,'S','1-adam-eve',57,12,'1-adam-eve',57,12,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Son manifested to destroy the devil's works is the answer to Adam's plea for deliverance in 1 Adam and Eve 57:12.$n$,$n$But we will ask Elohim (God), who created us, to deliver us out of his hands."$n$,false),
(46091,'S','1-adam-eve',57,7,'1-adam-eve',57,7,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The day of deliverance Satan fears in 1 Adam and Eve 57:7 is the Son manifested to destroy his rule.$n$,$n$But now, O Adam, because you fell you are under my rule, and I am king over you; because you have obeyed me and have transgressed against your Elohim (God). Neither will there be any deliverance from my hands until the day promised you by your Elohim (God)."$n$,false),
(46113,'S','1-adam-eve',59,10,'1-adam-eve',59,10,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Yahuah's patience that keeps Adam and Eve alive through the forty days in 1 Adam and Eve 59:10 is the mercy preserving the very seed that will bruise the serpent's head.$n$,$n$But Elohim (God) had patience with Adam, and let him and Eve remain in the cave until they had fulfilled the forty days.$n$,false),
(46114,'S','1-adam-eve',59,8,'1-adam-eve',59,8,$n$Genesis 3:9 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) called unto Adam, and said unto him, Where art thou?* The Yahuah whom Adam cries to for deliverance in 1 Adam and Eve 59:8 is the same who first sought fallen Adam in mercy rather than wrath.$n$,$n$Then Adam cried before Yahuah (Lord), and said, "O Yahuah (Lord) because I transgressed a little, You have severely punished me in return for it, I ask You to deliver me out of his hands; or else have pity on me, and take my soul out of my body now in this strange land."$n$,false),
(46115,'S','1-adam-eve',59,8,'1-adam-eve',59,8,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* Adam's cry to be delivered out of Satan's hands in 1 Adam and Eve 59:8 looks ahead to the Elohim of peace crushing that same adversary under the seed's feet.$n$,$n$Then Adam cried before Yahuah (Lord), and said, "O Yahuah (Lord) because I transgressed a little, You have severely punished me in return for it, I ask You to deliver me out of his hands; or else have pity on me, and take my soul out of my body now in this strange land."$n$,false),
(46116,'S','1-adam-eve',59,6,'1-adam-eve',59,6,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The deceiver whose hollow promise is unmasked in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6 is the same liar whose deceit leads the whole earth astray into corruption.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to him, "O Adam, see, he is lord and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you divinity. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?$n$,false),
(46117,'S','1-adam-eve',59,7,'1-adam-eve',59,7,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Yahuah's charge in 1 Adam and Eve 59:7 that Adam yielded to Satan's counsel exposes the works of the devil the Son would come to destroy.$n$,$n$Did it please him just once, O Adam, to come to you, comfort you, strengthen you, rejoice with you, or send his hosts to protect you; because you have obeyed him, and have yielded to his counsel; and have followed his commandment and transgressed Mine?"$n$,false),
(46118,'S','1-adam-eve',59,6,'1-adam-eve',59,6,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The undelivered 'gift he promised' in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6 proves him the liar he was from the beginning.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to him, "O Adam, see, he is lord and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you divinity. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?$n$,false),
(46119,'S','1-adam-eve',59,6,'1-adam-eve',59,6,$n$Genesis 3:5 — *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* The 'divinity' Satan said he would give, named in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6, is the very 'ye shall be as gods' lie by which he first deceived them.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to him, "O Adam, see, he is lord and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you divinity. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?$n$,false),
(46120,'S','1-adam-eve',59,4,'1-adam-eve',59,4,$n$Luke 22:43 — *And there appeared an angel unto him from heaven, strengthening him.* As Adam is raised and told 'Be strong' after Satan's assault in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4, so the Messiah was strengthened from heaven in His own agony.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their suffering, and Elohim (God) said to Adam, "Be strong, and be not afraid of him who has just come to you."$n$,false),
(46121,'S','1-adam-eve',59,4,'1-adam-eve',59,4,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* The Word speaking to father Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is the first of those many manners in which Elohim spoke to the fathers.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their suffering, and Elohim (God) said to Adam, "Be strong, and be not afraid of him who has just come to you."$n$,false),
(46122,'S','1-adam-eve',59,4,'1-adam-eve',59,4,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The Word who comforts Adam in the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is the One who would Himself be made flesh to save the seed.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their suffering, and Elohim (God) said to Adam, "Be strong, and be not afraid of him who has just come to you."$n$,false),
(46123,'S','1-adam-eve',59,4,'1-adam-eve',59,4,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The 'Word of Elohim' who comes and raises Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is this same eternal Word, the Logos who is Elohim.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their suffering, and Elohim (God) said to Adam, "Be strong, and be not afraid of him who has just come to you."$n$,false),
(46124,'S','1-adam-eve',59,1,'1-adam-eve',59,1,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The 'hater of all good' who calls his hosts in 1 Adam and Eve 59:1 is this same old serpent who deceiveth the whole world.$n$,$n$But Satan, the hater of all good, did not allow them to finish their prayers. For he called to his hosts, and they came, all of them. Then he said to them, "Since Adam and Eve, whom we deceived, have agreed together to pray to Elohim (God) night and day, and to beg Him to deliver them, and since they will not come out of the cave until the end of the fortieth day.$n$,false),
(46125,'S','1-adam-eve',59,3,'1-adam-eve',59,3,$n$Job 2:7 — *So went Satan forth from the presence of Yahuah (LORD), and smote Job with sore boils from the sole of his foot unto his crown.* As Satan smote righteous Job in his flesh, so he beats the praying Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 — the adversary permitted to afflict the body, never the covenant.$n$,$n$Then Satan, great in wickedness, took his hosts and came into the cave, in the thirtieth night of the forty days and one; and he beat Adam and Eve, until he left them dead.$n$,false),
(46126,'S','1-adam-eve',59,3,'1-adam-eve',59,3,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The hosts that came into the cave to leave Adam and Eve for dead in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 are this same devouring adversary at his ancient work.$n$,$n$Then Satan, great in wickedness, took his hosts and came into the cave, in the thirtieth night of the forty days and one; and he beat Adam and Eve, until he left them dead.$n$,false),
(46127,'S','1-adam-eve',59,3,'1-adam-eve',59,3,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's beating of Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 is the serpent striking at the woman's seed under the enmity Yahuah decreed.$n$,$n$Then Satan, great in wickedness, took his hosts and came into the cave, in the thirtieth night of the forty days and one; and he beat Adam and Eve, until he left them dead.$n$,false),
(46132,'S','1-adam-eve',60,16,'1-adam-eve',60,16,$n$Galatians 1:8 — *But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed.* Satan's counterfeit "restore them to their former state of grace" is exactly the other gospel from a false angel of heaven that stands accursed.$n$,$n$He further said to me, 'When you have taken them to yourself, give them to eat of the fruit of the Tree of Life, and give them to drink of the water of peace; and clothe them in a garment of light, and restore them to their former state of grace, and leave them not in misery, for they came from you. But grieve not over them, nor repent of that which has come over them.$n$,false),
(46140,'S','1-adam-eve',61,16,'1-adam-eve',61,16,$n$Matthew 4:11 — *Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.* Adam and Eve, fasting and weak, appealing to Elohim to satisfy their hunger in 1 Adam and Eve 61:16, foreshadow the wilderness fast where, the tempter gone, ministry comes.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve stood up and prayed, and appealed to Elohim (God) to strengthen them, and to send them something to satisfy their hunger.$n$,false),
(46141,'S','1-adam-eve',61,18,'1-adam-eve',61,18,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The same Word who comes to feed Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 61:18 would in time be made flesh and dwell among us, full of grace and truth.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) again, and said to them, "O Adam, get up, go and bring the two figs here."$n$,false),
(46142,'S','1-adam-eve',61,18,'1-adam-eve',61,18,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes again and speaks in 1 Adam and Eve 61:18 is the eternal Logos who was in the beginning.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) again, and said to them, "O Adam, get up, go and bring the two figs here."$n$,false),
(46143,'S','1-adam-eve',61,7,'1-adam-eve',61,7,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's design *to cut off all hope from you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:7 is exactly the work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to Adam, "See, that is the father of evil arts, who brought you and Eve out of the Garden of Delights. And now, indeed, when he saw that you and Eve both joined together in fasting and praying, and that you came not out of the cave before the end of the forty days, he wished to make your purpose vein, to break your mutual bond; to cut off all hope from you, and to drive you to some place where he might destroy you.$n$,false),
(46144,'S','1-adam-eve',61,10,'1-adam-eve',61,10,$n$Jubilees 10:11 — *And we did according to all His words: all the malignant evil ones we bound in the place of condemnation, and a tenth part of them we left that they might be subject before Satan on the earth.* The mercy that *did not allow him to destroy you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:10 belongs to the same restraint by which the evil ones are bound and only a remnant left to Satan.$n$,$n$But because I am merciful and am favorable to you, I did not allow him to destroy you; instead I drove him away from you.$n$,false),
(46145,'S','1-adam-eve',61,10,'1-adam-eve',61,10,$n$James 4:7 — *Submit yourselves therefore to Elohim (God). Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.* Yahuah driving the deceiver away in His mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 61:10 is the pattern of the adversary fleeing before submission to Elohim.$n$,$n$But because I am merciful and am favorable to you, I did not allow him to destroy you; instead I drove him away from you.$n$,false),
(46146,'S','1-adam-eve',61,9,'1-adam-eve',61,9,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The disguised deceiver of 1 Adam and Eve 61:9 is the old serpent who deceives the whole world, his deceit unchanged from the first days.$n$,$n$Therefore he came to you with a face like your own, and began to give you tokens as if they were all true.$n$,false),
(46147,'S','1-adam-eve',61,7,'1-adam-eve',61,7,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* Satan seeking *to drive you to some place where he might destroy you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:7 is the prowling adversary hunting whom he may devour.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to Adam, "See, that is the father of evil arts, who brought you and Eve out of the Garden of Delights. And now, indeed, when he saw that you and Eve both joined together in fasting and praying, and that you came not out of the cave before the end of the forty days, he wished to make your purpose vein, to break your mutual bond; to cut off all hope from you, and to drive you to some place where he might destroy you.$n$,false),
(46148,'S','1-adam-eve',61,5,'1-adam-eve',61,5,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The lying messenger of 1 Adam and Eve 61:5, claiming to come from Elohim, is the liar and father of lies from the beginning.$n$,$n$Then Adam said to Elohim (God), "Did you create a man before us? For when we were in the cave there suddenly came to us a friendly old man who said to us, 'I am a messenger from Elohim (God) to you, to bring you back to some place of rest.'$n$,false),
(46149,'S','1-adam-eve',61,9,'1-adam-eve',61,9,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* Satan coming *with a face like your own* and false tokens in 1 Adam and Eve 61:9 is the same transforming deceiver Paul warns of.$n$,$n$Therefore he came to you with a face like your own, and began to give you tokens as if they were all true.$n$,false),
(46151,'S','1-adam-eve',61,3,'1-adam-eve',61,3,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The driving-away of Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3 is the first installment of the bruising sworn from Eden and finished at the feet of the saints.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them.$n$,false),
(46152,'S','1-adam-eve',61,3,'1-adam-eve',61,3,$n$Genesis 3:14 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:* The same Yahuah who first cursed the serpent in the garden curses him again in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3, driving him from Adam.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them.$n$,false),
(46153,'S','1-adam-eve',61,3,'1-adam-eve',61,3,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The Word's cursing of Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3 is the very enmity of Eden, the seed-war still striking at the woman's line outside the garden.$n$,$n$Then the Word of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them.$n$,false),
(46163,'S','1-adam-eve',62,2,'1-adam-eve',62,2,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* John names the very pattern of 1 Adam & Eve 62:2 — the devil sinning from the beginning, with the Son foretold to destroy his work.$n$,$n$So he prevented them, and went into the cave and took the two figs, and buried them outside the cave, so that Adam and Eve should not find them. He also had in his thoughts to destroy them.$n$,false),
(46173,'S','1-adam-eve',63,8,'1-adam-eve',63,8,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's destroying intent in 63:8 is the work of the devil that the Son comes to undo.$n$,$n$Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, when I sent you to fetch the figs, Satan went before you to the cave, took the figs, and buried them outside, eastward of the cave, thinking to destroy them; and not sowing them with good intent.$n$,false),
(46199,'S','1-adam-eve',65,9,'1-adam-eve',65,9,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam owning that they are now *earthy* (65:9) is the first half of the contrast whose second man is the promised Saviour from heaven.$n$,$n$Then Adam said to Eve, "Behold, our hope is now lost; and so is our trust to enter the garden. We no longer belong to the inhabitants of the garden; but from now on we are earthy and of the dust, and of the inhabitants of the earth. We shall not return to the garden, until the day in which Elohim (God) has promised to save us, and to bring us again into the garden, as He promised us."$n$,false),
(46227,'S','1-adam-eve',68,10,'1-adam-eve',68,10,$n$Jubilees 3:27 — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* The primeval altar-offering of 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the same scene Jubilees records — Adam offering a sweet savour outside the garden.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve took of the corn, and made of it an offering, and took it and offered it up on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood.$n$,false),
(46228,'S','1-adam-eve',68,10,'1-adam-eve',68,10,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake...* The offering Adam raises on the altar in 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the sweet savour Yahuah receives, as later from Noah after the flood.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve took of the corn, and made of it an offering, and took it and offered it up on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood.$n$,false),
(46229,'S','1-adam-eve',68,11,'1-adam-eve',68,11,$n$Genesis 4:26 — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* The prayer and plea for mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 68:11 is the calling on the Name that the seed of Seth carries forward.$n$,$n$And they offered this offering again on the altar they had built at first. And they stood up and prayed, and besought Yahuah (Lord) saying, "Thus, O Elohim (God), when we were in the garden, our praises went up to you, like this offering; and our innocence went up to you like incense. But now, O Elohim (God), accept this offering from us, and don't turn us away, deprived of Your mercy."$n$,false),
(46230,'S','1-adam-eve',68,10,'1-adam-eve',68,10,$n$Genesis 4:4 — *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering:* Adam's offering on the mountain in 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the same accepted way of approach his son Abel keeps.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve took of the corn, and made of it an offering, and took it and offered it up on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood.$n$,false),
(46231,'S','1-adam-eve',68,22,'1-adam-eve',68,22,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The sufferings determined 'beforehand' on Adam's days in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 belong to the Lamb foreordained before the foundation of the world.$n$,$n$After this, came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said, "O Adam, you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday.$n$,false),
(46232,'S','1-adam-eve',68,22,'1-adam-eve',68,22,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The Word who says He will be 'made flesh' to suffer in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 comes in the fulness of time, sent forth and made of a woman.$n$,$n$After this, came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said, "O Adam, you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday.$n$,false),
(46233,'S','1-adam-eve',68,23,'1-adam-eve',68,23,$n$Mark 16:9 — *Now when Yahusha (Jesus) was risen early the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom he had cast seven devils.* The Word's promise to 'create joy' by rising on the first day in 1 Adam and Eve 68:23 is fulfilled when the Messiah rises early on the first day of the week.$n$,$n$But as to the first day, I created in it all things, and I raised the heavens. And, again, through My rising again on this day, will I create joy, and raise them on high, who believe in Me; O Adam, offer this offering, all the days of your life."$n$,false),
(46234,'S','1-adam-eve',68,22,'1-adam-eve',68,22,$n$John 19:31 — *The Yahudim (Jews) therefore, because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day, (for that sabbath day was an high day,) besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, and that they might be taken away.* The preparation-day suffering and the sabbath of 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 align exactly with the cross and the high sabbath.$n$,$n$After this, came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said, "O Adam, you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday.$n$,false),
(46235,'S','1-adam-eve',68,22,'1-adam-eve',68,22,$n$John 19:14 — *And it was the preparation of the passover, and about the sixth hour: and he saith unto the Yahudim (Jews), Behold your King!* The 'preparation day Friday' of suffering foretold in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 is the very preparation on which the King is delivered up.$n$,$n$After this, came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said, "O Adam, you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday.$n$,false),
(46236,'S','1-adam-eve',68,8,'1-adam-eve',68,8,$n$Exodus 16:31 — *And the house of Yashar'el (Israel) called the name thereof Manna: and it was like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it was like wafers made with honey.* The manna on the tree in 1 Adam and Eve 68:8 bears the same heaven-given name later called Manna by the house of Yashar'el.$n$,$n$There they saw a tree, and found on it solid manna; and wondered at Elohim's (God's) power. And the angels commanded them to eat of the manna when they were hungry.$n$,false),
(46237,'S','1-adam-eve',68,8,'1-adam-eve',68,8,$n$Exodus 16:4 — *Then said Yahuah (LORD) unto Moses, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.* The solid manna Adam and Eve find in 1 Adam and Eve 68:8 prefigures the bread from heaven Yahuah rains on Yashar'el in the wilderness.$n$,$n$There they saw a tree, and found on it solid manna; and wondered at Elohim's (God's) power. And the angels commanded them to eat of the manna when they were hungry.$n$,false),
(46238,'S','1-adam-eve',68,12,'1-adam-eve',68,12,$n$Hebrews 10:10 — *By the which will we are sanctified through the offering of the body of Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) once for all.* The 'for forgiveness and for mercy' through the offered flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is the one sufficient offering of the body of the Messiah.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to Adam and Eve, "Since you have made this offering and have offered it to Me, I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an altar, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly."$n$,false),
(46239,'S','1-adam-eve',68,12,'1-adam-eve',68,12,$n$Matthew 26:26 — *And as they were eating, Yahusha (Jesus) took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.* The offering 'make it My flesh' in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is fulfilled when the Messiah breaks bread and names it His body.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to Adam and Eve, "Since you have made this offering and have offered it to Me, I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an altar, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly."$n$,false),
(46240,'S','1-adam-eve',68,12,'1-adam-eve',68,12,$n$John 6:51 — *I am the living bread which came down from heaven: if any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever: and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world.* The Word's promise to make the offering His flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is the living bread He proclaims in the flesh.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) said to Adam and Eve, "Since you have made this offering and have offered it to Me, I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an altar, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly."$n$,false),
(46241,'S','1-adam-eve',68,5,'1-adam-eve',68,5,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's assault on Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman; the enmity of Eden is already at work.$n$,$n$But it is Satan, your master who did it; he to whom you have subjected yourself; my commandment being meanwhile set aside. He it is, who burnt down the corn, and poured out the water, and who has led you astray; and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie.$n$,false),
(46242,'S','1-adam-eve',68,5,'1-adam-eve',68,5,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The false promises exposed in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 are the deceiver's trade, the same transforming guile Paul warns of.$n$,$n$But it is Satan, your master who did it; he to whom you have subjected yourself; my commandment being meanwhile set aside. He it is, who burnt down the corn, and poured out the water, and who has led you astray; and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie.$n$,false),
(46243,'S','1-adam-eve',68,5,'1-adam-eve',68,5,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* Yahuah unmasks Satan's trickery in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 with the very charge the Messiah lays against him — a liar from the beginning.$n$,$n$But it is Satan, your master who did it; he to whom you have subjected yourself; my commandment being meanwhile set aside. He it is, who burnt down the corn, and poured out the water, and who has led you astray; and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie.$n$,false),
(46244,'S','1-adam-eve',68,2,'1-adam-eve',68,2,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* The Word who restores life in 1 Adam and Eve 68:2 is the Maker of all, able to raise what He first formed.$n$,$n$Elohim (God), therefore, sent His Word, and raised up Adam and Eve from their state of death.$n$,false),
(46245,'S','1-adam-eve',68,2,'1-adam-eve',68,2,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word who raises Adam and Eve from death in 1 Adam and Eve 68:2 is the same Logos who was with Elohim in the beginning.$n$,$n$Elohim (God), therefore, sent His Word, and raised up Adam and Eve from their state of death.$n$,false),
(46246,'S','1-adam-eve',69,11,'1-adam-eve',69,11,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins "from the very beginning" — warring on Adam outside the garden — is the one the Son is manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$But when there a multitude of beasts came all around them. It was Satan's doing, in his wickedness; in order to wage war against Adam through marriage.$n$,false),
(46251,'S','1-adam-eve',69,8,'1-adam-eve',69,8,$n$Leviticus 23:16 — *Even unto the morrow after the seventh sabbath shall ye number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meat offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* Adam's healing "which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day" is reckoned by the very count that fixes the feast of weeks.$n$,$n$And Elohim (God) healed Adam in one day, which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day.$n$,false),
(46278,'S','1-adam-eve',71,14,'1-adam-eve',71,14,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who plans to destroy Adam will himself be undone by the manifested Son (1 Adam and Eve 71:14).$n$,$n$But Satan was jealous of them; and planned to destroy them.$n$,false),
(46287,'S','1-adam-eve',71,6,'1-adam-eve',71,6,$n$*Then Adam got up, and spread his hands before Elohim (God), beseeching and entreating Him with tears, to forgive him what he had done. And Adam remained thus standing and praying forty days and forty nights. He neither ate nor drank until he dropped down on the ground from hunger and thirst.* (1 Adam and Eve 71:6). *And he was there with Yahuah (LORD) forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water. And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.* (Exodus 34:28). Adam stands with his hands spread before Elohim (God), beseeching Him with tears for forgiveness, and for forty days and forty nights he neither eats nor drinks. Moses was with Yahuah (the LORD) forty days and forty nights in the same way, neither eating bread nor drinking water, and wrote the words of the covenant. Both men stand empty in the presence of Elohim (God) for forty days, one seeking forgiveness and the other receiving the covenant.$n$,$n$Then Adam got up, and spread his hands before Elohim (God), beseeching and entreating Him with tears, to forgive him what he had done. And Adam remained thus standing and praying forty days and forty nights. He neither ate nor drank until he dropped down on the ground from hunger and thirst.$n$,true),
(46301,'S','1-adam-eve',72,11,'1-adam-eve',72,11,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins from the beginning is the very plotter of 72:11, and the Son is manifested to undo his works.$n$,$n$Now, then, if I deceive him to do this thing, and to marry Eve without Elohim's (God's) permission, Elohim (God) will kill him then."$n$,false),
(46308,'S','1-adam-eve',73,9,'1-adam-eve',73,9,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's defeat in 73:9 is one early work of the devil undone, the work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$Thus was Satan's war with Adam defeated.$n$,false),
(46320,'S','1-adam-eve',74,9,'1-adam-eve',74,9,$n$*Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."* (1 Adam and Eve 74:9). *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). Adam and Eve wait until their children are forty days old and then say they will make an offering on the children's behalf. Genesis records that in the days of Enos men began to call upon the name of Yahuah (the LORD). Offering for the newborn is part of that calling: the first family brings its children before Elohim (God) at the start of their lives, and Genesis names the line in which the practice becomes known.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."$n$,true),
(46321,'S','1-adam-eve',74,9,'1-adam-eve',74,9,$n$Jubilees 3:27 — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* The parallel record shows Adam already an offerer from the day he left Eden, the same priestly hand that offers for the children at 1 Adam and Eve 74:9.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."$n$,false),
(46322,'S','1-adam-eve',74,9,'1-adam-eve',74,9,$n$Genesis 4:3 — *And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* The offering Adam makes for his children at 1 Adam and Eve 74:9 is the same altar-practice his children will keep, the way kept before Sinai.$n$,$n$Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."$n$,false),
(46323,'S','1-adam-eve',74,8,'1-adam-eve',74,8,$n$Hebrews 11:4 — *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, Elohim (God) testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.* Against Cain the hater stands the righteous offerer, the parting of the two lines latent in the children of 1 Adam and Eve 74:6-8.$n$,$n$But Luluwa means "beautiful," because she was more beautiful than her mother.$n$,false),
(46324,'S','1-adam-eve',74,7,'1-adam-eve',74,7,$n$Jude 1:11 — *Woe unto them! for they have gone in the way of Cain, and ran greedily after the error of Balaam for reward, and perished in the gainsaying of Core.* Jude makes Cain a whole "way" — a lineage of works — which the womb-hatred named at 1 Adam and Eve 74:7 begins.$n$,$n$The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.$n$,false),
(46325,'S','1-adam-eve',74,5,'1-adam-eve',74,5,$n$Jubilees 4:1 — *And in the third week in the second jubilee she gave birth to Cain, and in the fourth she gave birth to Abel, and in the fifth she gave birth to her daughter 'Âwân.* The parallel primeval record keeps the same sequence — Cain first, then a daughter — matching the first-born son and daughter of 1 Adam and Eve 74:5.$n$,$n$And Elohim (God) looked at His maid-servant Eve, and delivered her, and she gave birth to her first-born son, and with him a daughter.$n$,false),
(46326,'S','1-adam-eve',74,7,'1-adam-eve',74,7,$n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* John names the line Cain belongs to, confirming the hatred that 1 Adam and Eve 74:7 traces back to the womb.$n$,$n$The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.$n$,false),
(46327,'S','1-adam-eve',74,7,'1-adam-eve',74,7,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The enmity decreed at Eden's gate already burns in the womb when Cain hates his sister before birth at 1 Adam and Eve 74:7.$n$,$n$The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.$n$,false),
(46328,'S','1-adam-eve',74,4,'1-adam-eve',74,4,$n$Genesis 4:1 — *And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bare Cain, and said, I have gotten a man from Yahuah (LORD).* The brief Genesis notice of the first conception is unfolded here into Adam's prayer and Eve's deliverance at 1 Adam and Eve 74:4-5.$n$,$n$But when Adam saw the distress in which Eve was, he got up and prayed to Elohim (God), and said, "O Yahuah (Lord), look at me with the eye of Your mercy, and bring her out of her distress."$n$,false),
(46329,'S','1-adam-eve',74,3,'1-adam-eve',74,3,$n$Genesis 3:16 — *Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.* The narrator names this very sentence as the word being fulfilled in Eve's hard labour at 1 Adam and Eve 74:3.$n$,$n$Adam then took Eve to that cave. When the time came for her to give birth, she strained a lot. Adam felt sorry, and he was very worried about her because she was close to death and the words of Elohim (God) to her were being fulfilled: "In suffering shall you bear a child, and in sorrow shall you bring forth a child."$n$,false),
(46448,'S','2-adam-eve',3,1,'2-adam-eve',3,1,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The seed-war Satan opens against Adam in 2 Adam & Eve 3:1 is the very work the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$,$n$"Spend thy youth in mirth and pleasure." (12) The different forms which Satan takes (15). As for our father Adam, at the end of seven years from the day he had been severed from his wife Eve, Satan envied him, when he saw him thus separated from her; and strove to make him live with her again.$n$,false),
(46463,'S','2-adam-eve',4,3,'2-adam-eve',4,3,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The one who made Adam fall from brightness into darkness is the very work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$And Elohim (God) said to Adam, 'Look at this devil, and at his hideous look, and know that he it is who made thee fall from brightness into darkness, from peace and rest to toil and misery.$n$,false),
(46464,'S','2-adam-eve',4,1,'2-adam-eve',4,1,$n$*THEN Elohim (God) ordered Satan to show himself to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form.* (2 Adam and Eve 4:1). *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44). Elohim (God) orders Satan to appear to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form, so that Adam sees him as he is. Yahusha (Jesus) names the same enemy in the same way: a murderer from the beginning, with no truth in him, a liar and the father of lying. Adam is shown the face of the liar, and Yahusha (Jesus) names what the liar does. Both put the lie and the killing at the root.$n$,$n$THEN Elohim (God) ordered Satan to show himself to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form.$n$,true),
(46469,'S','2-adam-eve',5,11,'2-adam-eve',5,11,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Against Satan's godless 'we all are gods' (2 Adam & Eve 5:11), the Son of Elohim is manifested to destroy these works.$n$,$n$"For in our world we have no Elohim (God); but we all are gods; we all are of the light, heavenly, powerful, strong and glorious."$n$,false),
(46503,'S','2-adam-eve',7,3,'2-adam-eve',7,3,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The "enemy" Adam fears in 2 Adam and Eve 7:3 is the Satan whose head Yahuah has sworn to crush, so the seed kept is the seed that will tread him down.$n$,$n$"Be not afraid, 0 my son; there is no disgrace in it. I wish thee to marry, from fear lest the enemy overcome thee.'$n$,false),
(46506,'S','2-adam-eve',7,1,'2-adam-eve',7,1,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Adam's dread that "the enemy should appear to him another time, and overcome him" Seth is exactly the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, so guarding that line is guarding the promise of 2 Adam and Eve 7:1.$n$,$n$WHEN our father Adam saw that Seth was of a perfect heart, he wished him to marry; lest the enemy should appear to him another time, and overcome him.$n$,false),
(46576,'S','2-adam-eve',12,5,'2-adam-eve',12,5,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Seth prays to be kept "from the hand of Satan"; the manifested Son is the answer that breaks Satan's works.$n$,$n$Then when the building of the roof was completed, he commanded them to make offerings. They worked diligently at these, and brought them to Seth their father who took them and offered them upon the altar; and prayed Elohim (God) to accept their offerings, to have mercy on the souls of his children, and to keep them from the hand of Satan.$n$,false),
(46606,'S','2-adam-eve',14,3,'2-adam-eve',14,3,$n$*Then Enos called his son Cainan and said to him, "See, 0 my son, and set thy heart on thy people, and establish them in righteousness, and in innocence; and stand ministering before the body of our father Adam, all the days of thy life."* (2 Adam and Eve 14:3). *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). Enos charges his son Cainan to set his heart on his people, to establish them in righteousness and innocence, and to stand ministering before the body of Adam all his days. Genesis says that in the days of Enos, son of Seth, men began to call upon the name of Yahuah (the LORD). The charge to Cainan shows what that calling looked like in Enos's house: a righteous people kept in order, ministering before the body of their father Adam.$n$,$n$Then Enos called his son Cainan and said to him, "See, 0 my son, and set thy heart on thy people, and establish them in righteousness, and in innocence; and stand ministering before the body of our father Adam, all the days of thy life."$n$,true),
(46646,'S','2-adam-eve',17,9,'2-adam-eve',17,9,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who counterfeits Adam and Abel here is the one the promised Son is manifested to destroy.$n$,$n$Then the elder began to weep, and the rest wept with him; and he said to Jared, "I am Adam whom Elohim (God) made first; and this is Abel my son, who was killed by his brother Cain, into whose heart Satan put to murder him.$n$,false),
(46653,'S','2-adam-eve',18,14,'2-adam-eve',18,14,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Elohim who *appeared* and *blessed* on the altar (18:14) is the same manifested Son who comes to undo the deceiver's apparitions throughout this book.$n$,$n$Then Elohim (God) appeared unto Jared on the altar and blessed him and his children, and accepted their offerings; and commanded Jared to take of the sacred fire from the altar, and with it to light the lamp that shed light on the body of Adam.$n$,false),
(46660,'S','2-adam-eve',18,9,'2-adam-eve',18,9,$n$Luke 22:31 — *And Yahusha (Lord) said, Simon, Simon, behold, Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat:* Jared asks to be hidden *from him unto the day of my death* (18:9) — the same sifting hand Messiah warns reaches for His own, met by intercession.$n$,$n$Then Jared fell upon the bodies and embraced them, and said, "0 my fathers, through your intercession, let Elohim (God) deliver me from the hand of Satan! And I beg you will ask Elohim (God) to keep me and to hide me from him unto the day of my death."$n$,false),
(46683,'S','2-adam-eve',20,27,'2-adam-eve',20,27,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Jared's warning that the descenders shall be called 'children of the devil' in 2 Adam & Eve 20:27 is John's same verdict on those of the devil who sins from the beginning.$n$,$n$He again adjured them, saying, "I adjure by the death of our father Adam, and by the blood of Abel, of Seth, of Enos, of Cainan, and of Mahalaleel, to hearken to me, and not to go down from this holy mountain; for the moment you leave it, you will be reft of life and of mercy; and you shall no longer be called 'children of Elohim (God),' but 'children of the devil.'$n$,false),
(46717,'S','2-adam-eve',22,10,'2-adam-eve',22,10,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* The children of Seth going down to fall "into sin with the children of Cain" (22:10) is Genesis' sons of Elohim taking the daughters of men.$n$,$n$Altogether, not one of our fathers or of their children, remained on that holy mountain, except those three, Methuselah, Lamech, and Noah. For all the rest went down from the mountain and fell into sin with the children of Cain. Therefore were they forbidden that mountain, and none remained on it but those three men.$n$,false);
INSERT INTO _s463eam VALUES
(10892,45529,$n$1 Adam and Eve 13:3 — *I deprived him of that bright nature, and he became dark.* Isaiah's son of the morning is the bright one who lost his light when he broke the commandment.$n$),
(10931,45631,$n$1 Adam and Eve 23:9 — *lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil thing; for Thine is the kingdom.* Adam's prayer asks for deliverance and confesses the kingdom as Elohim's, as Matthew 6:13 does.$n$),
(10934,45648,$n$1 Adam and Eve 24:5 — *so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it.* What Adam sought through blood, the Word promises to supply with His own, as Hebrews 9:22 says no remission comes without it.$n$),
(10942,45674,$n$1 Adam and Eve 26:11 — *bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days.* Adam is told to wait out the days until the covenant, and Abraham obtained the promise by patient endurance.$n$),
(10973,45776,$n$1 Adam and Eve 34:11 — *if You had punished me as You said, with death, I should have died that very moment.* Adam's wonder that death did not strike at once is the death by one man that Paul traces in Romans 5:12.$n$),
(10974,45772,$n$1 Adam and Eve 34:14 — *Then You drew a rib out of my side, and created it after my own likeness and image.* Adam tells of the rib and the sleep from his own side, and Jubilees 3:5 tells the same from Yahuah's.$n$),
(10989,45823,$n$1 Adam and Eve 38:2 — *I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled.* The wait given to Adam is counted in the days of a thousand years that Jubilees 4:30 describes.$n$),
(10989,45824,$n$1 Adam and Eve 38:2 — *only when the 5500 years are fulfilled.* The span set before Adam is measured on the scale Peter names, a day with Yahuah being a thousand years.$n$),
(10988,45825,$n$1 Adam and Eve 38:2 — *you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants.* The tree promised to Adam's righteous descendants is the tree open to those who do His commandments in Revelation 22:14.$n$),
(11002,45878,$n$1 Adam and Eve 42:8 — *My blood shall be the Water of Life to you at that time.* The Water of Life promised to Adam's believing descendants is the rivers of living water Yahusha gives in John 7:38.$n$),
(11023,45948,$n$1 Adam and Eve 47:6 — *they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins.* Adam and Eve's prayer for forgiveness is the same calling on the Name that Genesis 4:26 records in Enos's day.$n$),
(11031,45968,$n$1 Adam and Eve 49:9 — *on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam.* The third day rising spoken to Adam is the gospel Paul gives in 1 Corinthians 15:4.$n$),
(11114,46287,$n$1 Adam and Eve 71:6 — *He neither ate nor drank until he dropped down on the ground from hunger and thirst.* Adam's forty days without food or drink in prayer matches Moses' forty days before Yahuah in Exodus 34:28.$n$),
(11128,46320,$n$1 Adam and Eve 74:9 — *We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children.* Adam and Eve's offering for their children belongs to the calling on Yahuah's name that Genesis 4:26 records.$n$),
(11163,46464,$n$2 Adam and Eve 4:1 — *Elohim (God) ordered Satan to show himself to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form.* Satan shown to Adam in his own form is the murderer and liar from the beginning whom Yahusha names in John 8:44.$n$),
(11207,46606,$n$2 Adam and Eve 14:3 — *stand ministering before the body of our father Adam, all the days of thy life.* Enos's charge to Cainan to keep a righteous people is the calling on the Name that Genesis 4:26 places in Enos's days.$n$),
(10855,45379,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The covenant Elohim makes with the lifted-up Adam (1 Adam and Eve 3:9) is fulfilled when the Son is manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$),
(10868,45415,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Against the curse held over the hardened in 1 Adam and Eve 6:10 stands the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$),
(10895,45517,$n$Ephesians 5:8 — *For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in Yahusha (Lord): walk as children of light:* Those Elohim made to do their work in the day's light are called to walk as the children of light He willed from the first.$n$),
(10898,45537,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Yahuah's "But I will" save you (14:4) is the manifested Son destroying the very works of Satan whose hand held Adam.$n$),
(10903,45543,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The salvation Adam mourns over in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is exactly this — the Son manifested to suffer and undo the works of the serpent.$n$),
(10909,45568,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The serpent that became Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 17:2 is the devil who sinned from the beginning, whose works the Son of Elohim came to destroy.$n$),
(10913,45575,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word silencing the serpent's deceiving speech in 1 Adam and Eve 18:7 foreshadows the Son manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$),
(10918,45596,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word's stripping the serpent of its ability to hurt in 20:2 foreshadows the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$),
(10922,45609,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins "from the very beginning" is the very one assaulting the first parents at 21:6 — and the Son is manifested to undo his work.$n$),
(10926,45621,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Satan who deceived Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 22:5 is the enemy from the beginning whose works the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$),
(10936,45669,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The self-slaughter Adam imagines (25:1) is a work of the devil, and the promised Son comes precisely to undo it.$n$),
(10942,45676,$n$James 5:7 — *Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of Yahusha (Lord). Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain.* The "bear long... until the time of My covenant is come" of 1 Adam & Eve 26:11 is the same patient waiting for the coming of Yahusha (Lord).$n$),
(10946,45692,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The angel stripping Satan to his *own hideous form* in 1 Adam and Eve 27:13 foreshadows the Son manifested to undo his works.$n$),
(10951,45706,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The words that sink into the hearts of Adam and Eve at 1 Adam and Eve 28:6 are the devil's work, which only the manifested Son undoes.$n$),
(10953,45722,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* John names the very work Elohim begins to undo when He curses Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 29:1 — the devil who sins from the beginning meets the Son manifested to destroy his works.$n$),
(10970,45758,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* When Adam is given *to know it was Satan* in 1 Adam & Eve 33:14, the deceiver's work is unmasked — the very works the Son of Elohim was manifested to destroy.$n$),
(10971,45781,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam's confession of being made from earth's dust sets the very contrast Sha'ul draws against the heavenly Man.$n$),
(10986,45808,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The mercy Adam pleads in 1 Adam & Eve 37:10 is the seed-war's end — the Son manifested to undo the serpent's hour.$n$),
(10996,45845,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam’s animal body of earth that must be fed in 1 Adam & Eve 40:2 is the earthy first man, set against the heavenly Second.$n$),
(11006,45889,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The plot to put their souls to death in 1 Adam and Eve 43:10 is the devil's work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11011,45903,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The destruction withheld by mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 is appointed for the end, when the Son is manifested to destroy the devil's works.$n$),
(11015,45921,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The plague of fire "that will be burning around you" is the work of the devil the Son came to destroy.$n$),
(11023,45947,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Adam's plea for forgiven sin in 1 Adam and Eve 47:6 leans on the manifested Son who undoes the devil's works.$n$),
(11025,45960,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's murderous design against Adam from the first days outside Eden is the devil who sins from the beginning, whose works the Son came to destroy.$n$),
(11031,45966,$n$Matthew 28:6 — *He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where Yahusha (Lord) lay.* The third-day rising foretold to Adam is announced at the open rock — risen as He said, the place where He lay now empty, salvation made sure for Adam's descendants.$n$),
(11029,45973,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The works of the devil that buried Adam under the stone are the very works the Son was manifested to destroy, foretold in this same chapter's promise of the third-day rising.$n$),
(11037,46001,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The serpent who deceived and stripped Adam in 51:5 is the one whose works the Son came to destroy.$n$),
(11046,46029,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Word driving the lions from Adam and Eve (53:3) is the Son manifested to destroy the works of the devil.$n$),
(11056,46052,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The promise Adam is helped to await (55:16) is the manifesting of the Son to destroy the works of the very Satan warring against him.$n$),
(11060,46069,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The deceiver's renewed assault in 1 Adam & Eve 56:13 is the work the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$),
(11065,46084,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Son manifested to destroy the devil's works is the answer to Adam's plea for deliverance in 1 Adam and Eve 57:12.$n$),
(11063,46091,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The day of deliverance Satan fears in 1 Adam and Eve 57:7 is the Son manifested to destroy his rule.$n$),
(11071,46117,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Yahuah's charge in 1 Adam and Eve 59:7 that Adam yielded to Satan's counsel exposes the works of the devil the Son would come to destroy.$n$),
(11078,46143,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's design *to cut off all hope from you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:7 is exactly the work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11080,46163,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* John names the very pattern of 1 Adam & Eve 62:2 — the devil sinning from the beginning, with the Son foretold to destroy his work.$n$),
(11083,46173,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's destroying intent in 63:8 is the work of the devil that the Son comes to undo.$n$),
(11089,46199,$n$1 Corinthians 15:47 — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* Adam owning that they are now *earthy* (65:9) is the first half of the contrast whose second man is the promised Saviour from heaven.$n$),
(11108,46246,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins "from the very beginning" — warring on Adam outside the garden — is the one the Son is manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11116,46278,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who plans to destroy Adam will himself be undone by the manifested Son (1 Adam and Eve 71:14).$n$),
(11118,46301,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who sins from the beginning is the very plotter of 72:11, and the Son is manifested to undo his works.$n$),
(11124,46308,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Satan's defeat in 73:9 is one early work of the devil undone, the work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11159,46448,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The seed-war Satan opens against Adam in 2 Adam & Eve 3:1 is the very work the manifested Son comes to destroy.$n$),
(11163,46463,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The one who made Adam fall from brightness into darkness is the very work the Son was manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11169,46469,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Against Satan's godless 'we all are gods' (2 Adam & Eve 5:11), the Son of Elohim is manifested to destroy these works.$n$),
(11175,46503,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The "enemy" Adam fears in 2 Adam and Eve 7:3 is the Satan whose head Yahuah has sworn to crush, so the seed kept is the seed that will tread him down.$n$),
(11199,46576,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Seth prays to be kept "from the hand of Satan"; the manifested Son is the answer that breaks Satan's works.$n$),
(11217,46646,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The devil who counterfeits Adam and Abel here is the one the promised Son is manifested to destroy.$n$),
(11224,46653,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* The Elohim who *appeared* and *blessed* on the altar (18:14) is the same manifested Son who comes to undo the deceiver's apparitions throughout this book.$n$),
(11222,46660,$n$Luke 22:31 — *And Yahusha (Lord) said, Simon, Simon, behold, Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat:* Jared asks to be hidden *from him unto the day of my death* (18:9) — the same sifting hand Messiah warns reaches for His own, met by intercession.$n$),
(11233,46683,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Jared's warning that the descenders shall be called 'children of the devil' in 2 Adam & Eve 20:27 is John's same verdict on those of the devil who sins from the beginning.$n$),
(10875,45453,$n$1 Corinthians 13:12 — *For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known.* Adam who once could "see things far away" now sees "only near at hand" — the darkened glass of a fallen race awaiting restored sight.$n$),
(10934,45649,$n$Hebrews 9:12 — *Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us.* The Word's pledge "I will offer My blood" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is fulfilled when Messiah enters by His own blood — the once-for-all forgiveness promised to Adam.$n$),
(10938,45663,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The covenant 'that He would save him at the end of the days' (25:7) is kept when the same Word takes flesh.$n$),
(10941,45680,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "When, however, the covenant is fulfilled" of 1 Adam & Eve 26:15 is the fulness of time when the promised Son of the woman is sent.$n$),
(11010,45908,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The Word's charge that Satan "once before you deceived My servants" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 names the disguising deceiver Paul warns of.$n$),
(11075,46132,$n$Galatians 1:8 — *But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed.* Satan's counterfeit "restore them to their former state of grace" is exactly the other gospel from a false angel of heaven that stands accursed.$n$),
(11101,46238,$n$Hebrews 10:10 — *By the which will we are sanctified through the offering of the body of Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) once for all.* The 'for forgiveness and for mercy' through the offered flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is the one sufficient offering of the body of the Messiah.$n$),
(11101,46239,$n$Matthew 26:26 — *And as they were eating, Yahusha (Jesus) took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.* The offering 'make it My flesh' in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is fulfilled when the Messiah breaks bread and names it His body.$n$),
(11107,46251,$n$Leviticus 23:16 — *Even unto the morrow after the seventh sabbath shall ye number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meat offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* Adam's healing "which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day" is reckoned by the very count that fixes the feast of weeks.$n$),
(11175,46506,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Adam's dread that "the enemy should appear to him another time, and overcome him" Seth is exactly the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, so guarding that line is guarding the promise of 2 Adam and Eve 7:1.$n$),
(11242,46717,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* The children of Seth going down to fall "into sin with the children of Cain" (22:10) is Genesis' sons of Elohim taking the daughters of men.$n$),
(10856,45375,$n$Jubilees 3:29 — *And He sent out of the Garden of Eden all flesh that was in the Garden of Eden, and all flesh was scattered according to its kinds, and according to its types to the places which had been created for them.* The same primeval record of the expulsion that frames the gate-scene of 1 Adam and Eve 3:10 — one history of the driven-out, kept in both books.$n$),
(10856,45376,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The "Word of Yahuah" who comes to Adam and Eve and raises them up (1 Adam and Eve 3:15) is the Word who would be made flesh and dwell among men.$n$),
(10856,45377,$n$Psalms 91:11 — *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* The Angel Elohim sends "to keep the garden" (1 Adam and Eve 3:14) is the same mercy that gives His angels charge to keep His own.$n$),
(10856,45378,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The cherub "with a sword of flashing fire" at the gate (1 Adam and Eve 3:10) is the very cherub and flaming sword Yahuah set to keep the way of the tree of life.$n$),
(10855,45380,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The mercy that lifts the fallen Adam and seals a covenant (1 Adam and Eve 3:9) carries the same promise — Satan bruised under foot shortly.$n$),
(10855,45381,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The covenant made "by the tree where Eve took of the fruit" (1 Adam and Eve 3:7) is the seed-promise spoken over the serpent at that same fall.$n$),
(10854,45382,$n$Hebrews 1:2 — *Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds;* The Word promised to save "when the five and a half days are fulfilled" (1 Adam and Eve 3:2) is the Son who in the last days speaks and by whom the worlds were made.$n$),
(10854,45383,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour appointed to a fixed term in 1 Adam and Eve 3:6 is the Lamb foreordained before the foundation of the world.$n$),
(10854,45384,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "5,000 and 500 years" until One comes to save (1 Adam and Eve 3:6) is the fulness of time at which the Son was sent forth.$n$),
(10853,45385,$n$Colossians 1:16 — *For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:* The Word "that created you" in 1 Adam and Eve 3:1 is the One by whom all things were made.$n$),
(10853,45386,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The Word who "will again save you" (1 Adam and Eve 3:2) is the Word made flesh to come and save what was fallen.$n$),
(10853,45387,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* This is exactly the Word "that created you" of 1 Adam and Eve 3:1 — the Maker of Adam is the Saviour of Adam.$n$),
(10853,45388,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word Elohim promises to send Adam is the One who was with Elohim from the beginning, naming the Logos at the very first day outside Eden in 1 Adam and Eve 3:1.$n$),
(10864,45404,$n$1 Timothy 2:15 — *Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety.* As Eve fears to stand *one and alone* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:8, Sha'ul holds out the woman's saving hope through the seed and the faith she keeps.$n$),
(10864,45405,$n$Genesis 2:24 — *Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh.* Eve's plea that she and Adam *die the same day* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:13 is the one-flesh bond of Eden refusing to be sundered even by death.$n$),
(10863,45406,$n$Romans 5:17 — *For if by one man's offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by one, Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ).* The life and standing Eve begs for Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 5:7 is the reign-in-life that grace secures over the fall.$n$),
(10863,45407,$n$2 Corinthians 7:10 — *For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death.* Eve's prayer that Adam be raised *that he may cry and repent* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:6 is exactly the sorrow-unto-life Sha'ul distinguishes from the world's sorrow-unto-death.$n$),
(10862,45408,$n$Jubilees 3:5 — *And Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and he slept, and He took for the woman one rib from amongst his ribs, and this rib was the origin of the woman from amongst his ribs, and He built up the flesh in its stead, and built the woman.* The restored books keep one primeval history: Jubilees tells the same making of woman that Eve recites in 1 Adam and Eve 5:9-10.$n$),
(10862,45409,$n$Genesis 2:23 — *And Adam said, This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.* Eve's cry that *I and he are one* in 1 Adam and Eve 5:11 echoes Adam's first word over her in Eden.$n$),
(10862,45410,$n$Genesis 2:21 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof.* This is the very act Eve recounts to Yahuah in 1 Adam and Eve 5:9, the bone taken from Adam's side and the flesh restored.$n$),
(10861,45411,$n$Romans 5:12 — *Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned.* The fall from light into darkness Eve laments in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 is the entrance of sin and death that Sha'ul traces back to Eden.$n$),
(10861,45412,$n$1 Timothy 2:14 — *And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression.* Sha'ul's verdict matches Eve's own self-judgment in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 that she alone brought Adam down.$n$),
(10861,45413,$n$Genesis 3:13 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the woman, What is this that thou hast done? And the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.* Eve's plea that Yahuah forgive and not remember her sin in 1 Adam and Eve 5:4 unfolds the confession first wrung from her at the tree.$n$),
(10861,45414,$n$Genesis 3:6 — *And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat.* This is the very deed Eve confesses in 1 Adam and Eve 5:5 when she says she alone caused Adam to fall from the garden.$n$),
(10903,45542,$n$1 Peter 1:19 — *But with the precious blood of Messiah (Christ), as of a lamb without blemish and without spot:* — the suffering for salvation promised in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is purchased by the spotless blood of the Lamb.$n$),
(10903,45544,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The suffering Elohim foretold in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is the bruised heel of the woman's seed crushing the serpent's head.$n$),
(10902,45545,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* — the same Elohim who spake to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 with the word of His coming suffering.$n$),
(10902,45546,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* — Adam hears in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 of a salvation already foreordained before the world, manifest only in the last times.$n$),
(10902,45547,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The promise of 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 — that Elohim should suffer — is kept when the Word takes flesh to suffer for our salvation.$n$),
(10902,45548,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Elohim who in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 told Adam He should suffer for their salvation is the eternal Word, the Logos who speaks with Adam outside the garden.$n$),
(10901,45549,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The barred return of 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 ends here, when the way to the tree of life is opened again at the fulfillment of the days.$n$),
(10901,45550,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* — the fulfillment of the days decreed in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is the appointed coming of the seed of the woman.$n$),
(10901,45551,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The flaming sword is why Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 may not return until the days decreed are fulfilled.$n$),
(10901,45552,$n$Genesis 3:23 — *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.* This is the very expulsion 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 weeps over, the LORD's word that they should not return to the garden.$n$),
(10913,45574,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The contrast is sharp: in 1 Adam and Eve 18:5 a true angel of Yahuah delivers Adam and Eve, where elsewhere Satan only counterfeits the angelic to deceive them.$n$),
(10913,45576,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* The same Word who made the serpent and gave it speech now removes it in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6-7 — the Maker disposing of His own creature.$n$),
(10913,45577,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes to the serpent and pronounces judgment in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6 is the eternal Word of the prologue.$n$),
(10912,45578,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The Word's sentence against the serpent in 1 Adam and Eve 18:6 is the same bruising of Satan the gospel promises.$n$),
(10912,45579,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The serpent that still tries to kill though already cursed in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 is the murderer from the beginning.$n$),
(10912,45580,$n$Genesis 3:14 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:* The serpent's own words in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 — slippery, going on its belly — are Eden's curse confessed from its own mouth.$n$),
(10911,45581,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The serpent that threw down and squeezed Adam and Eve to kill them in 1 Adam and Eve 18:4 is the same devouring adversary the apostle names.$n$),
(10911,45582,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The blood-red serpent that swells to kill in 1 Adam and Eve 18:1 is that same old serpent named at the end of the war.$n$),
(10911,45583,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The serpent running straight for Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 18:2 is the very enmity Yahuah set in Eden being acted out from the first day outside the garden.$n$),
(10935,45644,$n$Hebrews 1:3 — *Who being the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high;* The Word who counts the days until He brings Adam back to the garden (1 Adam and Eve 24:6) is the Son who by Himself purges sins — the same Logos who comforts Adam now seated on high.$n$),
(10935,45645,$n$Jubilees 6:14 — *And for this law there is no limit of days, for it is for ever. They shall observe it throughout their generations, so that they may continue supplicating on your behalf with blood before the altar; every day and at the time of morning and evening they shall seek forgiveness on your behalf perpetually before Yahuah (God) that they may keep it and not be rooted out.* The standing order "when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:7 is Jubilees' perpetual blood-supplication before the altar — the same covenant of continual offering across the restored library.$n$),
(10935,45646,$n$Galatians 4:5 — *To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.* The return "into the garden" promised when the days of the covenant are fulfilled (1 Adam and Eve 24:6) is this redemption and adoption — the bound exile of Adam undone in Messiah.$n$),
(10934,45647,$n$Matthew 26:28 — *For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.* The blood the Word promises to make "forgiveness of sins" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:5 is the blood Messiah names at the table — shed for the remission Adam was first promised.$n$),
(10934,45650,$n$Genesis 8:20 — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD); and took of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl, and offered burnt offerings on the altar.* The "altar of the earth" the Word promises in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is the same earthen altar the fathers build, Noah's after the flood standing in the line that began with Adam's.$n$),
(10933,45651,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* That the Word can promise His own blood to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 shows the Lamb was foreordained before the foundation — manifest in the last days, but pledged at the first.$n$),
(10933,45652,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The "days of the covenant" the Word counts to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 close in this fulness of time, the Son made of a woman of Adam's seed.$n$),
(10933,45653,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The promise "I become flesh of your descendants" in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is the incarnation John records — the Word taking the flesh of Adam's own line.$n$),
(10933,45654,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 24:4 is this same eternal Word — the Logos addressing the man He had formed.$n$),
(10932,45655,$n$Leviticus 17:11 — *For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls: for it is the blood that maketh an atonement for the soul.* The law Sinai will write was already the unspoken ground of Adam's act in 1 Adam and Eve 24:1 — atonement by blood upon the altar, kept before ever it was commanded.$n$),
(10932,45656,$n$Jubilees 6:3 — *And he placed the fat thereof on the altar, and he took an ox, and a goat, and a sheep and kids, and salt, and a turtle-dove, and the young of a dove, and placed a burnt sacrifice on the altar, and poured thereon an offering mingled with oil, and sprinkled wine and strewed frankincense over everything, and caused a goodly savour to arise, acceptable before Yahuah (God).* Jubilees' goodly savour rising acceptable before Yahuah echoes the sweet savor of 1 Adam and Eve 24:3 — the same primeval altar-mercy carried across the restored library.$n$),
(10932,45657,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake; for the imagination of man's heart is evil from his youth; neither will I again smite any more every thing living, as I have done.* Noah's sweet savour at the post-flood altar is word-for-word the sweet savor Yahuah smells over Adam's offering in 1 Adam and Eve 24:3, mercy meeting the lifted blood.$n$),
(10932,45658,$n$Genesis 4:4 — *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering:* The respect Yahuah shows Abel's blood-offering is the same wondering acceptance He shows Adam and Eve's blood in 1 Adam and Eve 24:1, the way of approach kept from the first day outside Eden.$n$),
(10952,45702,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's plot to wipe off their name from the earth at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 is his strike at the heel, but the head-crushing Seed is already promised.$n$),
(10952,45703,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The Devil who draws near to throw Adam and Eve down and kill them at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 is the roaring lion seeking to devour the seed.$n$),
(10952,45704,$n$Matthew 4:8 — *Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;* As Satan covets to wipe off Adam's name so the earth remains his alone at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10, he likewise offers the kingdoms of the world he claims to own.$n$),
(10952,45705,$n$Matthew 4:6 — *And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of Elohim (God), cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.* The devil who marches the first Adam up a high mountain to throw him down at 1 Adam and Eve 28:10 tempts the second Adam to the very same fall.$n$),
(10951,45707,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The garden Satan promises to reopen at 1 Adam and Eve 28:5 was sealed by the flaming sword, so his offer is a lie at the very threshold.$n$),
(10951,45708,$n$Genesis 3:5 — *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* Satan's false promise of restoration at 1 Adam and Eve 28:5 is the same overreaching lie he used in the garden, offering by deceit what is not his to give.$n$),
(10950,45709,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Adam's trial at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7 is one stroke of the enmity Yahuah set between the serpent and the seed of the woman.$n$),
(10950,45710,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The deceiver testing Adam at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7 is the liar who has murdered by falsehood from the beginning.$n$),
(10950,45711,$n$Genesis 3:4 — *And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die:* The lie that overthrew Eve in the garden is named again at 1 Adam and Eve 28:7, where Yahuah waits to see whether Adam will be overcome as she was.$n$),
(10949,45712,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The host Satan gathers in 1 Adam and Eve 28:1 are the angels cast down with him, and his trade is the deceiving of the whole world.$n$),
(10949,45713,$n$2 Corinthians 11:3 — *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ).* As Adam and Eve mistake the deceiver for angels of Elohim at 1 Adam and Eve 28:2, Sha'ul warns the same subtilty still corrupts the mind.$n$),
(10949,45714,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The crafty Satan who comes on a cloud at 1 Adam and Eve 28:1 is the same adversary Sha'ul unmasks, working by counterfeit glory.$n$),
(10955,45715,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The golden rods laid up to shine in Adam's cave-night in 1 Adam and Eve 29:7 are the first of the treasure kept against the Saviour's coming — the very gold the magi at last bring to the child.$n$),
(10955,45716,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The Michael sent to comfort Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:6 is the great prince Daniel sees standing for the children of the covenant — the same guardian from the first man to the last trouble.$n$),
(10955,45717,$n$Jude 1:9 — *Yet Michael the archangel, when contending with the devil he disputed about the body of Moses, durst not bring against him a railing accusation, but said, Yahuah (Lord) rebuke thee.* The angel Michael whom Elohim sends to fetch the golden rods in 1 Adam and Eve 29:6 is the same archangel Jude names contending against the devil — Yahuah's appointed servant against the enemy of Adam's race.$n$),
(10954,45718,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The Satan who seeks to deceive Adam and his seed in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 is the very serpent John names as the deceiver of the whole world.$n$),
(10954,45719,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* Peter's charge to watchfulness is the practical form of the Word's first-day warning to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 — know and understand this Satan who seeks your destruction.$n$),
(10954,45720,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The Word's warning that Satan seeks to deceive Adam and his descendants in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 unmasks the enemy's one tactic — the false light Paul exposes.$n$),
(10954,45721,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word that comes to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 29:4 to counsel and warn him is the Logos John names — the same who was with Elohim from the beginning now walking with the first man.$n$),
(10953,45723,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* As Satan and his hosts flee the rebuke in 1 Adam and Eve 29:2, Paul names the end of that same war — the serpent bruised under the feet of the redeemed.$n$),
(10953,45724,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The loud curse Elohim speaks over Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 29:1 is the garden-curse still in force, the serpent striking at the seed of the woman.$n$),
(10959,45725,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim whose order moves the angels and the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 30:3 is the Logos who was in the beginning, soon to restore the light Adam lost.$n$),
(10959,45726,$n$Exodus 30:34 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* The sweet-smelling incense Yahuah commands brought for Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 30:2 is the same holy frankincense He later commands for the tabernacle's perfume.$n$),
(10958,45727,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The spring of water that comforts the mourners in 1 Adam and Eve 30:8 anticipates the river of life that flows from the throne in the City.$n$),
(10958,45728,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's seeking to make an end of Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 30:9 is the serpent striking at the seed; Yahuah's comfort keeps the seed He swore to preserve.$n$),
(10957,45729,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The Tree of Life in the garden of 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 is the same Yahuah planted in the midst of Eden at the beginning.$n$),
(10957,45730,$n$Revelation 22:2 — *In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* The Tree of Life beside which the angels stand in 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 stands again, unbarred, in the restored City.$n$),
(10957,45731,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The cherub who guards the Tree in 1 Adam and Eve 30:7 is the same guardian set at the east of Eden after the expulsion.$n$),
(10956,45732,$n$Genesis 3:17 — *And unto Adam he said, Because thou hast hearkened unto the voice of thy wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of which I commanded thee, saying, Thou shalt not eat of it: cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;* The myrrh that is a token of sorrow in 1 Adam and Eve 30:10 answers the sorrow pronounced over the ground at the fall.$n$),
(10956,45733,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The gold, incense, and myrrh gathered from the borders of the garden in 1 Adam and Eve 30:6 are the very gifts borne to Bethlehem.$n$),
(10956,45734,$n$Matthew 2:11 — *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* The three tokens given to Adam at 1 Adam and Eve 30:10 are the same three the magi lay before the Saviour — kept from the garden against His coming.$n$),
(10990,45821,$n$Hebrews 8:6 — *But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.* The covenant Adam is told to endure for in 1 Adam and Eve 38:5 is the better covenant the coming Mediator establishes.$n$),
(10990,45822,$n$2 Corinthians 1:20 — *For all the promises of Elohim (God) in him are yea, and in him Amen, unto the glory of Elohim (God) by us.* The hope the Word promises not to disappoint in 1 Adam and Eve 38:5 is sure because all His promises are Yea and Amen in the Son.$n$),
(10988,45826,$n$Revelation 2:7 — *He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God).* The deferred fruit of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is the overcomer's reward when paradise is restored.$n$),
(10988,45827,$n$Genesis 3:22 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said, Behold, the man is become as one of us, to know good and evil: and now, lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever:* The Word's "not now" in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 echoes the barring of fallen Adam from the tree of life.$n$),
(10988,45828,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The fruit Adam asks for in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is this same Tree of Life set in the midst of Eden.$n$),
(10987,45829,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The fulfilled 5500 years of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is the fulness of time when the promised Son is sent.$n$),
(10987,45830,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour pledged for the end of the 5500 years in 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 was already foreordained before the world was.$n$),
(10987,45831,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* The Word speaking to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 38:1 is the first of those manifold speakings to the fathers fulfilled at last in the Son.$n$),
(10987,45832,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The 5500-year promise of 1 Adam and Eve 38:2 is fulfilled when this same Word takes flesh to save Adam's seed.$n$),
(10987,45833,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word who comes to speak with Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 38:1 is the eternal Logos, with Elohim and Elohim from the beginning.$n$),
(11000,45855,$n$Jubilees 3:16 — *And he tilled (the garden), and was naked and knew it not, and was not ashamed, and he protected the garden from the birds and beasts and cattle, and gathered its fruit, and ate, and put aside the residue for himself and for his wife and put aside that which was being kept.* The garden-fruit Adam once gathered freely is the same garden he now stands outside of, fasting, in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5.$n$),
(11000,45856,$n$Genesis 4:26 — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* The praying and calling on Yahuah in 1 Adam and Eve 41:8 is the first keeping of the way of the seed, before ever the law was given.$n$),
(11000,45857,$n$Genesis 3:7 — *And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.* The fig Adam and Eve lift onto the rods and incense in 1 Adam and Eve 41:1 is the very leaf of their first shame, now offered up to Yahuah.$n$),
(10999,45858,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* Adam's cry for mercy under the curse in 1 Adam and Eve 41:13 rests on the seed-promise that crushes the serpent at last.$n$),
(10999,45859,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* Adam grieves in 1 Adam and Eve 41:6 that Yahuah has not fed him of the Tree of Life — for the way to it is kept by the flaming sword.$n$),
(10999,45860,$n$Genesis 3:19 — *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* Adam's parched, dying flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is this very curse worked out in his body.$n$),
(10998,45861,$n$Psalms 36:8 — *They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.* The river of Yahuah's pleasure is the same Water of Life Adam thirsts after in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12.$n$),
(10998,45862,$n$Revelation 22:17 — *And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.* The freely-given Water Adam asks for in 1 Adam and Eve 41:6 is held open at last to every thirst.$n$),
(10998,45863,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The Water of Life Adam mourns in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 flows again, unbarred, at the end of the seed-war.$n$),
(10998,45864,$n$John 7:37 — *In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.* Adam's parched cry in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is the very thirst Yahusha answers with Himself.$n$),
(10998,45865,$n$John 4:14 — *But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.* The Water of Life Adam begs for in 1 Adam and Eve 41:12 is the gift the Messiah Himself names and gives.$n$),
(10997,45867,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* The Water of Life Adam seeks in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 flows from beside the tree of life he has been barred from.$n$),
(10997,45868,$n$Genesis 2:10 — *And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.* The river Adam names in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 is Eden's own four-headed river, remembered from outside the gate.$n$),
(11013,45896,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The fire that separates Adam and Eve from the cave and afflicts them in 1 Adam and Eve 44:8 echoes the flaming sword that bars the way back to the garden.$n$),
(11013,45897,$n$Genesis 3:19 — *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* Adam's lament that "our nature is altered" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:9 unfolds the curse spoken in Eden that bound man to the ground and to death.$n$),
(11012,45898,$n$1 Enoch 54:1 — *And I looked and turned to another part of the earth, and saw there a deep valley with burning fire.* The fire that surrounds the cave but cannot reach the seed in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 foreshadows the valley of burning fire prepared for Satan's hosts that Enoch beheld.$n$),
(11012,45899,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The Saviour by whom the seed is kept from the forty-sixth day outside the garden in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 was foreordained before the world's foundation.$n$),
(11012,45900,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The enemy driven off at the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 will at the last be bruised wholly under the feet of the redeemed.$n$),
(11012,45901,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's fleeing in 1 Adam and Eve 44:6 is one defeat in the enmity Yahuah set between the serpent and the seed of the woman.$n$),
(11011,45904,$n$2 Peter 3:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.* The delayed judgment "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 is Yahuah's longsuffering, not slackness.$n$),
(11011,45905,$n$Romans 2:4 — *Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of Elohim (God) leadeth thee to repentance?* The mercy and patience that spare Satan "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 are this forbearance and longsuffering of Yahuah.$n$),
(11010,45906,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The Satan rebuked at the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is the same old serpent who deceiveth the whole world.$n$),
(11010,45907,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The one who first deceived and now seeks to destroy in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is the murderer and liar from the beginning.$n$),
(11010,45909,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 44:4 is this same Logos who was Elohim from the beginning.$n$),
(11009,45910,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* The same flaming cherubic guard set over Eden's way now guards the cave-of-treasures in 1 Adam and Eve 44:2.$n$),
(11009,45911,$n$Exodus 3:2 — *And the angel of Yahuah (LORD) appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.* As the bush burned unconsumed, so the angel keeps the cave unconsumed in the fire of 1 Adam and Eve 44:1.$n$),
(11009,45912,$n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The guarding angel of 1 Adam and Eve 44:2 is one of these ministers of flame, mastering the very fire Satan kindled.$n$),
(11035,45983,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes and speaks to Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 50:7 is this eternal Logos, Elohim Himself, walking with the first man.$n$),
(11034,45987,$n$Genesis 3:7 — *And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.* Standing stained and naked and unable to do the work in 1 Adam and Eve 50:5 reopens the garden's first nakedness, where human handiwork could not truly cover.$n$),
(11033,45991,$n$Psalm 130:1 — *Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O Yahuah (LORD).* Adam and Eve praying through the whole night and begging for mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 50:3 is this very cry de profundis from the first generation outside Eden.$n$),
(11052,46036,$n$Psalm 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The fiery angels coming down to Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 54:10 are the flaming-fire ministers of Yahuah.$n$),
(11052,46037,$n$Hebrews 1:14 — *Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?* The angels glad over Adam's hoped-for return in 1 Adam and Eve 54:11 are ministering spirits sent for the heirs of the promised salvation.$n$),
(11052,46038,$n$Hebrews 1:7 — *And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire.* The cherub of flaming sword and the descending angels of 1 Adam and Eve 54:10 are these flame-of-fire ministers.$n$),
(11051,46039,$n$Matthew 28:4 — *And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men.* The keepers becoming as dead men at the angel is the very terror that lays Adam and Eve as dead in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8.$n$),
(11051,46040,$n$Matthew 28:2 — *And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of Yahuah (Lord) descended from heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.* The heavens and earth shaking with the descending cherubim in 1 Adam and Eve 54:9 answers the earthquake and the descending angel at the tomb.$n$),
(11051,46041,$n$Daniel 10:9 — *Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground.* Daniel face-down and strengthless mirrors Adam and Eve fallen on their faces as dead in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8.$n$),
(11051,46042,$n$Revelation 1:17 — *And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:* Adam and Eve falling as dead before the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 54:8 is the same collapse of flesh before glory that fells John.$n$),
(11050,46043,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The enmity the stayed sword preserves in 1 Adam and Eve 54:5 ends with Satan crushed under the seed it kept alive.$n$),
(11050,46044,$n$Psalm 103:13 — *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him.* The favor the cherub perceives toward Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 54:6 is the Father's pity on His dust-made children.$n$),
(11050,46045,$n$Lamentations 3:22 — *It is of the LORD'S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.* The cherub's wonder that Elohim is favorable in 1 Adam and Eve 54:6 is exactly the un-consuming mercy of Yahuah.$n$),
(11050,46046,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The flame that will not flash forth in 1 Adam and Eve 54:5 is the first mercy that keeps the seed of the woman alive against the serpent.$n$),
(11049,46047,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The gate barred by the cherub in 1 Adam and Eve 54:4 is the same way to the tree of life the Lamb opens at the end to the keepers of the commandments.$n$),
(11049,46050,$n$Genesis 3:23 — *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.* The sending-forth is why Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 54:2 can only walk the outside border of the garden they once kept.$n$),
(11049,46051,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* This is the original of the cherub and flaming sword that meet Adam at the eastern gate in 1 Adam and Eve 54:3-4.$n$),
(11072,46113,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Yahuah's patience that keeps Adam and Eve alive through the forty days in 1 Adam and Eve 59:10 is the mercy preserving the very seed that will bruise the serpent's head.$n$),
(11072,46114,$n$Genesis 3:9 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) called unto Adam, and said unto him, Where art thou?* The Yahuah whom Adam cries to for deliverance in 1 Adam and Eve 59:8 is the same who first sought fallen Adam in mercy rather than wrath.$n$),
(11072,46115,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* Adam's cry to be delivered out of Satan's hands in 1 Adam and Eve 59:8 looks ahead to the Elohim of peace crushing that same adversary under the seed's feet.$n$),
(11071,46116,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The deceiver whose hollow promise is unmasked in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6 is the same liar whose deceit leads the whole earth astray into corruption.$n$),
(11071,46118,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The undelivered 'gift he promised' in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6 proves him the liar he was from the beginning.$n$),
(11071,46119,$n$Genesis 3:5 — *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* The 'divinity' Satan said he would give, named in 1 Adam and Eve 59:6, is the very 'ye shall be as gods' lie by which he first deceived them.$n$),
(11070,46120,$n$Luke 22:43 — *And there appeared an angel unto him from heaven, strengthening him.* As Adam is raised and told 'Be strong' after Satan's assault in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4, so the Messiah was strengthened from heaven in His own agony.$n$),
(11070,46121,$n$Hebrews 1:1 — *Elohim (God), who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,* The Word speaking to father Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is the first of those many manners in which Elohim spoke to the fathers.$n$),
(11070,46122,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The Word who comforts Adam in the cave in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is the One who would Himself be made flesh to save the seed.$n$),
(11070,46123,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The 'Word of Elohim' who comes and raises Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 59:4 is this same eternal Word, the Logos who is Elohim.$n$),
(11069,46124,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The 'hater of all good' who calls his hosts in 1 Adam and Eve 59:1 is this same old serpent who deceiveth the whole world.$n$),
(11069,46125,$n$Job 2:7 — *So went Satan forth from the presence of Yahuah (LORD), and smote Job with sore boils from the sole of his foot unto his crown.* As Satan smote righteous Job in his flesh, so he beats the praying Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 — the adversary permitted to afflict the body, never the covenant.$n$),
(11069,46126,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* The hosts that came into the cave to leave Adam and Eve for dead in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 are this same devouring adversary at his ancient work.$n$),
(11069,46127,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's beating of Adam and Eve in 1 Adam and Eve 59:3 is the serpent striking at the woman's seed under the enmity Yahuah decreed.$n$),
(11079,46140,$n$Matthew 4:11 — *Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.* Adam and Eve, fasting and weak, appealing to Elohim to satisfy their hunger in 1 Adam and Eve 61:16, foreshadow the wilderness fast where, the tempter gone, ministry comes.$n$),
(11079,46141,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* The same Word who comes to feed Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 61:18 would in time be made flesh and dwell among us, full of grace and truth.$n$),
(11079,46142,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word of Elohim who comes again and speaks in 1 Adam and Eve 61:18 is the eternal Logos who was in the beginning.$n$),
(11078,46144,$n$Jubilees 10:11 — *And we did according to all His words: all the malignant evil ones we bound in the place of condemnation, and a tenth part of them we left that they might be subject before Satan on the earth.* The mercy that *did not allow him to destroy you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:10 belongs to the same restraint by which the evil ones are bound and only a remnant left to Satan.$n$),
(11078,46145,$n$James 4:7 — *Submit yourselves therefore to Elohim (God). Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.* Yahuah driving the deceiver away in His mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 61:10 is the pattern of the adversary fleeing before submission to Elohim.$n$),
(11077,46146,$n$Revelation 12:9 — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* The disguised deceiver of 1 Adam and Eve 61:9 is the old serpent who deceives the whole world, his deceit unchanged from the first days.$n$),
(11077,46147,$n$1 Peter 5:8 — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* Satan seeking *to drive you to some place where he might destroy you* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:7 is the prowling adversary hunting whom he may devour.$n$),
(11077,46148,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* The lying messenger of 1 Adam and Eve 61:5, claiming to come from Elohim, is the liar and father of lies from the beginning.$n$),
(11077,46149,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* Satan coming *with a face like your own* and false tokens in 1 Adam and Eve 61:9 is the same transforming deceiver Paul warns of.$n$),
(11076,46151,$n$Romans 16:20 — *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* The driving-away of Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3 is the first installment of the bruising sworn from Eden and finished at the feet of the saints.$n$),
(11076,46152,$n$Genesis 3:14 — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:* The same Yahuah who first cursed the serpent in the garden curses him again in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3, driving him from Adam.$n$),
(11076,46153,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The Word's cursing of Satan in 1 Adam and Eve 61:3 is the very enmity of Eden, the seed-war still striking at the woman's line outside the garden.$n$),
(11103,46227,$n$Jubilees 3:27 — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* The primeval altar-offering of 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the same scene Jubilees records — Adam offering a sweet savour outside the garden.$n$),
(11103,46228,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake...* The offering Adam raises on the altar in 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the sweet savour Yahuah receives, as later from Noah after the flood.$n$),
(11103,46229,$n$Genesis 4:26 — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* The prayer and plea for mercy in 1 Adam and Eve 68:11 is the calling on the Name that the seed of Seth carries forward.$n$),
(11103,46230,$n$Genesis 4:4 — *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering:* Adam's offering on the mountain in 1 Adam and Eve 68:10 is the same accepted way of approach his son Abel keeps.$n$),
(11102,46231,$n$1 Peter 1:20 — *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* The sufferings determined 'beforehand' on Adam's days in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 belong to the Lamb foreordained before the foundation of the world.$n$),
(11102,46232,$n$Galatians 4:4 — *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* The Word who says He will be 'made flesh' to suffer in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 comes in the fulness of time, sent forth and made of a woman.$n$),
(11102,46233,$n$Mark 16:9 — *Now when Yahusha (Jesus) was risen early the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom he had cast seven devils.* The Word's promise to 'create joy' by rising on the first day in 1 Adam and Eve 68:23 is fulfilled when the Messiah rises early on the first day of the week.$n$),
(11102,46234,$n$John 19:31 — *The Yahudim (Jews) therefore, because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day, (for that sabbath day was an high day,) besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, and that they might be taken away.* The preparation-day suffering and the sabbath of 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 align exactly with the cross and the high sabbath.$n$),
(11102,46235,$n$John 19:14 — *And it was the preparation of the passover, and about the sixth hour: and he saith unto the Yahudim (Jews), Behold your King!* The 'preparation day Friday' of suffering foretold in 1 Adam and Eve 68:22 is the very preparation on which the King is delivered up.$n$),
(11101,46236,$n$Exodus 16:31 — *And the house of Yashar'el (Israel) called the name thereof Manna: and it was like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it was like wafers made with honey.* The manna on the tree in 1 Adam and Eve 68:8 bears the same heaven-given name later called Manna by the house of Yashar'el.$n$),
(11101,46237,$n$Exodus 16:4 — *Then said Yahuah (LORD) unto Moses, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.* The solid manna Adam and Eve find in 1 Adam and Eve 68:8 prefigures the bread from heaven Yahuah rains on Yashar'el in the wilderness.$n$),
(11101,46240,$n$John 6:51 — *I am the living bread which came down from heaven: if any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever: and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world.* The Word's promise to make the offering His flesh in 1 Adam and Eve 68:12 is the living bread He proclaims in the flesh.$n$),
(11100,46241,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* Satan's assault on Adam in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman; the enmity of Eden is already at work.$n$),
(11100,46242,$n$2 Corinthians 11:14 — *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* The false promises exposed in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 are the deceiver's trade, the same transforming guile Paul warns of.$n$),
(11100,46243,$n$John 8:44 — *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* Yahuah unmasks Satan's trickery in 1 Adam and Eve 68:5 with the very charge the Messiah lays against him — a liar from the beginning.$n$),
(11100,46244,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* The Word who restores life in 1 Adam and Eve 68:2 is the Maker of all, able to raise what He first formed.$n$),
(11100,46245,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The Word who raises Adam and Eve from death in 1 Adam and Eve 68:2 is the same Logos who was with Elohim in the beginning.$n$),
(11128,46321,$n$Jubilees 3:27 — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* The parallel record shows Adam already an offerer from the day he left Eden, the same priestly hand that offers for the children at 1 Adam and Eve 74:9.$n$),
(11128,46322,$n$Genesis 4:3 — *And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* The offering Adam makes for his children at 1 Adam and Eve 74:9 is the same altar-practice his children will keep, the way kept before Sinai.$n$),
(11127,46323,$n$Hebrews 11:4 — *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, Elohim (God) testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.* Against Cain the hater stands the righteous offerer, the parting of the two lines latent in the children of 1 Adam and Eve 74:6-8.$n$),
(11127,46324,$n$Jude 1:11 — *Woe unto them! for they have gone in the way of Cain, and ran greedily after the error of Balaam for reward, and perished in the gainsaying of Core.* Jude makes Cain a whole "way" — a lineage of works — which the womb-hatred named at 1 Adam and Eve 74:7 begins.$n$),
(11126,46325,$n$Jubilees 4:1 — *And in the third week in the second jubilee she gave birth to Cain, and in the fourth she gave birth to Abel, and in the fifth she gave birth to her daughter 'Âwân.* The parallel primeval record keeps the same sequence — Cain first, then a daughter — matching the first-born son and daughter of 1 Adam and Eve 74:5.$n$),
(11126,46326,$n$1 John 3:12 — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* John names the line Cain belongs to, confirming the hatred that 1 Adam and Eve 74:7 traces back to the womb.$n$),
(11126,46327,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The enmity decreed at Eden's gate already burns in the womb when Cain hates his sister before birth at 1 Adam and Eve 74:7.$n$),
(11125,46328,$n$Genesis 4:1 — *And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bare Cain, and said, I have gotten a man from Yahuah (LORD).* The brief Genesis notice of the first conception is unfolded here into Adam's prayer and Eve's deliverance at 1 Adam and Eve 74:4-5.$n$),
(11125,46329,$n$Genesis 3:16 — *Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.* The narrator names this very sentence as the word being fulfilled in Eve's hard labour at 1 Adam and Eve 74:3.$n$),
(10997,45866,$n$Jubilees 3:11 — *And when she had completed these eighty days we brought her into the Garden of Eden, for it is holier than all the earth besides, and every tree that is planted in it is holy.* The garden Adam now prays toward in 1 Adam and Eve 41:5 is, by Jubilees' witness, the holiest ground on earth — and he is shut outside it.$n$),
(11011,45902,$n$Jubilees 10:8 — *And the chief of the spirits, Mastêmâ, came and said: “Yahuah (God), Creator, let some of them remain before me, and let them hearken to my voice, and do all that I shall say to them; for if some of them are not left to me, I shall not be able to execute the power of my will on the sons of men; for these are for corruption and leading astray before my judgment, for great is the wickedness of the sons of men.” And He said: “Let the tenth part of them remain before him, and let nine parts descend into the place of condemnation.”* The same divine patience that leaves the enemy his hosts "until the end of the world" in 1 Adam and Eve 44:5 lets a remnant of Mastema's spirits remain in Noah's day.$n$),
(11076,46143,$n$1 John 3:8 — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* Calling Satan *the father of evil arts* in 1 Adam and Eve 61:7 names the one who sins from the beginning, whose works the manifested Son undoes.$n$);
INSERT INTO _s463eas VALUES
(10868,$n$Yahuah closes by declaring His own heart toward the seed He made: *For I am Elohim (God) the Creator, who, when I created My creatures, did not intend to destroy them. But after they had sorely roused My anger, I punished them with grievous plagues, until they repent. But, if on the contrary, they still continue hardened in their transgression, they shall be under a curse forever* (1 Adam and Eve 6:9-10). This is the bruising-of-the-serpent mercy promised in the garden — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — the very head Yahuah will crush under the feet of His people: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). The Son was *manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The chastening that aims at repentance, not destruction — it ain't new; it is covenant mercy keeping the seed from the first day outside Eden.$n$,$n$Yahuah closes by declaring His own heart toward the seed He made: *For I am Elohim (God) the Creator, who, when I created My creatures, did not intend to destroy them. But after they had sorely roused My anger, I punished them with grievous plagues, until they repent. But, if on the contrary, they still continue hardened in their transgression, they shall be under a curse forever* (1 Adam and Eve 6:9–10). This is the mercy promised in the garden, where the serpent's head is to be bruised — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — the very head Yahuah will crush under the feet of His people: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). The Son was *revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The chastening that aims at repentance, not destruction — it ain't new; it is covenant mercy keeping the seed from the first day outside Eden.$n$),
(10919,$n$*Then Adam and Eve worshipped before Elohim (God) and gave Him thanks, and praised Him for having delivered them from death.* (1 Adam & Eve 20:3). This is the worship of the righteous who cry and are heard — *The righteous cry, and Yahuah (LORD) heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.* (Psalm 34:17) — *Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but Yahuah (LORD) delivereth him out of them all.* (Psalm 34:19). The deliverance from death they praise is the very work the Son was sent to finish against the murderer-from-the-beginning — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him.* (John 8:44).$n$,$n$*Then Adam and Eve worshipped before Elohim (God) and gave Him thanks, and praised Him for having delivered them from death.* (1 Adam and Eve 20:3). This is the worship of the righteous who cry and are heard — *The righteous cry, and Yahuah (LORD) heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.* (Psalm 34:17) — *Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but Yahuah (LORD) delivereth him out of them all.* (Psalm 34:19). The deliverance from death they praise is the very work the Son was sent to finish against the one who was a murderer from the beginning — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him.* (John 8:44).$n$),
(10946,$n$Yahuah answers Adam's prayer with a true messenger who unmasks the lie and names the war from its first day: *This is Satan and his hosts; he wishes to deceive you as he deceived you at first. For the first time, he was hidden in the serpent; but this time he is come to you in the likeness of an angel of light.* (1 Adam and Eve 27:12) The serpent of the first deception is the very enmity Yahuah decreed — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) John names the deceiver-from-the-beginning plainly — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth* (John 8:44) — and the Revelation seals the identity across the ages — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world.* (Revelation 12:9) For this the Son was manifested — *that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8)$n$,$n$Yahuah answers Adam's prayer with a true messenger who unmasks the lie and names the war from its first day: *This is Satan and his hosts; he wishes to deceive you as he deceived you at first. For the first time, he was hidden in the serpent; but this time he is come to you in the likeness of an angel of light.* (1 Adam and Eve 27:12) The serpent of the first deception is the very enmity Yahuah decreed — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) John names that same enemy plainly — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth* (John 8:44) — and the Revelation seals the identity across the ages — *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world.* (Revelation 12:9) For this the Son was manifested — *to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8)$n$),
(10989,$n$The whole comfort hangs on a span of time — *"only when the 5500 years are fulfilled"* (1-adam-eve 38:2) — and the days of the fall are weighed against it: *"these forty-three days cannot make amends for the hour in which you transgressed My commandment"* (1-adam-eve 38:3). The reckoning is the day-for-a-thousand-years measure of the heavens, for *"one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day"* (2 Peter 3:8). The book of Jubilees reads Adam's own death by that same measure: *"one thousand years are as one day in the testimony of the heavens and therefore was it written concerning the tree of knowledge"* (Jubilees 4:30). It ain't new — the 5500-year prophecy of the incarnation is the primeval church's count of the Day toward which all the fathers waited.$n$,$n$The whole comfort hangs on a span of time — *"only when the 5500 years are fulfilled"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2) — and the days of the fall are weighed against it: *"these forty-three days cannot make amends for the hour in which you transgressed My commandment"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:3). The reckoning is the measure of the heavens, where a day is as a thousand years, for *"one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day"* (2 Peter 3:8). The book of Jubilees reads Adam's own death by that same measure: *"one thousand years are as one day in the testimony of the heavens and therefore was it written concerning the tree of knowledge"* (Jubilees 4:30). It ain't new — the 5500-year prophecy of the incarnation is the count of the Day toward which all the fathers waited.$n$),
(11021,$n$Come and see the coats of skins burned off and the shame of Eden returning. *And Elohim (God) withdrew His Word from them. At this time, the garments that Yahuah (Lord) had given them in Genesis 3:21 were burned off so that Adam and Eve were again naked* (1-adam-eve 46:8). It ain't new: those coats were Yahuah's own first covering — *Unto Adam also and to his wife did Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) make coats of skins, and clothed them* (Genesis 3:21), given the very day they learned the wage of the lie, *in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die* (Genesis 2:17). Satan's fire strips the covering Yahuah gave, leaving them as naked as the day the flaming sword shut the gate (Genesis 3:24) — yet the Word that withdrew is the same Word who had promised to come and save.$n$,$n$Come and see the coats of skins burned off and the shame of Eden returning. Elohim (God) withdrew His Word from them, and *At this time, the garments that Yahuah (Lord) had given them in Genesis 3:21 were burned off so that Adam and Eve were again naked* (1 Adam and Eve 46:8). It ain't new: those coats were Yahuah's own first covering — *Unto Adam also and to his wife did Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) make coats of skins, and clothed them* (Genesis 3:21), given the very day they learned the wage of the lie, *in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die* (Genesis 2:17). Satan's fire strips the covering Yahuah gave, leaving them as naked as the day the flaming sword shut the gate (Genesis 3:24) — yet the Word that withdrew is the same Word who had promised to come and save.$n$),
(11025,$n$Satan gathers his hosts against the man Yahuah made: *"You know that this Adam, whom Elohim (God) created out of the dust, is the one who has taken our kingdom, come, let us gather together and kill him; or hurl a rock at him and at Eve, and crush them under it."* (1 Adam and Eve 48:3) It ain't new — this is the serpent of Eden still striking at the seed of the woman: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) Jubilees tells the same primeval war from the garden — *And Elohim (God) cursed the serpent, and was wroth with it for ever….* (Jubilees 3:21) — and the war ends where it began, under the woman's seed: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20) For this very purpose the Son was manifested against the murderer-from-the-beginning: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8)$n$,$n$Satan gathers his hosts against the man Yahuah made: *"You know that this Adam, whom Elohim (God) created out of the dust, is the one who has taken our kingdom, come, let us gather together and kill him; or hurl a rock at him and at Eve, and crush them under it."* (1 Adam and Eve 48:3) It ain't new — this is the serpent of Eden still striking at the seed of the woman: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) Jubilees tells the same primeval war from the garden — *And Elohim (God) cursed the serpent, and was wroth with it for ever….* (Jubilees 3:21) — and the war ends where it began, under the woman's seed: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20) For this very purpose the Son was manifested against the one who was a murderer from the beginning: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8)$n$),
(11129,$n$Adam builds his altar and Yahuah answers with fire: *And Elohim (God) accepted Adam's offering, and sent a light from heaven that shown on the offering* (1 Adam & Eve 75:3), *And Yahuah (Lord) accepted the offering of Adam and Eve* (75:5). It ain't new — this is the first page of the whole sacrificial witness Genesis records of the same family: *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4). The Spirit names it for what it was, faith: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous* (Hebrews 11:4). And the same sweet-savour mercy that crowned Adam's altar will crown Noah's at the other end of this book: *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)... And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour* (Genesis 8:20-21). The restored Jubilees keeps the memory of the divided answer: *Cain slew Abel because Elohim (God) accepted the sacrifice of Abel, and did not accept the offering of Cain* (Jubilees 4:2).$n$,$n$Adam builds his altar and Yahuah answers with fire: *Then Elohim (God) accepted Adam's offering, and sent a light from heaven that shown on the offering* (1 Adam and Eve 75:3), *And Yahuah (Lord) accepted the offering of Adam and Eve* (1 Adam and Eve 75:5). It ain't new — this is the first page of the whole sacrificial witness Genesis records of the same family: *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4). The Spirit names it for what it was, faith: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous* (Hebrews 11:4). And the same mercy that crowned Adam's altar will crown Noah's at the other end of this book: *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)... And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour* (Genesis 8:20-21). The restored Jubilees keeps the memory of the divided answer: *Cain slew Abel because Elohim (God) accepted the sacrifice of Abel, and did not accept the offering of Cain* (Jubilees 4:2).$n$),
(11132,$n$The children are carried not to their birth-cave but up to the holy place: *they came to the Cave of Treasures, in order that the children should go around in it, and be blessed with the tokens brought from the garden* (1 Adam & Eve 75:6). These tokens kept against the Saviour's coming are the gold, the incense, and the myrrh of the cave, which Yahuah's wise men will one day lay before the child He promised Adam: *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh* (Matthew 2:11). And the household's whole life is a calling on the Name, the way kept from the first generation: *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26).$n$,$n$The children are carried not to the cave where they were born but up to the holy place: *But they returned not to the cave in which they were born; but came to the Cave of Treasures, in order that the children should go around in it, and be blessed with the tokens brought from the garden* (1 Adam and Eve 75:6). These tokens kept against the Saviour's coming are the gold, the incense, and the myrrh of the cave, which Yahuah's wise men will one day lay before the child He promised Adam: *And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh* (Matthew 2:11). And the household's whole life is a calling on the Name, the way kept from the first generation: *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26).$n$),
(11135,$n$Satan comes to the praying Abel disguised, exactly as he comes throughout this book. *While he was praying, Satan appeared to him under the figure of a man, who said to him, "You have frequently moved your father into making offerings, fasting and praying, therefore I will kill you, and make you perish from this world"* (1 Adam and Eve 76:7). Paul names the disguise: *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14); Peter names his hunger: *your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8). But Abel *prayed to Elohim (God), and drove away Satan from him* (1 Adam and Eve 76:8), and the true angel answers the false figure: *Be not afraid of the figure which appeared to you in the night... For, look, Yahuah (Lord) had accepted your prayer* (1 Adam and Eve 76:8). The deceiver from the beginning meets the prayer that resists him. It ain't new.$n$,$n$Satan comes to the praying Abel disguised, exactly as he comes throughout this book. *while he was praying, Satan appeared to him under the figure of a man, who said to him, "You have frequently moved your father into making offerings, fasting and praying, therefore I will kill you, and make you perish from this world"* (1 Adam and Eve 76:7). Paul names the disguise: *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14); Peter names his hunger: *your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8). But Abel *prayed to Elohim (God), and drove away Satan from him* (1 Adam and Eve 76:8), and the true angel answers the false figure: *For, look, Yahuah (Lord) had accepted your prayer. Be not afraid of the figure which appeared to you in the night* (1 Adam and Eve 76:8). The deceiver from the beginning meets the prayer that resists him. It ain't new.$n$),
(11158,$n$Eve and the babe wash for purification while Adam and his daughter wash for their sorrow, and the household returns to offer and to be blessed: *but Eve and the babe washed for purification.* (2 Adam and Eve 2:6) ... *and Elohim (God) accepted their offering, and sent His blessing upon them* (2 Adam and Eve 2:7). The way of cleansing and the calling on the Name is kept from the line of Seth onward — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). Jubilees binds the same: *He began to call on the name of Yahuah (God) on the earth.* (Jubilees 4:12). This is Torah-as-the-way kept before Sinai, the offerings and the Name called upon — never law-as-curse, but the covenant mercy of Yahuah keeping His people from the first generations.$n$,$n$Eve and the babe wash for purification while Adam and his daughter wash for their sorrow, and the household returns to offer and to be blessed: *but Eve and the babe washed for purification.* (2 Adam and Eve 2:6) ... *and Elohim (God) accepted their offering, and sent His blessing upon them* (2 Adam and Eve 2:7). The way of cleansing and the calling on the Name is kept from the line of Seth onward — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). Jubilees binds the same: *He began to call on the name of Yahuah (God) on the earth.* (Jubilees 4:12). This is the Torah kept as the way before Sinai, the offerings and the Name called upon — never the law as a curse, but the covenant mercy of Yahuah keeping His people from the first generations.$n$),
(11171,$n$Satan comes to the holy seed of Seth wearing borrowed beauty, painting "another world" more fair than this: *And Satan said "Yes; behold thou hast heard me; but I will yet praise them and their ways, in thy hearing."* (2 Adam & Eve 6:2), and *"come with me to-day, to our world; where thou shalt see beautiful things and enjoy thyself there"* (2 Adam & Eve 6:7). It ain't new — this is the serpent's first lie wearing fresh paint. *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). Adam himself names the disguise: the account *befell him from Satan, under the form of an angel* (2 Adam & Eve 6:15). The father of it has not changed his trade — *When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44) — the same dragon *which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$,$n$Satan comes to the holy seed of Seth wearing borrowed beauty, painting "another world" more fair than this: *And Satan said "Yes; behold thou hast heard me; but I will yet praise them and their ways, in thy hearing."* (2 Adam and Eve 6:2), and *"come with me to-day, to our world; where thou shalt see beautiful things and enjoy thyself there"* (2 Adam and Eve 6:7). It ain't new — this is the serpent's first lie wearing fresh paint. *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). Seth himself names the disguise: he told them *what had befallen him from Satan, under the form of an angel* (2 Adam and Eve 6:15). The father of it has not changed his trade — *When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44) — the same dragon *which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$),
(11189,$n$To Seth the Word renews the promise made to Adam: *I will send My Word and save thee and thy seed* (2 Adam & Eve 10:3) — the same enmity-and-deliverance set in Eden, *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The sending is appointed to its hour: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law* (Galatians 4:4), the Son *who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you* (1 Peter 1:20). The five-and-a-half days are the appointed clock of that one promise, foreordained before the world and kept down the line of the seed.$n$,$n$To Seth the Word renews the promise made to Adam: *I will send My Word and save thee and thy seed* (2 Adam and Eve 10:3) — the same enmity and deliverance set in Eden, *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The sending is appointed to its hour: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law* (Galatians 4:4), the Son *who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you* (1 Peter 1:20). The five and a half days are the appointed clock of that one promise, foreordained before the world and kept down the line of the seed.$n$),
(11199,$n$Before his death Seth roofs the altar and offers for his children, that the seed be kept: *he took them and offered them upon the altar; and prayed Elohim (God) to accept their offerings, to have mercy on the souls of his children, and to keep them from the hand of Satan.* (2-adam-eve 12:5). The way of acceptable offering was kept from the first generations — *to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26). It is the faith of righteous Abel before him: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous* (Hebrews 11:4). And the prayer "to keep them from the hand of Satan" is answered in the seed-promise itself — *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8); *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$,$n$Before his death Seth roofs the altar and offers for his children, that the seed be kept: *took them and offered them upon the altar; and prayed Elohim (God) to accept their offerings, to have mercy on the souls of his children, and to keep them from the hand of Satan.* (2 Adam and Eve 12:5). The way of acceptable offering was kept from the first generations — *to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26). It is the faith of righteous Abel before him: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous* (Hebrews 11:4). And the prayer "to keep them from the hand of Satan" is answered in the promise of the seed itself — *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8); *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$),
(11200,$n$The covenant blessing passes by hand down the holy generations: Enos, Cainan, Mahalaleel, Jared and Enoch come to receive it, and Seth commits the priesthood and the rule to Enos — *Then Seth blessed Enos, his first - born son, and commanded him habitually to minister in purity before the body of our father Adam... And he commanded him to feed his people in righteousness, in judgment and purity all the days of his life.* (2-adam-eve 12:12); *After the death of Seth, Enos rose at the head of his people, whom he fed in righteousness, and judgment, as his father had commanded him.* (2-adam-eve 12:15). This is the very genealogy of the kept seed in Scripture: *Seth lived an hundred and five years, and begat Enos* (Genesis 5:6); *Enos lived ninety years, and begat Cainan* (Genesis 5:9). It is the line that began to call on the Name — *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26) — and that runs on to the translated Enoch named here at twenty years old.$n$,$n$The covenant blessing passes by hand down the holy generations: Enos, Cainan, Mahalaleel, Jared and Enoch come to receive it, and Seth commits the priesthood and the rule to Enos — *Seth blessed Enos, his first - born son, and commanded him habitually to minister in purity before the body of our father Adam... And he commanded him to feed his people in righteousness, in judgment and purity all the days of his life.* (2 Adam and Eve 12:12); *After the death of Seth, Enos rose at the head of his people, whom he fed in righteousness, and judgment, as his father had commanded him.* (2 Adam and Eve 12:15). This is the very genealogy of the kept seed in Scripture: *Seth lived an hundred and five years, and begat Enos* (Genesis 5:6); *Enos lived ninety years, and begat Cainan* (Genesis 5:9). It is the line that began to call on the Name — *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26) — and that runs on to the translated Enoch named here at twenty years old.$n$),
(11212,$n$Mahalaleel feeds his people *in righteousness and innocence*, watching *that they held no intercourse with the children of Cain* (2 Adam & Eve 16:1), and charges Jared, *not to let one of them go down from this Holy Mountain to the children of Cain, lest he perish with them* (16:5). It ain't new: this is the seed-war drawn between two paternal lines from the very first generations outside the garden. John names the elder line by its father — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous* (1 John 3:12) — and Jude marks the apostate path as *the way of Cain* (Jude 1:11). The whole disaster of Genesis 6 begins here, when the two lines are at last mingled and *the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). The Jubilee record sets the very mingling in Mahalaleel and Jared's own days, when in Jared's days *the angels of Yahuah (God) descended on the earth, those who are named the Watchers* (Jubilees 4:15). This is election and the kept seed, not race; the covenant line guarded down toward Noah.$n$,$n$Mahalaleel feeds his people *in righteousness and innocence*, watching *to see they held no intercourse with the children of Cain* (2 Adam and Eve 16:1), and charges Jared, *not to let one of them go down from this Holy Mountain to the children of Cain, lest he perish with them* (16:5). It ain't new: this is the war between two paternal lines drawn from the very first generations outside the garden. John names the elder line by its father — *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous* (1 John 3:12) — and Jude marks the apostate path as *the way of Cain* (Jude 1:11). The whole disaster of Genesis 6 begins here, when the two lines are at last mingled and *the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). Jubilees sets the very mingling in Mahalaleel and Jared's own days, when in Jared's days *the angels of Yahuah (God) descended on the earth, those who are named the Watchers* (Jubilees 4:15). This is the paternal seed of promise kept apart from the line of Cain, the covenant line guarded down toward Noah.$n$),
(11219,$n$At the fountain by the houses of Cain the trap springs: *every one of Cain's sons brought his wife, and another brought his daughter, and so, many women came to them* (2 Adam and Eve 17:38), and the elder *spread his hands and took one of the women, and five of his companions did the same before Jared, that he should do as they did* (2 Adam and Eve 17:41). But Jared *when he saw them working infamy he wept, and said in his mind, - My fathers never did the like* (2 Adam and Eve 17:42). This is the same going *after strange flesh* (Jude 1:7) that the fair daughters of men provoked: *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). Jared keeps what Paul charges the redeemed to keep: *Know ye not that the unrighteous shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God)? Be not deceived: neither fornicators, nor idolaters, nor adulterers...* (1 Corinthians 6:9).$n$,$n$At the fountain by the houses of Cain the trap springs: *every one of Cain's sons brought his wife, and another brought his daughter, and so, many women came to them* (2 Adam and Eve 17:38), and the elder *spread his hands and took one of the women, and five of his companions did the same before Jared, that he should do as they did* (2 Adam and Eve 17:41). But *when Jared saw them working infamy he wept, and said in his mind, - My fathers never did the like* (2 Adam and Eve 17:42). This is the same going *after strange flesh* (Jude 1:7) that the fair daughters of men provoked: *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). Jared keeps what Paul charges the redeemed to keep: *Know ye not that the unrighteous shall not inherit the kingdom of Elohim (God)? Be not deceived: neither fornicators, nor idolaters, nor adulterers...* (1 Corinthians 6:9).$n$),
(11223,$n$Adam's own voice breaks from the bodies and lays down the way kept before Sinai: *"O Jared, my son, offer gifts to Elohim for having delivered thee from the hand of Satan... offerest them on the altar on which I did offer. Then also, beware of Satan; for he deluded me many a time with his apparitions, wishing to destroy me, but Elohim delivered me out of his hand."* (2 Adam & Eve 18:10). This is the worship of the seed from the first day outside the garden — *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah.* (Genesis 4:26). It is the altar Noah will keep — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah; and took of every clean beast... and offered burnt offerings on the altar.* (Genesis 8:20) — and the deliverance is the promise of Eden itself: *And the Elohim of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20). The enemy's *apparitions* are the serpent's old enmity (Genesis 3:15), and Yahuah's hand still parts the seed from the deceiver.$n$,$n$Adam's own voice breaks from the bodies and lays down the way kept before Sinai: *offer gifts to Elohim (God) for having delivered thee from the hand of Satan; and when thou bringest those offerings, so be it that thou offerest them on the altar on which I did offer. Then also, beware of Satan; for he deluded me many a time with his apparitions, wishing to destroy me, but Elohim (God) delivered me out of his hand* (2 Adam and Eve 18:10). This is the worship of the seed from the first day outside the garden — *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah.* (Genesis 4:26). It is the altar Noah will keep — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah; and took of every clean beast... and offered burnt offerings on the altar.* (Genesis 8:20) — and the deliverance is the promise of Eden itself: *And the Elohim of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20). The enemy's *apparitions* are the serpent's old enmity (Genesis 3:15), and Yahuah's hand still parts the seed from the deceiver.$n$),
(10855,$n$Where the fruit was taken, the promise is renewed; the seed-war and its remedy are bound to the same tree: *But before that, Elohim (God) had made this covenant with our father, Adam, in the same terms, before he came out of the garden, when he was by the tree where Eve took of the fruit and gave it to him to eat.* (1-adam-eve 3:7) — *And as Adam went to it he feared, trembled and fell down; but Elohim (God) in His mercy lifted him up, and then made this covenant with him.* (1-adam-eve 3:9) At that very tree the LORD had already spoken the seed-promise over the serpent: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) — a bruising soon finished: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20) For this the Son was manifested: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) The covenant of mercy is older than the curse is cold.$n$,$n$Where the fruit was taken, the promise is renewed; the seed-war and its remedy are bound to the same tree: *But before that, Elohim (God) had made this covenant with our father, Adam, in the same terms, before he came out of the garden, when he was by the tree where Eve took of the fruit and gave it to him to eat.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:7) — *And as Adam went to it he feared, trembled and fell down; but Elohim (God) in His mercy lifted him up, and then made this covenant with him.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:9) At that very tree the LORD had already spoken the seed-promise over the serpent: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) — a bruising soon finished: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20) For this the Son was manifested: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) The covenant of mercy is older than the curse is cold.$n$),
(10858,$n$Adam looks at his changed body and weeps: *And indeed, when Adam looked at his flesh, that was altered, he cried bitterly* (1 Adam & Eve 4:2); the eyes that once beheld heaven are now mere flesh — *Look at your eyes, and at mine, which before beheld angels praising in heaven... But now we do not see as we did; our eyes have become of flesh; they cannot see like they used to see before.* (1 Adam & Eve 4:8-9). This is the very loss Scripture names: man was *made a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour* (Psalm 8:5), and now *all have sinned, and come short of the glory of Elohim (God)* (Romans 3:23). Yet the seed-promise stands inside the ruin — Yahuah set *enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — and Paul, gazing on the same altered flesh, calls it grace: *But we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the excellency of the power may be of Elohim (God), and not of us.* (2 Corinthians 4:7); *though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day* (2 Corinthians 4:16). The body Adam mourns is the vessel mercy will yet fill.$n$,$n$Adam looks at his changed body and weeps: *And indeed, when Adam looked at his flesh, that was altered, he cried bitterly* (1 Adam & Eve 4:2); the eyes that once beheld heaven are now mere flesh — *Look at your eyes, and at mine, which before beheld angels praising in heaven... But now we do not see as we did; our eyes have become of flesh; they cannot see like they used to see before.* (1 Adam & Eve 4:8-9). This is the very loss Scripture names: of man it is said, *made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour* (Psalm 8:5), and now *all have sinned, and come short of the glory of Elohim (God)* (Romans 3:23). Yet the seed-promise stands inside the ruin — Yahuah set *enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — and Paul, gazing on the same altered flesh, calls it grace: *But we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the excellency of the power may be of Elohim (God), and not of us.* (2 Corinthians 4:7); *though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day* (2 Corinthians 4:16). The body Adam mourns is the vessel mercy will yet fill.$n$),
(10859,$n$Adam names the cave their place of exile: *Look at this cave that is to be our prison in this world, and a place of punishment!* (1 Adam & Eve 4:3), and recoils from the dark rock — *What is the gloom of this cavern, compared with the light of the garden?* (1 Adam & Eve 4:5). The first family becomes the first sojourners on a ground from which dust returns to dust — *for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return* (Genesis 3:19) — and the whole faithful line after them will *confess that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth* (Hebrews 11:13), people who *desire a better country, that is, an heavenly: wherefore Elohim (God) is not ashamed to be called their Elohim (God): for he hath prepared for them a city* (Hebrews 11:16). The groaning Adam feels in the cave Paul names exactly: *For we that are in this tabernacle do groan, being burdened... that mortality might be swallowed up of life* (2 Corinthians 5:4). It ain't new — the prison-cave is the first chapter of the long pilgrimage home.$n$,$n$Adam names the cave their place of exile: *Look at this cave that is to be our prison in this world, and a place of punishment!* (1 Adam & Eve 4:3), and recoils from the dark rock — *What is the gloom of this cavern, compared with the light of the garden?* (1 Adam & Eve 4:5). The first family becomes the first sojourners on a ground from which dust returns to dust — *for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return* (Genesis 3:19) — and the whole faithful line after them will confess *that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth* (Hebrews 11:13), people who *desire a better country, that is, an heavenly: wherefore Elohim (God) is not ashamed to be called their Elohim (God): for he hath prepared for them a city* (Hebrews 11:16). The groaning Adam feels in the cave Paul names exactly: *For we that are in this tabernacle do groan, being burdened... that mortality might be swallowed up of life* (2 Corinthians 5:4). It ain't new — the prison-cave is the first chapter of the long pilgrimage home.$n$),
(10881,$n$Adam and Eve lie in the water at the point of death, and the rescue comes by the Word: *Then Elohim (God) sent His Word to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their death* (1 Adam and Eve 10:3). This is no anonymous power but the same Word the psalmist names over every deliverance from the gates of death — *He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them from their destructions* (Psalm 107:20) — and the same Word that stands over the dry-bones valley, the breath that re-enters the slain that *they may live* (Ezekiel 37:5). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden, life comes only by Yahuah speaking His Word over the dead.$n$,$n$Adam and Eve lie in the water at the point of death, and the rescue comes by the Word: *Then Elohim (God) sent His Word to Adam and Eve, who raised them from their death* (1 Adam and Eve 10:3). This is no anonymous power but the same Word the psalmist names over every deliverance from the gates of death — *He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them from their destructions* (Psalm 107:20) — and the same Word that stands over the dry-bones valley, the breath that re-enters the slain: *I will cause breath to enter into you, and ye shall live* (Ezekiel 37:5). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden, life comes only by Yahuah speaking His Word over the dead.$n$),
(10895,$n$Elohim names the reason He formed Adam and the seed He purposed: *But, O Adam, I have made the day, and have placed the sun in it to give light; in order that you and your children should do your work.* (1 Adam & Eve 13:12) — *For I made you of the light; and I willed to bring out children of light from you and like to you.* (1 Adam & Eve 13:14). This is the Logos's own life, the light of men: *In him was life; and the life was the light of men.* (John 1:4). The apostle declares Adam's race remade into exactly these children of light: *Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness.* (1 Thessalonians 5:5) — *For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in Yahuah (Lord): walk as children of light.* (Ephesians 5:8). The covenant purpose declared over the first man is the very calling kept for the seed of the woman.$n$,$n$Elohim names the reason He formed Adam and the seed He purposed: *But, O Adam, I have made the day, and have placed the sun in it to give light; in order that you and your children should do your work.* (1 Adam & Eve 13:12) — *For I made you of the light; and I willed to bring out children of light from you and like to you.* (1 Adam & Eve 13:14). This is the Logos's own life, the light of men: *In him was life; and the life was the light of men.* (John 1:4). The apostle declares Adam's race remade into exactly these children of light: *Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness.* (1 Thessalonians 5:5) — *For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in Yahusha (Lord): walk as children of light* (Ephesians 5:8). The covenant purpose declared over the first man is the very calling kept for the seed of the woman.$n$),
(10898,$n$Yahuah will not let Adam's self-affliction be mistaken for atonement: *"All this misery that you have been made to take on yourself because of your transgression, will not free you from the hand of Satan, and will not save you. But I will."* (1 Adam and Eve 14:3-4) The seed-war declared in the garden runs through every page of Adam's exile: the serpent strikes, but only the seed of the woman crushes him. *"And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel."* (Genesis 3:15) Adam's penance cannot break Satan's grip; the Son of Elohim alone undoes the devil's work. *"He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil."* (1 John 3:8) And the bruising of the serpent's head is the believer's promised victory. *"And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly."* (Romans 16:20)$n$,$n$Yahuah will not let Adam's self-affliction be mistaken for atonement: *"All this misery that you have been made to take on yourself because of your transgression, will not free you from the hand of Satan, and will not save you. But I will."* (1 Adam and Eve 14:3-4) The seed-war declared in the garden runs through every page of Adam's exile: the serpent strikes, but only the seed of the woman crushes him. *"And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel."* (Genesis 3:15) Adam's penance cannot break Satan's grip; the Son of Elohim alone undoes the devil's work. *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) And the bruising of the serpent's head is the believer's promised victory. *"And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly."* (Romans 16:20)$n$),
(10903,$n$Behind Adam's tears in *Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation* stands the first gospel-word, the seed promise spoken in the garden itself: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The bruised heel is the suffering of the Saviour; its very purpose is the undoing of the serpent — *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). And the price of that salvation is no corruptible thing but blood — *But with the precious blood of Messiah (Christ), as of a lamb without blemish and without spot* (1 Peter 1:19). The suffering Elohim of 1-adam-eve 15:1 is the woman's seed bruising the serpent's head; the seed-war is opened on the first day, and so is the mercy that keeps the seed.$n$,$n$Behind Adam's tears in *Elohim (God) had told them that He should suffer for their salvation* stands the first gospel-word, the seed promise spoken in the garden itself: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The bruised heel is the suffering of the Saviour; its very purpose is the undoing of the serpent — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). And the price of that salvation is no corruptible thing but blood — *But with the precious blood of Messiah (Christ), as of a lamb without blemish and without spot* (1 Peter 1:19). The suffering Elohim of 1 Adam and Eve 15:1 is the woman's seed bruising the serpent's head; the seed-war is opened on the first day, and so is the mercy that keeps the seed.$n$),
(10909,$n$The book is careful to name what the licking beast really is: not a mere snake but the adversary himself — *the serpent that became Satan* (1 Adam and Eve 17:2). From the beginning the seed-war wears the serpent's skin, and the Revelation seals the identification: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). But the enmity laid in the gate already carries the promise of the serpent's undoing: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) — and the Son of Elohim comes for exactly this: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$The book is careful to name what the licking beast really is: not a mere snake but the adversary himself — *the serpent that became Satan* (1 Adam and Eve 17:2). From the beginning the seed-war wears the serpent's skin, and the Revelation seals the identification: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). But the enmity laid in the gate already carries the promise of the serpent's undoing: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) — and the Son of Elohim comes for exactly this: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(10913,$n$Mercy answers the murder: *But Elohim (God) sent an angel who threw the serpent away from them, and raised them up.* Then *the Word of Elohim (God) came to the serpent* and sealed its mouth — *"This time, however, you will be mute, and you and your race will speak no more."* The Word who comes and judges here is the Logos of the prologue — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1); *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). And the silencing of the serpent's speech is the very purpose for which He was manifested: *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The deceiver who once spoke to ruin Yahuah's creatures is now struck mute by the Word he could not overcome.$n$,$n$Mercy answers the murder: *But Elohim (God) sent an angel who threw the serpent away from them, and raised them up.* Then *the Word of Elohim (God) came to the serpent* and sealed its mouth — *"This time, however, you will be mute, and you and your race will speak no more."* The Word who comes and judges here is the Logos of the prologue — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1); *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). And the silencing of the serpent's speech is the very purpose for which He was manifested: *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The deceiver who once spoke to ruin Yahuah's creatures is now struck mute by the Word he could not overcome.$n$),
(10918,$n$Elohim answers the cry: *"From now on, don't be afraid, I will not let it come near you; I have driven it away from you, from this mountain; neither will I leave in it the ability to hurt you."* (1 Adam & Eve 20:2). The Word who guards the holy line on the mountain is the same mercy David sings — *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* (Psalm 91:11) — and *Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet.* (Psalm 91:13). It is Yahuah's own angel that hedges the seed about: *The angel of Yahuah (LORD) encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.* (Psalm 34:7). And the purpose behind the driving-away is the undoing of the serpent altogether — *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Elohim answers the cry: *"From now on, don't be afraid, I will not let it come near you; I have driven it away from you, from this mountain; neither will I leave in it the ability to hurt you."* (1 Adam & Eve 20:2). The Word who guards the holy line on the mountain is the same mercy David sings — *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* (Psalm 91:11) — and *Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet.* (Psalm 91:13). It is Yahuah's own angel that hedges the seed about: *The angel of Yahuah (LORD) encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.* (Psalm 34:7). And the purpose behind the driving-away is the undoing of the serpent altogether — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(10922,$n$Eve names herself the cause: *And she said, "I don't wish to live after him; for all that he did to himself was through me"* (1 Adam and Eve 21:6). Her self-accusation reaches back to the word spoken over the serpent and the woman in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The woman through whom the fall came is the very woman through whom the Bruiser of the serpent's head will come — and the promise of the crushing already stands: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). Satan drives Eve to despair precisely because she carries the seed of his undoing.$n$,$n$Eve names herself the cause: *And she said, "I don't wish to live after him; for all that he did to himself was through me"* (1 Adam and Eve 21:6). Her self-accusation reaches back to the word spoken over the serpent and the woman in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The woman through whom the fall came is the very woman through whom the Bruiser of the serpent's head will come — and the promise of the crushing already stands: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). Satan drives Eve to despair precisely because she carries the seed of his undoing.$n$),
(10926,$n$Adam confesses the root of the fall by name: *And Adam cried and said, "O Yahuah (Lord), do not cut me off for this, neither punish me with heavy plagues, nor yet repay me according to my sin; for we, of our own will, transgressed Your commandment, and ignored Your law, and tried to become gods like you, when Satan the enemy deceived us."* (1 Adam and Eve 22:5). This is the serpent's lie quoted back as confession: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* (Genesis 3:5). It ain't new — and the deceiver is the same liar still: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The Son was manifested for exactly this enemy: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). Adam's *of our own will* throws him on mercy, not law-as-curse, owning the seed-war as begun in his own house.$n$,$n$Adam confesses the root of the fall by name: *And Adam cried and said, "O Yahuah (Lord), do not cut me off for this, neither punish me with heavy plagues, nor yet repay me according to my sin; for we, of our own will, transgressed Your commandment, and ignored Your law, and tried to become gods like you, when Satan the enemy deceived us."* (1 Adam and Eve 22:5). This is the serpent's lie quoted back as confession: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* (Genesis 3:5). It ain't new — and the deceiver is the same liar still: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The Son was manifested for exactly this enemy: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). Adam's *of our own will* throws him on mercy, not law-as-curse, owning the seed-war as begun in his own house.$n$),
(10936,$n$*But Elohim (God) knew that Adam believed he should frequently kill himself and make an offering to Him of his blood... 'O Adam, don't ever kill yourself like this again, by throwing yourself down from that mountain.'* (1 Adam & Eve 25:1-2). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden the enmity declared in Eden is already at work, the serpent driving the man of dust to destroy himself — *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The despair is not Adam's own counsel but the prowling adversary, of whom it is written *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The same Yahuah who promised the bruising of the head will not let the seed-bearer perish: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$,$n$*But Elohim (God) knew that Adam believed he should frequently kill himself and make an offering to Him of his blood... 'O Adam, don't ever kill yourself like this again, by throwing yourself down from that mountain.'* (1 Adam & Eve 25:1-2). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden the enmity declared in Eden is already at work, the serpent driving the man of dust to destroy himself — *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The despair is not Adam's own counsel but the prowling adversary, of whom it is written *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The same Yahuah who promised the bruising of the head will not let the seed-bearer perish: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$),
(10942,$n$The Word's counsel is patience under the night, with light certain to follow: *Yes, rather, bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My covenant is come* (1 Adam & Eve 26:11), *Be patient and enter the cave, for the darkness, of which you were afraid, shall only be twelve hours long; and when ended, light shall come up* (1 Adam & Eve 26:16). The morning is promised after the night: *For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning* (Psalm 30:5); *Verily, verily, I say unto you, That ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice: and ye shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy* (John 16:20). This is the patience the husbandman keeps until the harvest: *Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of Yahuah (Lord). Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain* (James 5:7). So Adam, like Abraham, must endure to obtain the promise: *And so, after he had patiently endured, he obtained the promise* (Hebrews 6:15).$n$,$n$The Word's counsel is patience under the night, with light certain to follow: *Yes, rather, bear long and calm your soul while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My covenant is come* (1 Adam & Eve 26:11), *Be patient and enter the cave, for the darkness, of which you were afraid, shall only be twelve hours long; and when ended, light shall come up* (1 Adam & Eve 26:16). The morning is promised after the night: *For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning* (Psalm 30:5); *Verily, verily, I say unto you, That ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice: and ye shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy* (John 16:20). This is the patience the husbandman keeps until the harvest: *Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of Yahusha (Lord). Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain* (James 5:7). So Adam, like Abraham, must endure to obtain the promise: *And so, after he had patiently endured, he obtained the promise* (Hebrews 6:15).$n$),
(10951,$n$Satan dangles the one thing the exiles long for: *Elohim (God) has sent us to take you and bring you to the border of the garden northwards; to the shore of the clear sea, and bathe you and Eve in it, and raise you to your former gladness, that you return again to the garden* (1-adam-eve 28:5), and *These words sank into the heart of Adam and Eve* (1-adam-eve 28:6). It ain't new — the lie always promises the very blessing it cannot give, just as in Eden: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5). Yet the way back was barred by Yahuah Himself: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life* (Genesis 3:24). No false angel reopens that gate; only the Son destroys the deceiver's work — *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Satan dangles the one thing the exiles long for: *Elohim (God) has sent us to take you and bring you to the border of the garden northwards; to the shore of the clear sea, and bathe you and Eve in it, and raise you to your former gladness, that you return again to the garden* (1 Adam and Eve 28:5), and *These words sank into the heart of Adam and Eve* (1 Adam and Eve 28:6). It ain't new — the lie always promises the very blessing it cannot give, just as in Eden: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5). Yet the way back was barred by Yahuah Himself: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life* (Genesis 3:24). No false angel reopens that gate; only the Son destroys the deceiver's work — *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(10953,$n$When Satan plots Adam's death by his many tricks, *the merciful Elohim (God)... spoke to Satan in a loud voice, and cursed him* (1 Adam & Eve 29:1), and at the rebuke *he and his hosts fled* (29:2). This is no new quarrel — it is the curse first spoken in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The whole life of Adam outside Eden is that enmity playing out, and Yahuah keeps the seed. The apostle hears the same promise rolling forward to its end: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). And the reason the serpent is cursed and his works undone: *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new — the first day outside the garden is already Calvary's eve.$n$,$n$When Satan plots Adam's death by his many tricks, *the merciful Elohim (God)... spoke to Satan in a loud voice, and cursed him* (1 Adam & Eve 29:1), and at the rebuke *he and his hosts fled* (29:2). This is no new quarrel — it is the curse first spoken in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The whole life of Adam outside Eden is that enmity playing out, and Yahuah keeps the seed. The apostle hears the same promise rolling forward to its end: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). And the reason the serpent is cursed and his works undone: *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new — the first day outside the garden is already Calvary's eve.$n$),
(10970,$n$*But Elohim (God) looked at him and at his misery, and at his being about to breathe his last. And the Word of Elohim (God) came from heaven, raised him out of the water...* (1 Adam & Eve 33:12) When grief sinks Adam beneath the water it is the Word of Elohim who comes from heaven to lift him and to expose the deceiver. This is the Logos — the same who comforts Adam in the earlier chapters and foretells His own coming to save him. It ain't new: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us... full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14) The mercy that *raised him out of the water* and let Adam *know it was Satan* (1 Adam & Eve 33:14) is the same purpose for which the Word was manifested: *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) — and the promised crushing draws near: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20)$n$,$n$*But Elohim (God) looked at him and at his misery, and at his being about to breathe his last. And the Word of Elohim (God) came from heaven, raised him out of the water...* (1 Adam & Eve 33:12) When grief sinks Adam beneath the water it is the Word of Elohim who comes from heaven to lift him and to expose the deceiver. This is the Logos — the same who comforts Adam in the earlier chapters and foretells His own coming to save him. It ain't new: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us... full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14) The mercy that *raised him out of the water* and let Adam *know it was Satan* (1 Adam & Eve 33:14) is the same purpose for which the Word was manifested: *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) — and the promised crushing draws near: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.* (Romans 16:20)$n$),
(10971,$n$Adam, lean and parched outside the garden, rehearses his own making before Yahuah: *Then You spread Your hand and created me out of one element, that of dust of the earth; and You brought me into the garden at the third hour, on a Friday, and informed me of it in the cave.* This is the Genesis account told back to its Author — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.* (Genesis 2:7). Sha'ul sees in that first dust-formed man the figure of the One to come: *And so it is written, The first man Adam was made a living soul; the last Adam was made a quickening spirit.* (1 Corinthians 15:45) — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Yahuah (Lord) from heaven.* (1 Corinthians 15:47). The dust that bore the curse waits for the Seed who would raise it. It ain't new.$n$,$n$Adam, lean and parched outside the garden, rehearses his own making before Yahuah: *Then You spread Your hand and created me out of one element, that of dust of the earth; and You brought me into the garden at the third hour, on a Friday, and informed me of it in the cave.* This is the Genesis account told back to its Author — *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.* (Genesis 2:7). Sha'ul sees in that first dust-formed man the figure of the One to come: *And so it is written, The first man Adam was made a living soul; the last Adam was made a quickening spirit.* (1 Corinthians 15:45) — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven.* (1 Corinthians 15:47). The dust that bore the curse waits for the Seed who would raise it. It ain't new.$n$),
(10976,$n$*Then Elohim (God) looked again at Adam and his crying and groaning, and the Word of Elohim (God) came to him, and said to him* (1 Adam and Eve 35:1). From the very first day outside the garden it is the **Word** — the Logos — who comes to Adam, hears his groaning, and speaks. This is no created angel but the One of whom John testifies: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), and *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). The same Word who walked in Eden in the cool of the day — *And they heard the voice of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) walking in the garden in the cool of the day* (Genesis 3:8) — now seeks the fallen man outside it. And the Word that comforts Adam in his exile is the Word that will at last *be made flesh, and dwell among us* (John 1:14) to bear that exile away. It ain't new: the Comforter of Adam is the Saviour of the world.$n$,$n$*Then Elohim (God) looked again at Adam and his crying and groaning, and the Word of Elohim (God) came to him, and said to him* (1 Adam and Eve 35:1). From the very first day outside the garden it is the **Word** — the Logos — who comes to Adam, hears his groaning, and speaks. This is no created angel but the One of whom John testifies: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), and *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). The same Word who walked in Eden in the cool of the day — *And they heard the voice of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) walking in the garden in the cool of the day* (Genesis 3:8) — now seeks the fallen man outside it. And the Word that comforts Adam in his exile is the Word that at last *was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14) to bear that exile away. It ain't new: the Comforter of Adam is the Saviour of the world.$n$),
(10986,$n$Adam does not plead his merit but Yahuah's mercy: *"O Elohim (God), look at us with an eye of pity, and do not avenge us according to our transgression of Your commandment, in Your presence"* (1 Adam & Eve 37:7), *"Make these forty-three days an equivalent for the one hour in which we transgressed"* (1 Adam & Eve 37:10). The Psalm answers him in the same tongue: *He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities* (Psalm 103:10), *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him* (Psalm 103:13). And the eye of pity is not bare clemency but the seed-promise already moving against the serpent — the whole purpose of the war this book unfolds: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The mercy Adam asks on the forty-third day is the mercy that will crush the head of the one who stripped him.$n$,$n$Adam does not plead his merit but Yahuah's mercy: *"O Elohim (God), look at us with an eye of pity, and do not avenge us according to our transgression of Your commandment, in Your presence"* (1 Adam & Eve 37:7), *"Make these forty-three days an equivalent for the one hour in which we transgressed"* (1 Adam & Eve 37:10). The Psalm answers him in the same tongue: *He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities* (Psalm 103:10), *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him* (Psalm 103:13). And the eye of pity is not bare clemency but the seed-promise already moving against the serpent — the whole purpose of the war this book unfolds: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The mercy Adam asks on the forty-third day is the mercy that will crush the head of the one who stripped him.$n$),
(11006,$n$Adam dreads exile unto extinction: *O Eve, if Elohim (God) will bring us into a strange land other than this, in which we find consolation, it must be to put our souls to death, and blot out our name from the face of the earth* (1 Adam and Eve 43:10). This is the serpent's whole strategy laid bare — to end the line before the Promised Seed can come. Yet the sentence in Eden already named the war and its outcome: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The head Satan strikes at is the woman's seed, and the crushing is promised: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Son comes: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The name shall not be blotted out, for the seed is kept.$n$,$n$Adam dreads exile unto extinction: *O Eve, if Elohim (God) will bring us into a strange land other than this, in which we find consolation, it must be to put our souls to death, and blot out our name from the face of the earth* (1 Adam and Eve 43:10). This is the serpent's whole strategy laid bare — to end the line before the Promised Seed can come. Yet the sentence in Eden already named the war and its outcome: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The head Satan strikes at is the woman's seed, and the crushing is promised: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Son comes: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The name shall not be blotted out, for the seed is kept.$n$),
(11011,$n$Even the rebuke of Satan is held back by mercy: *Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world.* (1-adam-eve 44:5) — the longsuffering that delays judgment is the riches of Yahuah's goodness: *Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of Elohim (God) leadeth thee to repentance?* (Romans 2:4). The promise He withholds judgment to keep: *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.* (2 Peter 3:9). Yet the appointed undoing is sure, for the Son was manifested to end the enemy's works: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). The same patience-then-judgment over Mastema's hosts is told from the days of Noah: *And the chief of the spirits, Mastêmâ, came and said... "Let the tenth part of them remain before him, and let nine parts descend into the place of condemnation."* (Jubilees 10:8).$n$,$n$Even the rebuke of Satan is held back by mercy: *Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world.* (1 Adam and Eve 44:5) — the longsuffering that delays judgment is the riches of Yahuah's goodness: *Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of Elohim (God) leadeth thee to repentance?* (Romans 2:4). The promise He withholds judgment to keep: *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.* (2 Peter 3:9). Yet the appointed undoing is sure, for the Son was manifested to end the enemy's works: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). The same patience-then-judgment over Mastema's hosts is told from the days of Noah: *And the chief of the spirits, Mastêmâ, came and said... "Let the tenth part of them remain before him, and let nine parts descend into the place of condemnation."* (Jubilees 10:8).$n$),
(11015,$n$The Word warns Adam that Satan's fire is not for him alone: *"know that it will encompass about both you and your descendants, when you obey his command; that he will plague you with fire; and that you will go down into hell after you are dead"* (1-adam-eve 45:9). This is the enmity declared at the gate of Eden — Satan striking at the seed of the woman down all the generations. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The bruising of the serpent's head is the very deliverance Yahuah promises Adam here: *the Elohim of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). And the Son was manifested for exactly this end: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$The Word warns Adam that Satan's fire is not for him alone: *"know that it will encompass about both you and your descendants, when you obey his command; that he will plague you with fire; and that you will go down into hell after you are dead"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:9). This is the enmity declared at the gate of Eden — Satan striking at the seed of the woman down all the generations. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The bruising of the serpent's head is the very deliverance Yahuah promises Adam here: *the Elohim of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). And the Son was manifested for exactly this end: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11023,$n$Driven from the cave by the fire, Adam and Eve go to their accustomed place and do what the holy seed does — they pray: *And they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain.* (1 Adam and Eve 47:6). The repentant calling on the Name is the Torah-way kept long before Sinai; it begins in Seth's line in the very next generation — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). It is mercy, not law-as-curse — the confidence that Elohim hears the contrite and pardons sin — *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Driven from the cave by the fire, Adam and Eve go to their accustomed place and do what the holy seed does — they pray: *And they stood and prayed Elohim (God) to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain.* (1 Adam and Eve 47:6). The repentant calling on the Name is the Torah-way kept long before Sinai; it begins in Seth's line in the very next generation — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26). It is mercy, not law-as-curse — the confidence that Elohim hears the contrite and pardons sin — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11029,$n$The Word strips the disguise from the tempter: *It came from Satan, who had promised you the Godhead and majesty* (1 Adam and Eve 49:6). The serpent who whispered *ye shall be as gods* still trades in the same counterfeit majesty, for *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). His promises are murder dressed as glory, the lie of *a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44) — yet the Son of Elohim was manifested for precisely this end: *that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The false godhead he offered Adam is undone by the true Word who now stands speaking mercy over him.$n$,$n$The Word strips the disguise from the tempter: *It came from Satan, who had promised you the Godhead and majesty* (1 Adam and Eve 49:6). The serpent who whispered *ye shall be as gods* still trades in the same counterfeit majesty, for *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). His promises are murder dressed as glory, the lie of *a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44) — yet the Son of Elohim was manifested for precisely this end: *to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The false godhead he offered Adam is undone by the true Word who now stands speaking mercy over him.$n$),
(11031,$n$The rock of death gives way to resurrection and the promise of the seed redeemed: *But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam, and to your descendants, to believe in Me* (1 Adam and Eve 49:9). The gospel is preached to the first man on the first days outside Eden — it ain't new. Paul delivers the same as first of all: *how that Messiah (Christ) died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures* (1 Corinthians 15:3-4), the risen one become *the firstfruits of them that slept* (1 Corinthians 15:20). At the empty rock the angel proclaims it: *He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where Yahuah (Lord) lay* (Matthew 28:6). The third-day rising promised over Adam is salvation reaching back to cover the very father of the seed.$n$,$n$The rock of death gives way to resurrection and the promise of the seed redeemed: *But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be salvation to you, O Adam, and to your descendants, to believe in Me* (1 Adam and Eve 49:9). The gospel is preached to the first man on the first days outside Eden — it ain't new. Paul delivers the same as first of all: *how that Messiah (Christ) died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures* (1 Corinthians 15:3-4), the risen one become *the firstfruits of them that slept* (1 Corinthians 15:20). At the empty rock the angel proclaims it: *He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where Yahusha (Lord) lay* (Matthew 28:6). The third-day rising promised over Adam is salvation reaching back to cover the very father of the seed.$n$),
(11037,$n$The Word names the adversary to his victims: *This is he who was hidden in the serpent, and who deceived you, and stripped you of the garment of light and glory in which you were.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:5) — *This is he who promised you majesty and divinity.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:6). It ain't new: this is the seed-war of Eden carried outside the garden. The serpent who hid himself is unmasked in Revelation as *that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9); he is the one of whom Yahusha said *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him* (John 8:44). His false promise of *majesty and divinity* is the same lie Paul warned of: *as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ)* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the Son was manifested for just this: *that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$The Word names the adversary to his victims: *This is he who was hidden in the serpent, and who deceived you, and stripped you of the garment of light and glory in which you were.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:5) — *This is he who promised you majesty and divinity.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:6). It ain't new: this is the seed-war of Eden carried outside the garden. The serpent who hid himself is unmasked in Revelation as *that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9); he is the one of whom Yahusha said *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him* (John 8:44). His false promise of *majesty and divinity* is the same lie Paul warned of: *as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ)* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the Son was manifested for just this: *to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11040,$n$The lesson the Word teaches by binding the enemy: *See, I bound him until you came and saw him and beheld his weakness, that no power is left with him.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:10) — *And Elohim (God) released him from his bonds.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:11). It ain't new: this open shaming of the enemy before the seed prefigures the cross, where the Mighty One *having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it* (Colossians 2:15). For the Son took flesh *that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil* (Hebrews 2:14) — the same purpose for which *the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). From the first days outside Eden, the seed's victory over the bound and powerless adversary was already shown.$n$,$n$The lesson the Word teaches by binding the enemy: *See, I bound him until you came and saw him and beheld his weakness, that no power is left with him.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:10) — *And Elohim (God) released him from his bonds.* (1 Adam and Eve 51:11). It ain't new: this open shaming of the enemy before the seed prefigures the cross, where the Mighty One *having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it* (Colossians 2:15). For the Son took flesh *that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil* (Hebrews 2:14) — the same purpose for which *the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). From the first days outside Eden, the seed's victory over the bound and powerless adversary was already shown.$n$),
(11046,$n$Adam and Eve cry, and the One who answers is the Word: *Then Adam and Eve cried, and prayed Elohim (God) to deliver them from their paws. Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to them, and drove away the lions from them* (1 Adam & Eve 53:2-3). The Comforter who comes is no mere voice; He is the same Word who was in the beginning — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1) — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3) — and who at the fulness of time would put on flesh: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth* (John 1:14). The Word who drives off the lions on the first day outside Eden is the Son manifested to undo the adversary: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Adam and Eve cry, and the One who answers is the Word: *Then Adam and Eve cried, and prayed Elohim (God) to deliver them from their paws. Then the Word of Elohim (God) came to them, and drove away the lions from them* (1 Adam & Eve 53:2-3). The Comforter who comes is no mere voice; He is the same Word who was in the beginning — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1) — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3) — and who at the fulness of time would put on flesh: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth* (John 1:14). The Word who drives off the lions on the first day outside Eden is the Son manifested to undo the adversary: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11050,$n$The cherub raises the sword to kill — and it will not strike: *But when he raised it over Adam and Eve, the flame of the sword did not flash forth* (1-adam-eve 54:5); *Therefore the cherub thought that Elohim (God) was favorable to them* (1-adam-eve 54:6). The serpent has struck at the seed of the woman from the first day, and from the first day Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed alive — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The withheld flame is the LORD's compassion: *It is of the LORD'S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not* (Lamentations 3:22); *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him. For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* (Psalm 103:13). The same enmity that spares them here ends with the head-blow: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20) — *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new: the stayed sword over the dust-made man already preaches the Saviour who will come and save the seed.$n$,$n$The cherub raises the sword to kill — and it will not strike: *But when he raised it over Adam and Eve, the flame of the sword did not flash forth* (1 Adam and Eve 54:5); *Therefore the cherub thought that Elohim (God) was favorable to them* (1 Adam and Eve 54:6). The serpent has struck at the seed of the woman from the first day, and from the first day Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed alive — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The withheld flame is the LORD's compassion: *It is of the LORD'S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not* (Lamentations 3:22); *Like as a father pitieth his children, so Yahuah (LORD) pitieth them that fear him. For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust* (Psalm 103:13). The same enmity that spares them here ends with the head-blow: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20) — *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new: the stayed sword over the dust-made man already preaches the Saviour who will come and save the seed.$n$),
(11056,$n$Satan's war does not cease at the gate of Eden — it follows the seed: *And he has continued, O Adam, to make war against you, until he tricked you and made you come out of the garden ... because you obeyed him, and trespassed against Elohim (God)* (1 Adam & Eve 55:15). But the angels plead, and mercy holds the line: *and asked Him not to destroy Adam this time ... but to bear with him until the fulfillment of the promise; and to help him in this world until he was free from Satan's hand* (1 Adam & Eve 55:16). This is the enmity first decreed in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The same bruising is pledged to the saints: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), for *the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The promise Adam waits on IS the seed who crushes the serpent's head. It ain't new — the seed-war and the seed-mercy open on the first day outside Eden.$n$,$n$Satan's war does not cease at the gate of Eden — it follows the seed: *And he has continued, O Adam, to make war against you, until he tricked you and made you come out of the garden ... because you obeyed him, and trespassed against Elohim (God)* (1 Adam & Eve 55:15). But the angels plead, and mercy holds the line: *and asked Him not to destroy Adam this time ... but to bear with him until the fulfillment of the promise; and to help him in this world until he was free from Satan's hand* (1 Adam & Eve 55:16). This is the enmity first decreed in the garden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The same bruising is pledged to the saints: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), for *the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The promise Adam waits on IS the seed who crushes the serpent's head. It ain't new — the seed-war and the seed-mercy open on the first day outside Eden.$n$),
(11060,$n$No sooner have the angels gone than the adversary returns disguised: *But after the angels had departed from Adam and Eve, Satan came with shamefacedness, and stood at the entrance of the cave in which were Adam and Eve...* (1 Adam & Eve 56:12), and Adam is taken in — *Then Adam came out of the cave, thinking he was one of Elohim's (God's) angels that was come to give him some good counsel.* (1 Adam & Eve 56:13). It ain't new: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The roaring lion never rests: *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* (1 Peter 5:8). But the seed of the woman comes to undo him: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$No sooner have the angels gone than the adversary returns disguised: *But after the angels had departed from Adam and Eve, Satan came with shamefacedness, and stood at the entrance of the cave in which were Adam and Eve...* (1 Adam & Eve 56:12), and Adam is taken in — *Then Adam came out of the cave, thinking he was one of Elohim's (God's) angels that was come to give him some good counsel.* (1 Adam & Eve 56:13). It ain't new: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The roaring lion never rests: *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:* (1 Peter 5:8). But the seed of the woman comes to undo him: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11063,$n$Satan claims a throne over the man who heeded him: *"But now, O Adam, because you fell you are under my rule, and I am king over you; because you have obeyed me and have transgressed against your Elohim (God). Neither will there be any deliverance from my hands until the day promised you by your Elohim (God)"* (1 Adam and Eve 57:7). This is the iron law of obedience that Sha'ul wrote out: *Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?* (Romans 6:16). Satan's reign is real but temporary — the Messiah called him *the prince of this world* and announced his fall: *Now is the judgment of this world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out* (John 12:31). The promised day Satan dreads is the Seed who comes to overthrow the usurper: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Satan claims a throne over the man who heeded him: *"But now, O Adam, because you fell you are under my rule, and I am king over you; because you have obeyed me and have transgressed against your Elohim (God). Neither will there be any deliverance from my hands until the day promised you by your Elohim (God)"* (1 Adam and Eve 57:7). This is the iron law of obedience that Sha'ul wrote out: *Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?* (Romans 6:16). Satan's reign is real but temporary — the Messiah called him *the prince of this world* and announced his fall: *Now is the judgment of this world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out* (John 12:31). The promised day Satan dreads is the Seed who comes to overthrow the usurper: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11065,$n$Against Satan's boast of kingship, Adam turns the only direction that breaks the enemy — back to his Maker: *"Hear what he said; that he won't fulfil any of what he told you in the garden. Did he really then become king over us? But we will ask Elohim (God), who created us, to deliver us out of his hands"* (1 Adam and Eve 57:11-12). The promised deliverance is no idle hope; it is the gospel from the foundation: *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8), the One who *also himself likewise took part of the same; that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil* (Hebrews 2:14). And the war-wearied saints are given the same word Adam reached for: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). Adam's prayer is the first crying-out of the seed of the woman to the God who keeps His covenant mercy.$n$,$n$Against Satan's boast of kingship, Adam turns the only direction that breaks the enemy — back to his Maker: *"Hear what he said; that he won't fulfil any of what he told you in the garden. Did he really then become king over us? But we will ask Elohim (God), who created us, to deliver us out of his hands"* (1 Adam and Eve 57:11-12). The promised deliverance is no idle hope; it is the gospel from the foundation: *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8), the One who *also himself likewise took part of the same; that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil* (Hebrews 2:14). And the war-wearied saints are given the same word Adam reached for: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). Adam's prayer is the first crying-out of the seed of the woman to the God who keeps His covenant mercy.$n$),
(11071,$n$Yahuah exposes the serpent's lie by its emptiness: *Then Elohim (God) said to him, "O Adam, see, he is lord and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you divinity. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?* (1 Adam and Eve 59:6) The promise of divinity is the very lie of the garden: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* (Genesis 3:5) — first whispered through the serpent's *Ye shall not surely die:* (Genesis 3:4). He is a liar from the start: *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44) — for *he that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning* (1 John 3:8). The same godlessness still spreads from his deceit: *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* (1 Enoch 8:2) It ain't new — the gift the deceiver promised is never delivered.$n$,$n$Yahuah exposes the serpent's lie by its emptiness: *Then Elohim (God) said to him, "O Adam, see, he is lord and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you divinity. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?* (1 Adam and Eve 59:6) The promise of divinity is the very lie of the garden: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.* (Genesis 3:5) — first whispered through the serpent's *Ye shall not surely die:* (Genesis 3:4). He is a liar from the start: *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44) — for *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning* (1 John 3:8). The same godlessness still spreads from his deceit: *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* (1 Enoch 8:2) It ain't new — the gift the deceiver promised is never delivered.$n$),
(11076,$n$When Satan has lured Adam and Eve out of the cave before the forty days are ended, *Then the Word of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them* (1 Adam & Eve 61:3) — and Adam learns the deceiver is *the father of evil arts, who brought you and Eve out of the Garden of Delights* (61:7). It ain't new: this is the very enmity of Eden replayed on the second day outside the gate. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15); the same Yahuah who, in the garden, *said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field* (Genesis 3:14) now curses him again. The seed-war's end is sworn: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$When Satan has lured Adam and Eve out of the cave before the forty days are ended, *Then the Word of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them* (1 Adam & Eve 61:3) — and Adam learns the deceiver is *the father of evil arts, who brought you and Eve out of the Garden of Delights* (61:7). It ain't new: this is the very enmity of Eden replayed on the second day outside the gate. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15); the same Yahuah who, in the garden, *said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field* (Genesis 3:14) now curses him again. The seed-war's end is sworn: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11078,$n$Against the destroyer Yahuah sets His mercy: *But because I am merciful and am favorable to you, I did not allow him to destroy you; instead I drove him away from you* (1 Adam & Eve 61:10). The promise that the head shall be bruised is already mercy in motion. *Submit yourselves therefore to Elohim (God). Resist the devil, and he will flee from you* (James 4:7) — and the binding of the adversary is the same primeval history the watchers' book tells: *And we did according to all His words: all the malignant evil ones we bound in the place of condemnation, and a tenth part of them we left that they might be subject before Satan on the earth* (Jubilees 10:11). For Satan's whole purpose, *to break your mutual bond; to cut off all hope from you* (61:7), is undone because *the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Against the destroyer Yahuah sets His mercy: *But because I am merciful and am favorable to you, I did not allow him to destroy you; instead I drove him away from you* (1 Adam & Eve 61:10). The promise that the head shall be bruised is already mercy in motion. *Submit yourselves therefore to Elohim (God). Resist the devil, and he will flee from you* (James 4:7) — and the binding of the adversary is the same primeval history the watchers' book tells: *And we did according to all His words: all the malignant evil ones we bound in the place of condemnation, and a tenth part of them we left that they might be subject before Satan on the earth* (Jubilees 10:11). For Satan's whole purpose, *to break your mutual bond; to cut off all hope from you* (61:7), is undone because *the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11080,$n$Satan cannot bear the comfort Yahuah gives the first parents, so he moves at once against the seed: *But Satan the wicked was envious, because of the consolation Elohim (God) had given them.* (1 Adam & Eve 62:1) *So he prevented them, and went into the cave and took the two figs, and buried them outside the cave, so that Adam and Eve should not find them. He also had in his thoughts to destroy them.* (1 Adam & Eve 62:2) It ain't new — this is the enmity declared in the garden, the serpent forever striking at the woman's seed: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) The devil has worked thus from the first day outside Eden: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) The same subtilty that beguiled Eve presses on still: *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ).* (2 Corinthians 11:3) And John names the burier of the fruit — *that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$,$n$Satan cannot bear the comfort Yahuah gives the first parents, so he moves at once against the seed: *But Satan the wicked was envious, because of the consolation Elohim (God) had given them.* (1 Adam & Eve 62:1) *So he prevented them, and went into the cave and took the two figs, and buried them outside the cave, so that Adam and Eve should not find them. He also had in his thoughts to destroy them.* (1 Adam & Eve 62:2) It ain't new — this is the enmity declared in the garden, the serpent forever striking at the woman's seed: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15) The devil has worked thus from the first day outside Eden: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8) The same subtilty that beguiled Eve presses on still: *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ).* (2 Corinthians 11:3) And John names the burier of the fruit — *that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$),
(11083,$n$The enemy reaches the cave first and buries the very fruit Adam was sent to fetch: *when I sent you to fetch the figs, Satan went before you to the cave, took the figs, and buried them outside, eastward of the cave, thinking to destroy them; and not sowing them with good intent* (1 Adam & Eve 63:8). It ain't new — this is the serpent striking again at the seed of the woman, and Yahuah turning the malice into mercy: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The devourer prowls the very first day outside Eden — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8) — *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). What Satan buried to destroy, Yahuah raised to overshadow.$n$,$n$The enemy reaches the cave first and buries the very fruit Adam was sent to fetch: *when I sent you to fetch the figs, Satan went before you to the cave, took the figs, and buried them outside, eastward of the cave, thinking to destroy them; and not sowing them with good intent* (1 Adam & Eve 63:8). It ain't new — this is the serpent striking again at the seed of the woman, and Yahuah turning the malice into mercy: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). The devourer prowls the very first day outside Eden — *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8) — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). What Satan buried to destroy, Yahuah raised to overshadow.$n$),
(11089,$n$Outside the garden the very food alters them: *Then Adam and Eve came back into the cave sorrowful and crying because of the alteration of their bodies. And they both knew from that hour that they were altered beings* (1 Adam & Eve 65:7), and Adam confesses *from now on we are earthy and of the dust, and of the inhabitants of the earth* (65:9). It ain't new — this is the very frame Yahuah named at the forming: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul* (Genesis 2:7), the dust to which the curse returns him: *for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return* (Genesis 3:19). Sha'ul carries the same two-Adam pattern — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Yahuah (Lord) from heaven* (1 Corinthians 15:47) — and the whole creation that fell with Adam now *groaneth and travaileth in pain together until now* (Romans 8:22), waiting for the deliverance the cave-dwellers were promised.$n$,$n$Outside the garden the very food alters them: *Then Adam and Eve came back into the cave sorrowful and crying because of the alteration of their bodies. And they both knew from that hour that they were altered beings* (1 Adam & Eve 65:7), and Adam confesses *from now on we are earthy and of the dust, and of the inhabitants of the earth* (65:9). It ain't new — this is the very frame Yahuah named at the forming: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul* (Genesis 2:7), the dust to which the curse returns him: *for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return* (Genesis 3:19). Sha'ul carries the same two-Adam pattern — *The first man is of the earth, earthy: the second man is Adonai (Lord) from heaven* (1 Corinthians 15:47) — and the whole creation that fell with Adam now *groaneth and travaileth in pain together until now* (Romans 8:22), waiting for the deliverance the cave-dwellers were promised.$n$),
(11101,$n$Over Adam's offering of corn the Word speaks the gospel before the garden gate is cold: *I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an altar, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly* (1-adam-eve 68:12). This is the bread of the upper room — *Take, eat; this is my body* (Matthew 26:26) — and the living bread foretold: *I am the living bread which came down from heaven... and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world* (John 6:51). On the field they find *solid manna* (1-adam-eve 68:8), as Yahuah once *raine[d] bread from heaven* (Exodus 16:4) and the house of Yashar'el *called the name thereof Manna* (Exodus 16:31); and the offering *continually on an altar* answers the one offering by which *we are sanctified through the offering of the body of Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) once for all* (Hebrews 10:10). Adam's altar-fire, kept burning, is the figure long before Sinai — *The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out* (Leviticus 6:13).$n$,$n$Over Adam's offering of corn the Word speaks the gospel before the garden gate is cold: *I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an altar, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly* (1 Adam and Eve 68:12). This is the bread of the upper room — *Take, eat; this is my body* (Matthew 26:26) — and the living bread foretold: *I am the living bread which came down from heaven... and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world* (John 6:51). On the field they find *solid manna* (1 Adam and Eve 68:8), as Yahuah once said, *I will rain bread from heaven* (Exodus 16:4) and the house of Yashar'el *called the name thereof Manna* (Exodus 16:31); and the offering *continually on an altar* answers the one offering by which *we are sanctified through the offering of the body of Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) once for all* (Hebrews 10:10). Adam's altar-fire, kept burning, is the figure long before Sinai — *The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out* (Leviticus 6:13).$n$),
(11103,$n$Restored, Adam and Eve build no new way but keep the old one: they *took of the corn, and made of it an offering... on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood* (1-adam-eve 68:10), pleading *accept this offering from us, and don't turn us away, deprived of Your mercy* (1-adam-eve 68:11). This is the way kept before Sinai — Abel who *brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4); the day *men [began] to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26); and Noah who *builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)... and offered burnt offerings* so that *Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour* (Genesis 8:20-21). The witness is one: Jubilees keeps the same scene — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun* (Jubilees 3:27). Adam offers in hope, not law-as-curse, against the day of the Saviour.$n$,$n$Restored, Adam and Eve build no new way but keep the old one: they *took of the corn, and made of it an offering... on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood* (1 Adam and Eve 68:10), pleading *accept this offering from us, and don't turn us away, deprived of Your mercy* (1 Adam and Eve 68:11). This is the way kept before Sinai — Abel who *brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4); the day *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26); and Noah who *builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)... and offered burnt offerings* so that *Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour* (Genesis 8:20-21). The witness is one: Jubilees keeps the same scene — *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun* (Jubilees 3:27). Adam offers in hope, not law-as-curse, against the day of the Saviour.$n$),
(11107,$n$*And Elohim (God) healed Adam in one day, which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day.* (1 Adam and Eve 69:8). The fiftieth day, the morrow after seven sabbaths, is the count of Shavuot, the feast appointed in Torah: *seven sabbaths shall be complete* (Leviticus 23:15) until *ye shall number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meat offering unto Yahuah (LORD)* (Leviticus 23:16). It is this same fiftieth day on which the Spirit was poured: *And when the day of Pentecost was fully come, they were all with one accord in one place* (Acts 2:1). Adam's healing is dated to the appointed time — the moedim are written into the first man's days.$n$,$n$*And Elohim (God) healed Adam in one day, which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day.* (1 Adam and Eve 69:8). The fiftieth day, the morrow after seven sabbaths, is the count of Shavuot, the feast appointed in Torah: *seven sabbaths shall be complete* (Leviticus 23:15) until *shall ye number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meat offering unto Yahuah (LORD)* (Leviticus 23:16). It is this same fiftieth day on which the Spirit was poured: *And when the day of Pentecost was fully come, they were all with one accord in one place* (Acts 2:1). Adam's healing is dated to the appointed time — the moedim are written into the first man's days.$n$),
(11108,$n$The chapter closes with the adversary's next stratagem: *But when there a multitude of beasts came all around them. It was Satan's doing, in his wickedness; in order to wage war against Adam through marriage.* (1 Adam and Eve 69:11). This is the old enmity, the serpent striking at the seed of the woman: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Satan's assault on the covenant line through corrupt union is the same war later seen when *the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). Yet the head-crushing is sure: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$The chapter closes with the adversary's next stratagem: *But when there a multitude of beasts came all around them. It was Satan's doing, in his wickedness; in order to wage war against Adam through marriage.* (1 Adam and Eve 69:11). This is the old enmity, the serpent striking at the seed of the woman: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Satan's assault on the covenant line through corrupt union is the same war later seen when *the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair* (Genesis 6:2). Yet the head-crushing is sure: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20), *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11116,$n$The chapter closes on the war that began at the gate: *But Satan was jealous of them; and planned to destroy them* (1 Adam and Eve 71:14). This is Genesis 3:15 in motion — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — every assault upon Adam and Eve is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman. Wisdom names the motive: *Nevertheless through envy of the devil came death into the world: and they that do hold of his side do find it* (Wisdom of Solomon 2:24). But the head-bruising is sure: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The jealous adversary who plotted by the river will be crushed.$n$,$n$The chapter closes on the war that began at the gate: *But Satan was jealous of them; and planned to destroy them* (1 Adam and Eve 71:14). This is Genesis 3:15 in motion — *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15) — every assault upon Adam and Eve is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman. Wisdom names the motive: *Nevertheless through envy of the devil came death into the world: and they that do hold of his side do find it* (Wisdom of Solomon 2:24). But the head-bruising is sure: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). The jealous adversary who plotted by the river will be crushed.$n$),
(11118,$n$Satan's reasoning lays the plot bare: *Now, then, if I deceive him to do this thing, and to marry Eve without Elohim's (God's) permission, Elohim (God) will kill him then.* (1 Adam and Eve 72:11), *because he sought to kill him, and to make him disappear from off the face of the earth.* (72:12). The whole stratagem is one more blow at the promised Seed — the enmity declared in Eden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The serpent strikes at the heel that he may keep the head from ever coming. Yet the same Word who set the enmity sets the outcome: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20). For this end the Seed Himself appears: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). The murderer who was a murderer from the beginning fails again at the beginning.$n$,$n$Satan's reasoning lays the plot bare: *Now, then, if I deceive him to do this thing, and to marry Eve without Elohim's (God's) permission, Elohim (God) will kill him then.* (1 Adam and Eve 72:11), *because he sought to kill him, and to make him disappear from off the face of the earth.* (72:12). The whole stratagem is one more blow at the promised Seed — the enmity declared in Eden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The serpent strikes at the heel that he may keep the head from ever coming. Yet the same Word who set the enmity sets the outcome: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20). For this end the Seed Himself appears: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8). The murderer who was a murderer from the beginning fails again at the beginning.$n$),
(11124,$n$The chapter closes the long siege: *Thus was Satan's war with Adam defeated* (1 Adam & Eve 73:9). The serpent who struck at the woman and her seed from the first day is overthrown by Yahuah's mercy — the spine of the whole conflict is the seed-promise: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Every assault repelled here is a foretaste of the final crushing: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Word came to Adam, and for this He would come in flesh: *For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new — the war Satan loses at Eve's wedding is the war he loses at the cross.$n$,$n$The chapter closes the long siege: *Thus was Satan's war with Adam defeated* (1 Adam & Eve 73:9). The serpent who struck at the woman and her seed from the first day is overthrown by Yahuah's mercy — the spine of the whole conflict is the seed-promise: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Every assault repelled here is a foretaste of the final crushing: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Word came to Adam, and for this He would come in flesh: *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). It ain't new — the war Satan loses at Eve's wedding is the war he loses at the cross.$n$),
(11159,$n$*As for our father Adam, at the end of seven years from the day he had been severed from his wife Eve, Satan envied him, when he saw him thus separated from her; and strove to make him live with her again* (2 Adam & Eve 3:1) — and the grief of the murdered Abel and the rejoicing over the born Seth (3:8-9) name the war out loud. It ain't new: this is the enmity Yahuah set in the dust at the gate of the garden, *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Every assault on Adam's marriage and seed is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, and the verdict is already written: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Son was manifested — *that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). And the first murder, Abel, is the first casualty of the seed-war the apostle remembers — *He was a murderer from the beginning* (John 8:44).$n$,$n$*As for our father Adam, at the end of seven years from the day he had been severed from his wife Eve, Satan envied him, when he saw him thus separated from her; and strove to make him live with her again* (2 Adam & Eve 3:1) — and the grief of the murdered Abel and the rejoicing over the born Seth (3:8-9) name the war out loud. It ain't new: this is the enmity Yahuah set in the dust at the gate of the garden, *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). Every assault on Adam's marriage and seed is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, and the verdict is already written: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20). For this the Son was manifested — *to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8). And the first murder, Abel, is the first casualty of the seed-war the apostle remembers — *He was a murderer from the beginning* (John 8:44).$n$),
(11163,$n$Yahuah strips the disguise off the deceiver and makes Adam look him in the face: *THEN Elohim (God) ordered Satan to show himself to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form.* (2 Adam & Eve 4:1), *And Elohim (God) said to Adam, 'Look at this devil, and at his hideous look, and know that he it is who made thee fall from brightness into darkness, from peace and rest to toil and misery.* (2 Adam & Eve 4:3). It ain't new — this is the old serpent of the garden unmasked. From the first day outside Eden he is named for what he is: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). Messiah declares his nature with the same plainness — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him.* (John 8:44). And the reason the Son of Elohim came is the destruction of this very enemy: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Yahuah strips the disguise off the deceiver and makes Adam look him in the face: *THEN Elohim (God) ordered Satan to show himself to Adam plainly, in his own hideous form.* (2 Adam & Eve 4:1), *And Elohim (God) said to Adam, 'Look at this devil, and at his hideous look, and know that he it is who made thee fall from brightness into darkness, from peace and rest to toil and misery.* (2 Adam & Eve 4:3). It ain't new — this is the old serpent of the garden unmasked. From the first day outside Eden he is named for what he is: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). Messiah declares his nature with the same plainness — *Ye are of your father the devil... He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him.* (John 8:44). And the reason the Son of Elohim came is the destruction of this very enemy: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11169,$n$Satan's offer to Seth recycles the first deception word for word: *thou shalt remain in our world, and rest from this world and the misery of it... thou shalt never bring up an offering, nor sue for mercy; for thou shalt commit no more sin nor be swayed by passions* (2 Adam & Eve 5:9), and the climax — *For in our world we have no Elohim (God); but we all are gods; we all are of the light, heavenly, powerful, strong and glorious* (2 Adam & Eve 5:11). This is the serpent's word in the garden made plain — the promise of godhood without Yahuah, the very voice cursed in Eden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). It ain't new: the deceiver of the whole world is still selling the lie — *and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9). But the Son of Elohim was manifested for this very war — *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Satan's offer to Seth recycles the first deception word for word: *thou shalt remain in our world, and rest from this world and the misery of it... thou shalt never bring up an offering, nor sue for mercy; for thou shalt commit no more sin nor be swayed by passions* (2 Adam & Eve 5:9), and the climax — *For in our world we have no Elohim (God); but we all are gods; we all are of the light, heavenly, powerful, strong and glorious* (2 Adam & Eve 5:11). This is the serpent's word in the garden made plain — the promise of godhood without Yahuah, the very voice cursed in Eden: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15). It ain't new: the deceiver of the whole world is still selling the lie — *and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9). But the Son of Elohim was manifested for this very war — *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11197,$n$Elohim renews to Seth the very promise made to Adam in the cave: *And Elohim (God) accepted his offering, and sent His blessing upon him and upon his children. And then Elohim (God) made a promise to Seth, saying, "At the end of the great five days and a half, concerning which I have made a promise to thee and to thy father, I will send My Word and save thee and thy seed."* (2-adam-eve 12:6). It ain't new — this is the Logos foretold from the second generation outside Eden. The Word who is promised is the same who *was in the beginning... and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), and who *was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14) when *the fulness of the time was come* (Galatians 4:4). And the seed He comes to save is the seed of the woman of the first promise: *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$,$n$Elohim renews to Seth the very promise made to Adam in the cave: *And Elohim (God) accepted his offering, and sent His blessing upon him and upon his children. And then Elohim (God) made a promise to Seth, saying, "At the end of the great five days and a half, concerning which I have made a promise to thee and to thy father, I will send My Word and save thee and thy seed."* (2 Adam and Eve 12:6). It ain't new — this is the Logos foretold from the second generation outside Eden. The Word who is promised is the same Word of whom it is written, *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), and who *was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14) when *the fulness of the time was come* (Galatians 4:4). And the seed He comes to save is the seed of the woman of the first promise: *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$),
(11217,$n$The lie is precise and genealogical: *I am Adam whom Elohim (God) made first; and this is Abel my son, who was killed by his brother Cain... Then this is my son Seth, whom I asked of Yahuah (Lord), who gave him to me, to comfort me instead of Abel* (2 Adam and Eve 17:9-10), and the false elder names the whole line down to *Mahalaleel... thy father* (2 Adam and Eve 17:11). Satan counterfeits the very seed Yahuah is keeping. This is the garden lie wearing new robes — there the serpent said *Ye shall not surely die* (Genesis 3:4) and *ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5); here he raises the dead fathers as bait. But the Son comes precisely to undo this: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$The lie is precise and genealogical: *I am Adam whom Elohim (God) made first; and this is Abel my son, who was killed by his brother Cain... Then this is my son Seth, whom I asked of Yahuah (Lord), who gave him to me, to comfort me instead of Abel* (2 Adam and Eve 17:9-10), and the false elder names the whole line down to *Mahalaleel... thy father* (2 Adam and Eve 17:11). Satan counterfeits the very seed Yahuah is keeping. This is the garden lie wearing new robes — there the serpent said *Ye shall not surely die* (Genesis 3:4) and *ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5); here he raises the dead fathers as bait. But the Son comes precisely to undo this: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11224,$n$Jared offers as Adam commanded, and the Word answers from the altar: *Then Elohim appeared unto Jared on the altar and blessed him and his children, and accepted their offerings; and commanded Jared to take of the sacred fire from the altar, and with it to light the lamp that shed light on the body of Adam.* (2 Adam & Eve 18:13-14). The fire Adam keeps is the fire Torah will guard at Sinai — *The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.* (Leviticus 6:13). The accepted offering is Noah's accepted offering — *And Yahuah smelled a sweet savour... I will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake* (Genesis 8:21). And the Elohim who *appeared* and *blessed* on the altar is the same Word who delivers the seed from the deceiver — *For this purpose the Son of Elohim was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$,$n$Jared offers as Adam commanded, and the Word answers from the altar: *Then Elohim appeared unto Jared on the altar and blessed him and his children, and accepted their offerings; and commanded Jared to take of the sacred fire from the altar, and with it to light the lamp that shed light on the body of Adam.* (2 Adam & Eve 18:13-14). The fire Adam keeps is the fire Torah will guard at Sinai — *The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.* (Leviticus 6:13). The accepted offering is Noah's accepted offering — *And Yahuah smelled a sweet savour... I will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake* (Genesis 8:21). And the Elohim who *appeared* and *blessed* on the altar is the same Word who delivers the seed from the deceiver — *This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil.* (1 John 3:8).$n$),
(11233,$n$Jared's warning sets the two destinies in the plainest terms: *He again adjured them, saying... for the moment you leave it, you will be reft of life and of mercy; and you shall no longer be called 'children of Elohim (God),' but 'children of the devil'* (2 Adam & Eve 20:27). And when they fall, it is the Word of Elohim who comes to Jared: *Then Elohim (God) sent His Word to Jared, saying, "These thy children, whom thou didst call 'My children,' - behold they have transgressed My commandment"* (2 Adam & Eve 20:35). That sent Word is the Logos: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1). And Jared's two names are John's two lines exactly: *He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of Elohim (God) was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8); *In this the children of Elohim (God) are manifest, and the children of the devil* (1 John 3:10). Election before confession — the seed kept, the seed lost.$n$,$n$Jared's warning sets the two destinies in the plainest terms: *He again adjured them, saying... for the moment you leave it, you will be reft of life and of mercy; and you shall no longer be called 'children of Elohim (God),' but 'children of the devil'* (2 Adam & Eve 20:27). And when they fall, it is the Word of Elohim who comes to Jared: *Then Elohim (God) sent His Word to Jared, saying, "These thy children, whom thou didst call 'My children,' - behold they have transgressed My commandment"* (2 Adam & Eve 20:35). That sent Word is the Logos: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1). And Jared's two names are John's two lines exactly: *Whoever goes on sinning belongs to the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the very beginning. This is why the Son of Elohim (God) was revealed: to undo the works of the devil* (1 John 3:8); *In this the children of Elohim (God) are manifest, and the children of the devil* (1 John 3:10). Election before confession — the seed kept, the seed lost.$n$),
(10853,$n$On the very first days outside the garden Elohim points Adam to the One by whom he was made: *Elohim (God) said to Adam, "I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen."* (1-adam-eve 3:1) This is the Logos — the Word who was in the beginning: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* (John 1:3) The same Word who made Adam is the Word who comes to save him: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14) And He framed the worlds: *For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:* (Colossians 1:16) It ain't new — the Saviour Adam looked for is the Maker he had known.$n$,$n$On the very first days outside the garden Elohim points Adam to the One by whom he was made: *Elohim (God) said to Adam, "I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen."* (1 Adam and Eve 3:1) This is the Logos — the Word who was in the beginning: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* (John 1:3) The same Word who made Adam is the Word who comes to save him: *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14) And He framed the worlds: *For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:* (Colossians 1:16) It ain't new — the Saviour Adam looked for is the Maker he had known.$n$),
(10854,$n$Elohim sets the term of the promise and Adam mishears it as a span of days: *Yes, the Word that will again save you when the five and a half days are fulfilled.* (1-adam-eve 3:2) — *For Adam was thinking there would be only five and a half days for him until the end of the world.* (1-adam-eve 3:4) But mercy explains the count: *Then Elohim (God) in his mercy for Adam who was made after His own image and likeness, explained to him, that these were 5,000 and 500 years; and how One would then come and save him and his descendants.* (1-adam-eve 3:6) This is the appointed term — the fulness of time — kept from before the world: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* (Galatians 4:4) the Lamb foreordained from the beginning: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* (1 Peter 1:20) spoken in the last days by the Son: *Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds;* (Hebrews 1:2) The redemption was set from the first day — it ain't new.$n$,$n$Elohim sets the term of the promise and Adam mishears it as a span of days: *Yes, the Word that will again save you when the five and a half days are fulfilled.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:2) — *For Adam was thinking there would be only five and a half days for him until the end of the world.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:4) But mercy explains the count: *Then Elohim (God) in his mercy for Adam who was made after His own image and likeness, explained to him, that these were 5,000 and 500 years; and how One would then come and save him and his descendants.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:6) This is the appointed term — the fulness of time — kept from before the world: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,* (Galatians 4:4) the Lamb foreordained from the beginning: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* (1 Peter 1:20) spoken in the last days by the Son: *Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds;* (Hebrews 1:2) The redemption was set from the first day — it ain't new.$n$),
(10856,$n$At the gate Adam and Eve meet the guardian of the way, and again receive mercy: *And again, when Adam was by the gate of the garden, and saw the cherub with a sword of flashing fire in his hand, and the cherub grew angry and frowned at him, both Adam and Eve became afraid of him, and thought he meant to put them to death. So they fell on their faces, trembled with fear.* (1-adam-eve 3:10) — *Then Elohim (God) had pity on them, and showed them mercy, and sent His Angel to keep the garden.* (1-adam-eve 3:14) — *And the Word of Yahuah (Lord) came to Adam and Eve, and raised them up.* (1-adam-eve 3:15) This is the very cherub of Eden: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24) The angel set to keep is the Father's charge: *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* (Psalms 91:11) And the same primeval history records the expulsion: *And He sent out of the Garden of Eden all flesh that was in the Garden of Eden, and all flesh was scattered according to its kinds, and according to its types to the places which had been created for them.* (Jubilees 3:29) It ain't new — the guarded gate and the Word who raises the fallen are one story, told twice.$n$,$n$At the gate Adam and Eve meet the guardian of the way, and again receive mercy: *And again, when Adam was by the gate of the garden, and saw the cherub with a sword of flashing fire in his hand, and the cherub grew angry and frowned at him, both Adam and Eve became afraid of him, and thought he meant to put them to death. So they fell on their faces, trembled with fear.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:10) — *Then Elohim (God) had pity on them, and showed them mercy, and sent His Angel to keep the garden.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:14) — *And the Word of Yahuah (Lord) came to Adam and Eve, and raised them up.* (1 Adam and Eve 3:15) This is the very cherub of Eden: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24) The angel set to keep is the Father's charge: *For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.* (Psalms 91:11) And the same primeval history records the expulsion: *And He sent out of the Garden of Eden all flesh that was in the Garden of Eden, and all flesh was scattered according to its kinds, and according to its types to the places which had been created for them.* (Jubilees 3:29) It ain't new — the guarded gate and the Word who raises the fallen are one story, told twice.$n$),
(10861,$n$Outside the garden, in the dark of the cave, Eve makes the first confession of the seed-war: *O Elohim (God), forgive me my sin, the sin which I committed, and don't remember it against me. For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison* (1-adam-eve 5:4-5). This is the very scene of Genesis: *And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat* (Genesis 3:6), and when Yahuah questioned her, *the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat* (Genesis 3:13). It ain't new — Sha'ul reads the same record: *And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression* (1 Timothy 2:14), and *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* (Romans 5:12). The serpent's beguiling in Eden is the first strike at the seed of the woman, and Eve's grief is already the bruised heel longing for the promised mercy.$n$,$n$Outside the garden, in the dark of the cave, Eve makes the first confession of the seed-war: *O Elohim (God), forgive me my sin, the sin which I committed, and don't remember it against me. For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison* (1 Adam and Eve 5:4-5). This is the very scene of Genesis: *And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat* (Genesis 3:6), and when Yahuah questioned her, *the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat* (Genesis 3:13). It ain't new — Sha'ul reads the same record: *And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression* (1 Timothy 2:14), and *as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned* (Romans 5:12). The serpent's beguiling in Eden is the first strike at the seed of the woman, and Eve's grief is already the bruised heel longing for the promised mercy.$n$),
(10862,$n$Eve grounds her plea in the mystery of her own making: *For You, O Elohim (God), caused him to fall asleep, and took a bone from his side, and restored the flesh in the place of it, by Your divine power. And You took me, the bone, and make me a woman... O Yahuah (Lord), I and he are one, and You, O Elohim (God), are our Creator, You are He who made us both in one day* (1-adam-eve 5:9-11). This is the creation of woman rehearsed back to the Creator: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof* (Genesis 2:21), so that Adam cried, *This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh* (Genesis 2:23). The same primeval history is kept in Jubilees: *And Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and he slept, and He took for the woman one rib from amongst his ribs... and built the woman* (Jubilees 3:5). Because the two were made one, Eve cannot conceive of living on alone — the one-flesh bond of Eden is the very plea on which she stands.$n$,$n$Eve grounds her plea in the mystery of her own making: *For You, O Elohim (God), caused him to fall asleep, and took a bone from his side, and restored the flesh in the place of it, by Your divine power. And You took me, the bone, and make me a woman... O Yahuah (Lord), I and he are one, and You, O Elohim (God), are our Creator, You are He who made us both in one day* (1 Adam and Eve 5:9-11). This is the creation of woman rehearsed back to the Creator: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof* (Genesis 2:21), so that Adam cried, *This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh* (Genesis 2:23). The same primeval history is kept in Jubilees: *And Yahuah our Elohim (the LORD our God) caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and he slept, and He took for the woman one rib from amongst his ribs... and built the woman* (Jubilees 3:5). Because the two were made one, Eve cannot conceive of living on alone — the one-flesh bond of Eden is the very plea on which she stands.$n$),
(10863,$n$Eve does not ask only for Adam's breath but for his repentance: *O Elohim (God), look at this Your servant fallen in this manner, and bring him back to life, that he may cry and repent of his transgression which he committed through me. Don't take away his soul right now; but let him live that he may stand after the measure of his repentance, and do Your will, as before his death* (1-adam-eve 5:6-7). This is the godly sorrow Sha'ul commends: *For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death* (2 Corinthians 7:10). And the mercy she leans on is no innovation but the grace that reigns over the fall: *For if by one man's offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by one, Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ)* (Romans 5:17). From the first day outside the garden, Yahuah's covenant mercy keeps the seed alive to repent — it ain't new.$n$,$n$Eve does not ask only for Adam's breath but for his repentance: *O Elohim (God), look at this Your servant fallen in this manner, and bring him back to life, that he may cry and repent of his transgression which he committed through me. Don't take away his soul right now; but let him live that he may stand after the measure of his repentance, and do Your will, as before his death* (1 Adam and Eve 5:6-7). This is the godly sorrow Sha'ul commends: *For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death* (2 Corinthians 7:10). And the mercy she leans on is no innovation but the grace that reigns over the fall: *For if by one man's offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by one, Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ)* (Romans 5:17). From the first day outside the garden, Yahuah's covenant mercy keeps the seed alive to repent — it ain't new.$n$),
(10864,$n$Eve will not be parted from the husband made one with her: *But if You do not bring him back to life, then, O Elohim (God), take away my own soul, that I be like him, and leave me not in this dungeon, one and alone; for I could not stand alone in this world, but with him only* (1-adam-eve 5:8), and again, *But if You will not give him life, then take me, even me, like him; that we both may die the same day* (1-adam-eve 5:13). This is the cleaving of Eden carried to its uttermost: *Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh* (Genesis 2:24). And even here, in the woman who fell, Sha'ul holds out a saving hope through the seed she will bear: *Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety* (1 Timothy 2:15). Her sorrowing fidelity over the seemingly dead Adam is the love that will not let the covenant line die.$n$,$n$Eve will not be parted from the husband made one with her: *But if You do not bring him back to life, then, O Elohim (God), take away my own soul, that I be like him, and leave me not in this dungeon, one and alone; for I could not stand alone in this world, but with him only* (1 Adam and Eve 5:8), and again, *But if You will not give him life, then take me, even me, like him; that we both may die the same day* (1 Adam and Eve 5:13). This is the cleaving of Eden carried to its uttermost: *Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh* (Genesis 2:24). And even here, in the woman who fell, Sha'ul holds out a saving hope through the seed she will bear: *Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety* (1 Timothy 2:15). Her sorrowing fidelity over the seemingly dead Adam is the love that will not let the covenant line die.$n$),
(10874,$n$Adam mourns the vision the garden once gave him: *"O Elohim (God), when we lived in the garden, and our hearts were lifted up, we saw the angels that sang praises in heaven, but now we can't see like we used to; no, when we entered the cave, all creation became hidden from us."* (1-adam-eve 8:1) The sight he laments is the very sight Enoch was later caught up to behold — *And I saw how the winds stretch out the vaults of heaven, and have their station between heaven and earth: these are the pillars of the heaven.* (1 Enoch 18:3) and the throne of the Most High, *But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.* (1 Enoch 18:8) What Adam forfeited by transgression, the seed kept holy may yet be lifted to see. And the loss is plainly named where the prophet tells it: *"But your iniquities have separated between you and your Elohim (God), and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear."* (Isaiah 59:2) It ain't new — sin is what hides the face of heaven from man.$n$,$n$Adam mourns the vision the garden once gave him: *"O Elohim (God), when we lived in the garden, and our hearts were lifted up, we saw the angels that sang praises in heaven, but now we can't see like we used to; no, when we entered the cave, all creation became hidden from us."* (1 Adam and Eve 8:1) The sight he laments is the very sight Enoch was later caught up to behold — *And I saw how the winds stretch out the vaults of heaven, and have their station between heaven and earth: these are the pillars of the heaven.* (1 Enoch 18:3) and the throne of the Most High, *But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.* (1 Enoch 18:8) What Adam forfeited by transgression, the seed kept holy may yet be lifted to see. And the loss is plainly named where the prophet tells it: *"But your iniquities have separated between you and your Elohim (God), and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear."* (Isaiah 59:2) It ain't new — sin is what hides the face of heaven from man.$n$),
(10875,$n$Yahuah answers Adam with the anatomy of the fall: *"When you were under subjection to Me, you had a bright nature within you, and for that reason could you see things far away. But after your transgression your bright nature was withdrawn from you; and it was not left to you to see things far away, but only near at hand; after the ability of the flesh; for it is brutish."* (1-adam-eve 8:2) This is Eden's reckoning carried out — *"And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked"* (Genesis 3:7) — eyes opened to shame are eyes shut to glory. Paul names the same brutish, near-sighted mind: *"For to be carnally minded is death; but to be spiritually minded is life and peace."* (Romans 8:6), *"Because the carnal mind is enmity against Elohim (God): for it is not subject to the law of Elohim (God), neither indeed can be."* (Romans 8:7) And the god of this world keeps that veil over fallen sight: *"In whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, lest the light of the glorious gospel of Messiah (Christ), who is the image of Elohim (God), should shine unto them."* (2 Corinthians 4:4) The withdrawn bright nature is the dimmed glass of a fallen race — *"For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face."* (1 Corinthians 13:12)$n$,$n$Yahuah answers Adam with the anatomy of the fall: *"When you were under subjection to Me, you had a bright nature within you, and for that reason could you see things far away. But after your transgression your bright nature was withdrawn from you; and it was not left to you to see things far away, but only near at hand; after the ability of the flesh; for it is brutish."* (1 Adam and Eve 8:2) This is Eden's reckoning carried out — *"And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked"* (Genesis 3:7) — eyes opened to shame are eyes shut to glory. Paul names the same brutish, near-sighted mind: *"For to be carnally minded is death; but to be spiritually minded is life and peace."* (Romans 8:6), *"Because the carnal mind is enmity against Elohim (God): for it is not subject to the law of Elohim (God), neither indeed can be."* (Romans 8:7) And the god of this world keeps that veil over fallen sight: *"In whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, lest the light of the glorious gospel of Messiah (Christ), who is the image of Elohim (God), should shine unto them."* (2 Corinthians 4:4) The withdrawn bright nature is the dimmed glass of a fallen race — *"For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face."* (1 Corinthians 13:12)$n$),
(10876,$n$The chapter closes in grief and in distance: *"When Adam and Eve had heard these words from Elohim (God), they went their way; praising and worshipping Him with a sorrowful heart. And Elohim (God) ceased to commune with them."* (1-adam-eve 8:3-4) The walking voice of Eden is now withdrawn — *"And they heard the voice of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) walking in the garden in the cool of the day: and Adam and his wife hid themselves from the presence of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) amongst the trees of the garden."* (Genesis 3:8) Yet the same Word who walked and spoke is the Logos who will not leave the seed forever — *"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)"* (John 1:1), and *"the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth."* (John 1:14). What Adam lost — the sight of his Maker — is the very promise restored to the redeemed: *"Beloved, now are we the sons of Elohim (God), and it doth not yet appear what we shall be: but we know that, when he shall appear, we shall be like him; for we shall see him as he is."* (1 John 3:2), when *"Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God)."* (Revelation 21:3). The communion that ceased in chapter 8 is the communion the Saviour comes to restore — it ain't new.$n$,$n$The chapter closes in grief and in distance: *"When Adam and Eve had heard these words from Elohim (God), they went their way; praising and worshipping Him with a sorrowful heart. And Elohim (God) ceased to commune with them."* (1 Adam and Eve 8:3-4) The walking voice of Eden is now withdrawn — *"And they heard the voice of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) walking in the garden in the cool of the day: and Adam and his wife hid themselves from the presence of Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) amongst the trees of the garden."* (Genesis 3:8) Yet the same Word who walked and spoke is the Logos who will not leave the seed forever — *"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)"* (John 1:1), and *"the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth."* (John 1:14). What Adam lost — the sight of his Maker — is the very promise restored to the redeemed: *"Beloved, now are we the sons of Elohim (God), and it doth not yet appear what we shall be: but we know that, when he shall appear, we shall be like him; for we shall see him as he is."* (1 John 3:2), when *"Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God)."* (Revelation 21:3). The communion that ceased in chapter 8 is the communion the Saviour comes to restore — it ain't new.$n$),
(10932,$n$Outside the garden Adam and Eve lift up their own blood as an offering, and mercy answers: *Then the merciful Elohim (God), good and lover of men, looked at Adam and Eve, and at their blood, which they had held up as an offering to Him; without an order from Him for so doing. But He wondered at them; and accepted their offerings* (1-adam-eve 24:1). *And Elohim (God) sent from His presence a bright fire, that consumed their offering* (1-adam-eve 24:2), and *He smelled the sweet savor of their offering, and showed them mercy* (1-adam-eve 24:3). It ain't new — the very first altar outside Eden already keeps the way of approach by blood that the whole Torah will guard. So Abel's firstlings find favour while Cain's bloodless fruit does not: *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4). So Noah's altar after the flood draws the same mercy: *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake* (Genesis 8:21). Jubilees tells the same scene of the goodly savour rising acceptable before Yahuah (Jubilees 6:3). And the whole sacrificial order rests on the word given to Adam here in deed: *For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls* (Leviticus 17:11).$n$,$n$Outside the garden Adam and Eve lift up their own blood as an offering, and mercy answers: *Then the merciful Elohim (God), good and lover of men, looked at Adam and Eve, and at their blood, which they had held up as an offering to Him; without an order from Him for so doing. But He wondered at them; and accepted their offerings* (1 Adam and Eve 24:1). *And Elohim (God) sent from His presence a bright fire, that consumed their offering* (1 Adam and Eve 24:2), and *He smelled the sweet savor of their offering, and showed them mercy* (1 Adam and Eve 24:3). It ain't new — the very first altar outside Eden already keeps the way of approach by blood that the whole Torah will guard. So Abel's firstlings find favour while Cain's bloodless fruit does not: *And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And Yahuah (LORD) had respect unto Abel and to his offering* (Genesis 4:4). So Noah's altar after the flood draws the same mercy: *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man's sake* (Genesis 8:21). Jubilees tells the same scene of the goodly savour rising acceptable before Yahuah (Jubilees 6:3). And the whole sacrificial order rests on the word given to Adam here in deed: *For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls* (Leviticus 17:11).$n$),
(10933,$n$Then the Logos Himself comes to Adam and pledges the incarnation and the cross: *Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die"* (1-adam-eve 24:4). The Word who speaks is the Word who was always with Elohim: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1) — and the promise to become flesh of Adam's descendants is fulfilled when *the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14). It ain't new: the gospel is preached to Adam on day one. Paul dates the very moment Adam is here promised: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law* (Galatians 4:4). And the Lamb's death was no afterthought but foreordained from this beginning: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$,$n$Then the Logos Himself comes to Adam and pledges the incarnation and the cross: *Then came the Word of Elohim (God) to Adam, and said to him, "O Adam, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adam, so also will I die"* (1 Adam and Eve 24:4). The Word who speaks is the Word who was always with Elohim: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1) — and the promise to become flesh of Adam's descendants is fulfilled when *the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14). It ain't new: the gospel is preached to Adam on day one. Paul dates the very moment Adam is here promised: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law* (Galatians 4:4). And the Lamb's death was no afterthought but foreordained from this beginning: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$),
(10934,$n$The Word matches Adam's altar to His own: *And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth* (1-adam-eve 24:4), *and as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it* (1-adam-eve 24:5). The altar of earth is the very altar Yahuah names to the fathers — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 8:20) — and the blood that makes forgiveness is the blood of Messiah: *Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us* (Hebrews 9:12). The rule Adam lived by stands behind the cross: *and without shedding of blood is no remission* (Hebrews 9:22). At the table the Messiah names this blood as the one Adam was promised: *For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins* (Matthew 26:28). It ain't new — Calvary is the altar of earth pledged outside Eden.$n$,$n$The Word matches Adam's altar to His own: *And as you built an altar, so also will I make for you an altar of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an altar on the earth* (1 Adam and Eve 24:4), *and as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it* (1 Adam and Eve 24:5). The altar of earth is the very altar Yahuah names to the fathers — *And Noah builded an altar unto Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 8:20) — and the blood that makes forgiveness is the blood of Messiah: *Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us* (Hebrews 9:12). The rule Adam lived by stands behind the cross: *and without shedding of blood is no remission* (Hebrews 9:22). At the table the Messiah names this blood as the one Adam was promised: *For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins* (Matthew 26:28). It ain't new — Calvary is the altar of earth pledged outside Eden.$n$),
(10935,$n$The Word seals the promise with the long appointed reckoning and the offering kept against sorrow: *And now, behold, I have accepted your offering, O Adam, but the days of the covenant in which I have bound you are not fulfilled. When they are fulfilled, then will I bring you back into the garden* (1-adam-eve 24:6), *"Now, therefore, strengthen your heart; and when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering, and I will be favorable to you"* (1-adam-eve 24:7). These "days of the covenant" run to the fulness Paul names: *To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons* (Galatians 4:5). The same blood-bound covenant of perpetual offering is given to Noah's house in Jubilees, that they continue supplicating with blood before the altar morning and evening for ever (Jubilees 6:14). And the way back into the garden the Word promises Adam is the very last-days work He provides — *Who being the brightness of his glory... when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high* (Hebrews 1:3). It ain't new — the covenant that ends in Eden restored was bound on Adam the first day out.$n$,$n$The Word seals the promise with the long appointed reckoning and the offering kept against sorrow: *And now, behold, I have accepted your offering, O Adam, but the days of the covenant in which I have bound you are not fulfilled. When they are fulfilled, then will I bring you back into the garden* (1 Adam and Eve 24:6), *"Now, therefore, strengthen your heart; and when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering, and I will be favorable to you"* (1 Adam and Eve 24:7). These "days of the covenant" run to the fulness Paul names: *To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons* (Galatians 4:5). The same blood-bound covenant of perpetual offering is given to Noah's house in Jubilees, that they continue supplicating with blood before the altar morning and evening for ever (Jubilees 6:14). And the way back into the garden the Word promises Adam is the very last-days work He provides — *Who being the brightness of his glory... when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high* (Hebrews 1:3). It ain't new — the covenant that ends in Eden restored was bound on Adam the first day out.$n$),
(10949,$n$Satan comes against the first pair in borrowed glory: *But when the crafty Satan saw them, that they were going to the garden, he gathered together his host, and came in appearance on a cloud, intent on deceiving them* (1-adam-eve 28:1), and *But when Adam and Eve saw him thus in a vision, they thought they were angels of Elohim (God) come to comfort them about having left the garden* (1-adam-eve 28:2). It ain't new — Sha'ul names the very disguise: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The same subtilty that first beguiled the woman wears now a robe of light: *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ)* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the deceiver who *came in appearance on a cloud* is the *old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$,$n$Satan comes against the first pair in borrowed glory: *But when the crafty Satan saw them, that they were going to the garden, he gathered together his host, and came in appearance on a cloud, intent on deceiving them* (1 Adam and Eve 28:1), and *But when Adam and Eve saw him thus in a vision, they thought they were angels of Elohim (God) come to comfort them about having left the garden* (1 Adam and Eve 28:2). It ain't new — Sha'ul names the very disguise: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The same subtilty that first beguiled the woman wears now a robe of light: *But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Messiah (Christ)* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the deceiver who *came in appearance on a cloud* is the *old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world* (Revelation 12:9).$n$),
(10950,$n$Where the serpent's lie overthrew Eve in the garden, Yahuah now lets Adam be tried: *Yet Elohim (God) withheld His Word from Adam, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Eve was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail* (1-adam-eve 28:7). The Word withheld here is the very Word the serpent first contradicted — *And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die* (Genesis 3:4) — the seed-war that began the moment the deceiver opened his mouth. Yahusha holds the same Word against the same tempter: *And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free* (John 8:32), for the devil *is a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44). And the whole contest moves toward the promise that the woman's Seed *shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$,$n$Where the serpent's lie overthrew Eve in the garden, Yahuah now lets Adam be tried: *Yet Elohim (God) withheld His Word from Adam, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Eve was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail* (1 Adam and Eve 28:7). The Word withheld here is the very Word the serpent first contradicted — *And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die* (Genesis 3:4) — the seed-war that began the moment the deceiver opened his mouth. Yahusha holds the same Word against the same tempter: *And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free* (John 8:32), for the devil *is a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44). And the whole contest moves toward the promise that the woman's Seed *shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$),
(10952,$n$Satan's mercy is murder in disguise: he leads them *to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it*, and *made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone* (1-adam-eve 28:10). It ain't new — the same tempter takes the second Adam up the same kind of height with the same word: *Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the temple, And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of Elohim (God), cast thyself down* (Matthew 4:5-6), and *Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain* (Matthew 4:8). The adversary who would *wipe off their name from the earth* is the *roaring lion* who *walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8) — but the promised Seed shall *bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$,$n$Satan's mercy is murder in disguise: he leads them *to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it*, and *made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone* (1 Adam and Eve 28:10). It ain't new — the same tempter takes the second Adam up the same kind of height with the same word: *Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the temple, And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of Elohim (God), cast thyself down* (Matthew 4:5-6), and *Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain* (Matthew 4:8). The adversary who would *wipe off their name from the earth* is the *roaring lion* who *walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8) — but the promised Seed shall *bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$),
(10956,$n$From the gates of the lost garden the angels bring three tokens to the grieving man: *The golden rods were from the Indian sea, where there are precious stones. The incense was from the eastern border of the garden; and the myrrh from the western border, from where bitterness came over Adam.* (1-adam-eve 30:6). These are the very treasures the holy line will keep in the Cave of Treasures down to the manger, for when the wise men came they *presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* (Matthew 2:11) — the gold for the King, the incense for Elohim, the myrrh for the burial; it ain't new, the gifts were chosen the first day outside Eden. Adam reads them aright: *And when Adam saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he was rejoiced and cried because he thought that the gold was a token of the kingdom from where he had come, that the incense was a token of the bright light which had been taken from him, and that the myrrh was a token of the sorrow in which he was.* (1-adam-eve 30:10). The myrrh of bitterness answers the curse spoken over the ground: *cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;* (Genesis 3:17) — and that same sorrow is undone in the seed who carries the myrrh to His own grave.$n$,$n$From the gates of the lost garden the angels bring three tokens to the grieving man: *The golden rods were from the Indian sea, where there are precious stones. The incense was from the eastern border of the garden; and the myrrh from the western border, from where bitterness came over Adam.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:6). These are the very treasures the holy line will keep in the Cave of Treasures down to the manger, for when the wise men came they *presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.* (Matthew 2:11) — the gold for the King, the incense for Elohim, the myrrh for the burial; it ain't new, the gifts were chosen the first day outside Eden. Adam reads them aright: *And when Adam saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he was rejoiced and cried because he thought that the gold was a token of the kingdom from where he had come, that the incense was a token of the bright light which had been taken from him, and that the myrrh was a token of the sorrow in which he was.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:10). The myrrh of bitterness answers the curse spoken over the ground: *cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;* (Genesis 3:17) — and that same sorrow is undone in the seed who carries the myrrh to His own grave.$n$),
(10957,$n$Elohim sends His angels back to the very gate that was barred against Adam: *And the angels brought these things to Elohim (God), by the Tree of Life, in the garden.* (1-adam-eve 30:7), and at the Tree's spring the cherub yields up the incense and myrrh. This is the gate kept by the guardian set after the fall: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24) — the way is shut, yet mercy reaches through the cherub to comfort the exiles. And the Tree of Life is not lost forever; it stands again in the City at the end: *In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* (Revelation 22:2). The seed-war that opens here closes at that Tree.$n$,$n$Elohim sends His angels back to the very gate that was barred against Adam: *And the angels brought these things to Elohim (God), by the Tree of Life, in the garden.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:7), and at the Tree's spring the cherub yields up the incense and myrrh. This is the gate kept by the guardian set after the fall: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24) — the way is shut, yet mercy reaches through the cherub to comfort the exiles. And the Tree of Life is not lost forever; it stands again in the City at the end: *In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* (Revelation 22:2). The seed-war that opens here closes at that Tree.$n$),
(10958,$n$Yahuah does not leave the exiles to despair on the mountain where Satan had driven them: *Then Elohim (God) said to the angels, "Dip them in the spring of water; then take them and sprinkle their water over Adam and Eve, that they be a little comforted in their sorrow, and give them to Adam and Eve.* (1-adam-eve 30:8), and the angels carry the comfort to the very crag of the enemy's assault: *And the angels did as Elohim (God) had commanded them, and they gave all those things to Adam and Eve on the top of the mountain on which Satan had placed them, when he sought to make an end of them.* (1-adam-eve 30:9). This is covenant mercy keeping the seed Satan sought to destroy — the enmity sworn at the gate: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The water of comfort sprinkled here flows on to the throne: *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* (Revelation 22:1).$n$,$n$Yahuah does not leave the exiles to despair on the mountain where Satan had driven them: *Then Elohim (God) said to the angels, "Dip them in the spring of water; then take them and sprinkle their water over Adam and Eve, that they be a little comforted in their sorrow, and give them to Adam and Eve.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:8), and the angels carry the comfort to the very crag of the enemy's assault: *And the angels did as Elohim (God) had commanded them, and they gave all those things to Adam and Eve on the top of the mountain on which Satan had placed them, when he sought to make an end of them.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:9). This is covenant mercy keeping the seed Satan sought to destroy — the enmity sworn at the gate: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The water of comfort sprinkled here flows on to the throne: *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* (Revelation 22:1).$n$),
(10959,$n$Twice the angels are sent for the holy incense — Gabriel by command, the cherub assenting: *Then the angel Gabriel went down by Elohim's (God's) order to the garden, and told the cherub as Elohim (God) had commanded him.* and *The cherub then said, "Well." And Gabriel went in and took the incense.* (1-adam-eve 30:2, 30:3). The incense is no ordinary spice but a holy thing set apart before Yahuah, as the perfume of the tabernacle was commanded: *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* (Exodus 30:34). Adam reads it rightly — the incense a token of the bright light taken from him in 1-adam-eve 30:10 — the ascending smoke a sign of the light and presence he had lost, kept against the day the True Light returns. The Word who will restore that light is the Logos: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1).$n$,$n$Twice the angels are sent for the holy incense — Gabriel by command, the cherub assenting: *Then the angel Gabriel went down by Elohim's (God's) order to the garden, and told the cherub as Elohim (God) had commanded him.* and *The cherub then said, "Well." And Gabriel went in and took the incense.* (1 Adam and Eve 30:2, 30:3). The incense is no ordinary spice but a holy thing set apart before Yahuah, as the perfume of the tabernacle was commanded: *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* (Exodus 30:34). Adam reads it rightly — the incense a token of the bright light taken from him in 1 Adam and Eve 30:10 — the ascending smoke a sign of the light and presence he had lost, kept against the day the True Light returns. The Word who will restore that light is the Logos: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1).$n$),
(10987,$n$The very Word who made the worlds comes down to comfort fallen Adam, and the comfort He gives is Himself: *"After these things the Word of Elohim (God) came to Adam, and said to him"* (1-adam-eve 38:1), promising that *"only when the 5500 years are fulfilled... I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever"* (1-adam-eve 38:2). It ain't new — this is the Logos of the prologue, the One *"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)"* (John 1:1), who would in due time be *"made flesh, and dwelt among us"* (John 1:14). The 5500-year promise is the foreordained incarnation, for He *"who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets"* (Hebrews 1:1) was *"foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you"* (1 Peter 1:20), and at the appointed hour *"when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law"* (Galatians 4:4). From the first day outside the garden the Word is already the Saviour-to-come.$n$,$n$The very Word who made the worlds comes down to comfort fallen Adam, and the comfort He gives is Himself: *"After these things the Word of Elohim (God) came to Adam, and said to him"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:1), promising that *"only when the 5500 years are fulfilled... I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2). It ain't new — this is the Logos of the prologue, the One *"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)"* (John 1:1), who would in due time be *"made flesh, and dwelt among us"* (John 1:14). The 5500-year promise is the foreordained incarnation, for He *"who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets"* (Hebrews 1:1) was *"foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you"* (1 Peter 1:20), and at the appointed hour *"when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law"* (Galatians 4:4). From the first day outside the garden the Word is already the Saviour-to-come.$n$),
(10988,$n$Adam begs for the Tree of Life, and the Word does not deny but defers it: *"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants"* (1-adam-eve 38:2). This is the very tree Genesis set in the garden — *"the tree of life also in the midst of the garden"* (Genesis 2:9) — from which fallen man was barred, for Yahuah drove him out *"lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever"* (Genesis 3:22). What was sealed by the flaming sword is reopened at the end of the age: the overcomer is told *"To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God)"* (Revelation 2:7), and the regathered are blessed who *"do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city"* (Revelation 22:14). The promise to Adam is the promise of paradise restored.$n$,$n$Adam begs for the Tree of Life, and the Word does not deny but defers it: *"O Adam, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Eve, and your righteous descendants"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:2). This is the very tree Genesis set in the garden — *"the tree of life also in the midst of the garden"* (Genesis 2:9) — from which fallen man was barred, for Yahuah drove him out *"lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever"* (Genesis 3:22). What was sealed by the flaming sword is reopened at the end of the age: the overcomer is told *"To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God)"* (Revelation 2:7), and the regathered are blessed who *"do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city"* (Revelation 22:14). The promise to Adam is the promise of paradise restored.$n$),
(10990,$n$The Word seals the comfort with covenant faithfulness: *"I will not deny your request, neither will I disappoint your hope; therefore, endure until the fulfillment of the covenant I made with you"* (1-adam-eve 38:5). Every pledge of Elohim is sure in the One who is coming, for *"all the promises of Elohim (God) in him are yea, and in him Amen, unto the glory of Elohim (God) by us"* (2 Corinthians 1:20). The covenant Adam is told to endure for is the better covenant the Saviour Himself mediates, He who *"obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises"* (Hebrews 8:6). Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed from the first day, never law-as-curse but a hope undisappointed.$n$,$n$The Word seals the comfort with covenant faithfulness: *"I will not deny your request, neither will I disappoint your hope; therefore, endure until the fulfillment of the covenant I made with you"* (1 Adam and Eve 38:5). Every pledge of Elohim is sure in the One who is coming, for *"all the promises of Elohim (God) in him are yea, and in him Amen, unto the glory of Elohim (God) by us"* (2 Corinthians 1:20). The covenant Adam is told to endure for is the better covenant the Saviour Himself mediates, He who *"obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises"* (Hebrews 8:6). Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed from the first day, never law-as-curse but a hope undisappointed.$n$),
(10997,$n$Adam turns Eve toward the one landmark of the lost garden that still flows in their memory: *"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink."* (1-adam-eve 41:5). It ain't new — the four-headed river is Eden's own geography from the sixth-day account: *And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.* (Genesis 2:10). The Water of Life Adam thirsts for is the water that ran beneath the very tree Yahuah barred: *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* (Genesis 2:9). And the same restored history is told again in Jubilees, where the garden is no ordinary ground: *And when she had completed these eighty days we brought her into the Garden of Eden, for it is holier than all the earth besides, and every tree that is planted in it is holy.* (Jubilees 3:11) — Adam stands now at the border of the holiest place on earth, shut out, and prays toward it.$n$,$n$Adam turns Eve toward the one landmark of the lost garden that still flows in their memory: *"O Eve, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Elohim (God), and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink."* (1 Adam and Eve 41:5). It ain't new — the four-headed river is Eden's own geography from the sixth-day account: *And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.* (Genesis 2:10). The Water of Life Adam thirsts for is the water that ran beneath the very tree Yahuah barred: *the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* (Genesis 2:9). And the same restored history is told again in Jubilees, where the garden is no ordinary ground: *And when she had completed these eighty days we brought her into the Garden of Eden, for it is holier than all the earth besides, and every tree that is planted in it is holy.* (Jubilees 3:11) — Adam stands now at the border of the holiest place on earth, shut out, and prays toward it.$n$),
(10998,$n$From the dust outside Eden, Adam cries the thirst of all flesh: *"But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live."* (1-adam-eve 41:12). It ain't new — this is the longing the whole of Scripture answers, and answers in One. The Word who comes to comfort Adam is the same who stood at Jacob's well and said, *But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.* (John 4:14), and who cried on the great day of the feast, *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.* (John 7:37). The seed-promise runs the whole arc: the river Adam mourns will run again unbarred at the end, *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* (Revelation 22:1), and the invitation is laid open to the very thirst Adam feels: *And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.* (Revelation 22:17). Even now the psalmist tastes the foretaste: *thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.* (Psalms 36:8).$n$,$n$From the dust outside Eden, Adam cries the thirst of all flesh: *"But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live."* (1 Adam and Eve 41:12). It ain't new — this is the longing the whole of Scripture answers, and answers in One. The Word who comes to comfort Adam is the same who stood at Jacob's well and said, *But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.* (John 4:14), and who cried on the great day of the feast, *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.* (John 7:37). The seed-promise runs the whole arc: the river Adam mourns will run again unbarred at the end, *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* (Revelation 22:1), and the invitation is laid open to the very thirst Adam feels: *And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.* (Revelation 22:17). Even now the psalmist tastes the foretaste: *thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.* (Psalms 36:8).$n$),
(10999,$n$Adam's whole plaint turns on a single sentence of the Genesis judgment made flesh in him: *"But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst."* (1-adam-eve 41:12). It ain't new — this is the sentence spoken over him at the gate: *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* (Genesis 3:19). And the barred Tree of Life he longs to be fed from is barred by the Cherubim's flaming sword: *and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24). Yet his plea — *bring me into another land different from this, if You will not let me live in Your garden* — is mercy seeking mercy under the very curse, and the seed-promise is its ground, *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$,$n$Adam's whole plaint turns on a single sentence of the Genesis judgment made flesh in him: *"But now, O Elohim (God), I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst."* (1 Adam and Eve 41:12). It ain't new — this is the sentence spoken over him at the gate: *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* (Genesis 3:19). And the barred Tree of Life he longs to be fed from is barred by the Cherubim's flaming sword: *and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24). Yet his plea — *bring me into another land different from this, if You will not let me live in Your garden* — is mercy seeking mercy under the very curse, and the seed-promise is its ground, *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly* (Romans 16:20).$n$),
(11000,$n$The chapter opens not with despair but with worship — the first offering Adam and Eve bring outside the garden: *Then Adam took the fig, and laid it on the golden rods. Eve also took her fig, and put it on the incense.* (1-adam-eve 41:1), and *Adam and Eve remained standing and fasting the whole of that night, until the morning dawned.* (1-adam-eve 41:3). It ain't new — the fig is the very leaf of their first covering, *and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons* (Genesis 3:7), now lifted up not to hide but to offer. This is the way kept before Sinai: long before the law was law-as-curse, the line of the seed called on the Name, *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26). The same restored history is told in Jubilees, where Adam in the garden *gathered its fruit, and ate, and put aside the residue for himself and for his wife and put aside that which was being kept* (Jubilees 3:16) — the very garden-fruit he now stands outside of, fasting before Yahuah.$n$,$n$The chapter opens not with despair but with worship — the first offering Adam and Eve bring outside the garden: *Then Adam took the fig, and laid it on the golden rods. Eve also took her fig, and put it on the incense.* (1 Adam and Eve 41:1), and *Adam and Eve remained standing and fasting the whole of that night, until the morning dawned.* (1 Adam and Eve 41:3). It ain't new — the fig is the very leaf of their first covering, *and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons* (Genesis 3:7), now lifted up not to hide but to offer. This is the way kept before Sinai: long before the law was law-as-curse, the line of the seed called on the Name, *then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD)* (Genesis 4:26). The same restored history is told in Jubilees, where Adam in the garden *gathered its fruit, and ate, and put aside the residue for himself and for his wife and put aside that which was being kept* (Jubilees 3:16) — the very garden-fruit he now stands outside of, fasting before Yahuah.$n$),
(11009,$n$Satan builds the flames high to consume the cave, *And Satan kept on bringing trees and throwing them into the fire, until the flames of the fire rose up on high, and covered the whole cave, thinking, as he did in his own mind, to consume the cave with much fire. But the angel of Yahuah (Lord) was guarding it.* (1-adam-eve 44:2) — and the unburnt dwelling within the fire is the old wonder. Yahuah's ministering ones ARE fire: *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* (Psalm 104:4). At the bush the flame did not consume: *And the angel of Yahuah (LORD) appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.* (Exodus 3:2). And the same flaming guard had kept Eden's gate: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24).$n$,$n$Satan builds the flames high to consume the cave, *And Satan kept on bringing trees and throwing them into the fire, until the flames of the fire rose up on high, and covered the whole cave, thinking, as he did in his own mind, to consume the cave with much fire. But the angel of Yahuah (Lord) was guarding it.* (1 Adam and Eve 44:2) — and the unburnt dwelling within the fire is the old wonder. Yahuah's ministering ones ARE fire: *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* (Psalm 104:4). At the bush the flame did not consume: *And the angel of Yahuah (LORD) appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.* (Exodus 3:2). And the same flaming guard had kept Eden's gate: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24).$n$),
(11010,$n$The Logos Himself silences the accuser: *until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.* (1-adam-eve 44:4) — the Word who was from the beginning, *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1). The charge names the same enemy under his masks. He counterfeits even comfort and light: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). He was a deceiver and destroyer from the first: *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44). It is that old serpent still: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). It ain't new.$n$,$n$The Logos Himself silences the accuser: *until the Word of Elohim (God) came who said to Satan, "Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them.* (1 Adam and Eve 44:4) — the Word who was from the beginning, *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1). The charge names the same enemy under his masks. He counterfeits even comfort and light: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). He was a deceiver and destroyer from the first: *Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44). It is that old serpent still: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.* (Revelation 12:9). It ain't new.$n$),
(11012,$n$The deceiver cannot stand before the Word and is driven off, the seed preserved: *Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.* (1-adam-eve 44:6) — every assault is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, and Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The crushing is sure and soon: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20). The Saviour who keeps the seed was no afterthought but foreordained from before the world: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* (1 Peter 1:20). The valley of burning fire prepared for the enemy's hosts is the same judgment Enoch saw: *And I looked and turned to another part of the earth, and saw there a deep valley with burning fire.* (1 Enoch 54:1).$n$,$n$The deceiver cannot stand before the Word and is driven off, the seed preserved: *Then Satan fled from before Yahuah (Lord). But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adam and Eve had spent since they came out of the garden.* (1 Adam and Eve 44:6) — every assault is the serpent striking at the seed of the woman, and Yahuah's mercy keeps the seed: *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The crushing is sure and soon: *And the Elohim (God) of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) be with you. Amen.* (Romans 16:20). The Saviour who keeps the seed was no afterthought but foreordained from before the world: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,* (1 Peter 1:20). The valley of burning fire prepared for the enemy's hosts is the same judgment Enoch saw: *And I looked and turned to another part of the earth, and saw there a deep valley with burning fire.* (1 Enoch 54:1).$n$),
(11013,$n$Adam reads his fallen estate in the fire that once served him and now burns: *See this fire of which we have a portion in us: which formerly yielded to us, but no longer does so, now that we have transgressed the limit of creation, and changed our condition, and our nature is altered.* (1-adam-eve 44:9) — the sentence of the fall is that the creature, once at home in the garden, is now subject to the ground and to death: *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* (Genesis 3:19). The way back is barred by the very fire of the guard: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24).$n$,$n$Adam reads his fallen estate in the fire that once served him and now burns: *See this fire of which we have a portion in us: which formerly yielded to us, but no longer does so, now that we have transgressed the limit of creation, and changed our condition, and our nature is altered.* (1 Adam and Eve 44:9) — the sentence of the fall is that the creature, once at home in the garden, is now subject to the ground and to death: *In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.* (Genesis 3:19). The way back is barred by the very fire of the guard: *So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* (Genesis 3:24).$n$),
(11014,$n$The Word of Elohim names the deceiver to Adam: *"See, O Adam, how Satan has exalted you! He has deprived you of the Godhead, and of an exalted state like Me, and has not kept his word to you; but has, after all, become your enemy. He is the one who made this fire in which he meant to burn you and Eve"* (1-adam-eve 45:5), and *"he wished to make you come out of light into darkness; and from an exalted state to degradation"* (1-adam-eve 45:8). It ain't new — the fire around the cave is the same serpent who struck in Eden, the murderer and liar from the beginning. *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44). His lie is dressed as light: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The roaring lion still walks: *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour.* (1 Peter 5:8). And he is the same dragon the heavens cast out: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world.* (Revelation 12:9).$n$,$n$The Word of Elohim names the deceiver to Adam: *"See, O Adam, how Satan has exalted you! He has deprived you of the Godhead, and of an exalted state like Me, and has not kept his word to you; but has, after all, become your enemy. He is the one who made this fire in which he meant to burn you and Eve"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:5), and *"he wished to make you come out of light into darkness; and from an exalted state to degradation"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:8). It ain't new — the fire around the cave is the same serpent who struck in Eden, the murderer and liar from the beginning. *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.* (John 8:44). His lie is dressed as light: *And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.* (2 Corinthians 11:14). The roaring lion still walks: *Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour.* (1 Peter 5:8). And he is the same dragon the heavens cast out: *And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world.* (Revelation 12:9).$n$),
(11016,$n$Into Adam's hell-shadowed dread the Word sets the Messianic hope: *"You will not be delivered from it until My coming... not until My Word comes and makes a way for you on the day My covenant is fulfilled"* (1-adam-eve 45:10), and *"There is no way for you at present to come from this life to rest, not until My Word comes, who is My Word. Then He will make a way for you, and you shall have rest"* (1-adam-eve 45:11). The Comforter who speaks to Adam IS the Logos, and He foretells His own incarnation in the fulness of time. *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us... full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14). The day of the covenant came at the appointed hour: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law.* (Galatians 4:4). And this coming was no afterthought but foreordained from the very foundation Adam stood at: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you.* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$,$n$Into Adam's hell-shadowed dread the Word sets the Messianic hope: *"You will not be delivered from it until My coming... not until My Word comes and makes a way for you on the day My covenant is fulfilled"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:10), and *"There is no way for you at present to come from this life to rest, not until My Word comes, who is My Word. Then He will make a way for you, and you shall have rest"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:11). The Comforter who speaks to Adam IS the Logos, and He foretells His own incarnation in the fulness of time. *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* (John 1:1) — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us... full of grace and truth.* (John 1:14). The day of the covenant came at the appointed hour: *But when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law.* (Galatians 4:4). And this coming was no afterthought but foreordained from the very foundation Adam stood at: *Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you.* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$),
(11017,$n$Then the Logos acts as He spoke: *"Then Elohim (God) called with His Word to the fire that burned around the cave, that it split itself in half, until Adam had gone through it. Then the fire parted itself by Elohim's (God's) order, and a way was made for Adam"* (1-adam-eve 45:11). The Word who makes a way through the fire is the same who later cleaves the sea and the river for His people. *And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and Yahuah (LORD) caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided.* (Exodus 14:21) — *And the children of Yashar'el (Israel) went into the midst of the sea upon the dry ground.* (Exodus 14:22). So too the Jordan stood up in a heap before the ark at the city named for Adam himself: *That the waters which came down from above stood and rose up upon an heap very far from the city Adam... and the people passed over right against Jericho.* (Joshua 3:16). And the Son of Elohim still stands unhurt with His own in the furnace: *Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of Elohim (God).* (Daniel 3:25).$n$,$n$Then the Logos acts as He spoke: *"Then Elohim (God) called with His Word to the fire that burned around the cave, that it split itself in half, until Adam had gone through it. Then the fire parted itself by Elohim's (God's) order, and a way was made for Adam"* (1 Adam and Eve 45:11). The Word who makes a way through the fire is the same who later cleaves the sea and the river for His people. *And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and Yahuah (LORD) caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided.* (Exodus 14:21) — *And the children of Yashar'el (Israel) went into the midst of the sea upon the dry ground.* (Exodus 14:22). So too the Jordan stood up in a heap before the ark at the city named for Adam himself: *That the waters which came down from above stood and rose up upon an heap very far from the city Adam... and the people passed over right against Jericho.* (Joshua 3:16). And the Son of Elohim still stands unhurt with His own in the furnace: *Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of Elohim (God).* (Daniel 3:25).$n$),
(11018,$n$Come and see how the serpent strikes at the seed with fire, and how Yahuah's mercy keeps it. *Then Adam and Eve began again to come into the cave. And when they came to the way between the fire, Satan blew into the fire like a whirlwind, and caused the burning coal-fire to cover Adam and Eve; so that their bodies were singed; and the coal-fire scorched them* (1-adam-eve 46:1). They cry, *O Yahuah (Lord), save us! Leave us not to be consumed and plagued by this burning fire* (1-adam-eve 46:2), and *Elohim (God) sent His angel that stayed the burning fire* (1-adam-eve 46:3). It ain't new: the adversary is *your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8), yet *the angel of Yahuah (LORD) encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them* (Psalm 34:7). The same Elohim who appears to Adam in fire is the One of whom it is written *our Elohim (God) is a consuming fire* (Hebrews 12:29) — the fire that scorches the flesh cannot consume the seed He has sworn to keep.$n$,$n$Come and see how the serpent strikes at the seed with fire, and how Yahuah's mercy keeps it. *Then Adam and Eve began again to come into the cave. And when they came to the way between the fire, Satan blew into the fire like a whirlwind, and caused the burning coal-fire to cover Adam and Eve; so that their bodies were singed; and the coal-fire scorched them* (1 Adam and Eve 46:1). They cry, *O Yahuah (Lord), save us! Leave us not to be consumed and plagued by this burning fire* (1 Adam and Eve 46:2), and *Elohim (God) sent His angel that stayed the burning fire* (1 Adam and Eve 46:3). It ain't new: the adversary is *your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour* (1 Peter 5:8), yet *the angel of Yahuah (LORD) encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them* (Psalm 34:7). The same Elohim who appears to Adam in fire is the One of whom it is written *our Elohim (God) is a consuming fire* (Hebrews 12:29) — the fire that scorches the flesh cannot consume the seed He has sworn to keep.$n$),
(11019,$n$Come and see the deceiver unmasked, and the Deliverer remembered. *And Elohim (God) said to Adam, "See Satan's love for you, who pretended to give you the Godhead and greatness; and, behold, he burns you with fire, and seeks to destroy you from off the earth"* (1-adam-eve 46:4), *"I created you, and how many times have I delivered you out of his hand?"* (1-adam-eve 46:5). It ain't new: *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14), the murderer who *was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth* (John 8:44). But over against his pretended love stands the covenant faithfulness that *will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape* (1 Corinthians 10:13), for *many are the afflictions of the righteous: but Yahuah (LORD) delivereth him out of them all* (Psalm 34:19).$n$,$n$Come and see the deceiver unmasked, and the Deliverer remembered. *And Elohim (God) said to Adam, "See Satan's love for you, who pretended to give you the Godhead and greatness; and, behold, he burns you with fire, and seeks to destroy you from off the earth"* (1 Adam and Eve 46:4), *"I created you, and how many times have I delivered you out of his hand?"* (1 Adam and Eve 46:5). It ain't new: *Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14), the murderer who *was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth* (John 8:44). But over against his pretended love stands the covenant faithfulness that *will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape* (1 Corinthians 10:13), for *many are the afflictions of the righteous: but Yahuah (LORD) delivereth him out of them all* (Psalm 34:19).$n$),
(11020,$n$Come and see the old lie quoted back and judged. *Elohim (God) said again to Eve, "What is that he promised you in the garden, saying, 'As soon as you eat from the tree, your eyes will be opened, and you shall become like gods, knowing good and evil.' But look! He has burnt your bodies with fire"* (1-adam-eve 46:6); *"as to the Godhead he cannot give it to you... No, he was bitter against you and your descendants, that will come after you"* (1-adam-eve 46:7). It ain't new — this is the serpent's first sentence verbatim: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5), the subtilty by which *the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the bitterness against "your descendants that will come after you" is the very enmity Yahuah decreed: *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15).$n$,$n$Come and see the old lie quoted back and judged. *Elohim (God) said again to Eve, "What is that he promised you in the garden, saying, 'As soon as you eat from the tree, your eyes will be opened, and you shall become like gods, knowing good and evil.' But look! He has burnt your bodies with fire"* (1 Adam and Eve 46:6); *"as to the Godhead he cannot give it to you... No, he was bitter against you and your descendants, that will come after you"* (1 Adam and Eve 46:7). It ain't new — this is the serpent's first sentence verbatim: *For Elohim (God) doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil* (Genesis 3:5), the subtilty by which *the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty* (2 Corinthians 11:3). And the bitterness against "your descendants that will come after you" is the very enmity Yahuah decreed: *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel* (Genesis 3:15).$n$),
(11049,$n$Adam and Eve, blind with sorrow, climb the border of the garden until they stand at the gate they may no longer enter: *And the cherub who guarded the garden was standing at the western gate, and guarding it against Adam and Eve, lest they should suddenly come into the garden* (1-adam-eve 54:3); *suddenly came the cherub with a flashing sword of fire in his hand* (1-adam-eve 54:4). This is the very scene Moses sealed at the close of Eden: *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken* (Genesis 3:23), and *he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life* (Genesis 3:24). Jubilees keeps the same memory of the sending-forth: *And He made for them coats of skin, and clothed them, and sent them forth from the Garden of Eden* (Jubilees 3:26). Enoch was carried to the same garden and shown the tree that put them outside it, and the angel told him whose parents had eaten from it: *Then Raphael the holy angel, who was with me, answered me and said: ‘This is the tree of wisdom, of which thy father old (in years) and thy aged mother, who were before thee, have eaten, and they learnt wisdom and their eyes were opened, and they knew that they were naked and they were driven out of the garden.’* (1 Enoch 32:6). From the first day outside the garden the way to life is guarded, and it stays guarded until the Lamb opens it again: *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city* (Revelation 22:14).$n$,$n$Adam and Eve, blind with sorrow, climb the border of the garden until they stand at the gate they may no longer enter: *And the cherub who guarded the garden was standing at the western gate, and guarding it against Adam and Eve, lest they should suddenly come into the garden* (1 Adam and Eve 54:3); *suddenly came the cherub with a flashing sword of fire in his hand* (1 Adam and Eve 54:4). This is the very scene Moses sealed at the close of Eden: *Therefore Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken* (Genesis 3:23), and *he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life* (Genesis 3:24). Jubilees keeps the same memory of the sending-forth: *And He made for them coats of skin, and clothed them, and sent them forth from the Garden of Eden* (Jubilees 3:26). Enoch was carried to the same garden and shown the tree that put them outside it, and the angel told him whose parents had eaten from it: *Then Raphael the holy angel, who was with me, answered me and said: ‘This is the tree of wisdom, of which thy father old (in years) and thy aged mother, who were before thee, have eaten, and they learnt wisdom and their eyes were opened, and they knew that they were naked and they were driven out of the garden.’* (1 Enoch 32:6). From the first day outside the garden the way to life is guarded, and it stays guarded until the Lamb opens it again: *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city* (Revelation 22:14).$n$),
(11051,$n$Before the flaming presence Adam and Eve collapse: *they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead* (1-adam-eve 54:8); *At that time the heavens and the earth shook; and another cherubim came down from heaven* (1-adam-eve 54:9). This is the unfailing measure of mortal flesh before the holy — Daniel falls the same way: *Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground* (Daniel 10:9); and John on Patmos: *And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not* (Revelation 1:17). At the empty tomb the guards meet the same shaking and the same terror: *And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of Yahuah (Lord) descended from heaven* (Matthew 28:2); *And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men* (Matthew 28:4). It ain't new: the dread of the guarding angel at the gate of life is the dread of the rolling angel at the gate of the grave.$n$,$n$Before the flaming presence Adam and Eve collapse: *they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead* (1 Adam and Eve 54:8); *At that time the heavens and the earth shook; and another cherubim came down from heaven* (1 Adam and Eve 54:9). This is the unfailing measure of mortal flesh before the holy — Daniel falls the same way: *Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground* (Daniel 10:9); and John on Patmos: *And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not* (Revelation 1:17). At the empty tomb the guards meet the same shaking and the same terror: *And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of Yahuah (Lord) descended from heaven* (Matthew 28:2); *And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men* (Matthew 28:4). It ain't new: the dread of the guarding angel at the gate of life is the dread of the rolling angel at the gate of the grave.$n$),
(11052,$n$The host gathers about the fallen pair: *Then, again, other angels came down close to the place where Adam and Eve were. They were divided between joy and sorrow* (1-adam-eve 54:10) — glad in hope of his return, grieving over the man fallen like the dead. These guarding, descending, fiery messengers are exactly what Scripture names them: *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* (Psalm 104:4); *And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire* (Hebrews 1:7). And their errand of mercy over the fallen heirs of Adam is no idle watching: *Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?* (Hebrews 1:14). It ain't new: the angels that watch and weep over Adam at the gate are the same flame-of-fire spirits sent to minister to the heirs of the very salvation Yahuah promised the man.$n$,$n$The host gathers about the fallen pair: *Then, again, other angels came down close to the place where Adam and Eve were. They were divided between joy and sorrow* (1 Adam and Eve 54:10) — glad in hope of his return, grieving over the man fallen like the dead. These guarding, descending, fiery messengers are exactly what Scripture names them: *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire* (Psalm 104:4); *And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire* (Hebrews 1:7). And their errand of mercy over the fallen heirs of Adam is no idle watching: *Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?* (Hebrews 1:14). It ain't new: the angels that watch and weep over Adam at the gate are the same flame-of-fire spirits sent to minister to the heirs of the very salvation Yahuah promised the man.$n$),
(11100,$n$Satan has worked his ruin, but the Logos answers him: *Elohim (God), therefore, sent His Word, and raised up Adam and Eve from their state of death.* (1-adam-eve 68:2) — the same Word *In the beginning... and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). When Adam pleads, the Word names the true hand behind the burnt corn and the spilled water: *But it is Satan, your master who did it... and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie* (1-adam-eve 68:5) — for Yahusha said of him, *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him... for he is a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44), and Satan *himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden the serpent strikes at the seed, yet Yahuah keeps it — *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$,$n$Satan has worked his ruin, but the Logos answers him: *Elohim (God), therefore, sent His Word, and raised up Adam and Eve from their state of death.* (1 Adam and Eve 68:2) — the same Word *In the beginning... and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1), *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made* (John 1:3). When Adam pleads, the Word names the true hand behind the burnt corn and the spilled water: *But it is Satan, your master who did it... and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie* (1 Adam and Eve 68:5) — for Yahusha said of him, *He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him... for he is a liar, and the father of it* (John 8:44), and Satan *himself is transformed into an angel of light* (2 Corinthians 11:14). It ain't new: from the first day outside the garden the serpent strikes at the seed, yet Yahuah keeps it — *I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head* (Genesis 3:15).$n$),
(11102,$n$Adam resolves to bring the offering *three times every week, on the fourth day Wednesday, on the preparation day Friday, and on the Sabbath* (1-adam-eve 68:20), and the Word turns his choice into prophecy: *you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday* (1-adam-eve 68:22). So it came — *it was the preparation of the passover... Behold your King!* (John 19:14); *because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day* (John 19:31). Then the Word names the first day for joy: *through My rising again on this day, will I create joy, and raise them on high, who believe in Me* (1-adam-eve 68:23) — *when Yahusha (Jesus) was risen early the first day of the week* (Mark 16:9). The flesh in which He suffers comes *when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman* (Galatians 4:4), the Lamb *foreordained before the foundation of the world* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$,$n$Adam resolves to bring the offering *three times every week, on the fourth day Wednesday, on the preparation day Friday, and on the Sabbath* (1 Adam and Eve 68:20), and the Word turns his choice into prophecy: *you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday* (1 Adam and Eve 68:22). So it came — *it was the preparation of the passover... Behold your King!* (John 19:14); *because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day* (John 19:31). Then the Word names the first day for joy: *through My rising again on this day, will I create joy, and raise them on high, who believe in Me* (1 Adam and Eve 68:23) — *when Yahusha (Jesus) was risen early the first day of the week* (Mark 16:9). The flesh in which He suffers comes *when the fulness of the time was come, Elohim (God) sent forth his Son, made of a woman* (Galatians 4:4), the Lamb *foreordained before the foundation of the world* (1 Peter 1:20).$n$),
(11125,$n$Eve's first labour, far from the cave of treasures, fulfils to the letter the word spoken at the gate of Eden. *When the time came for her to give birth, she strained a lot. Adam felt sorry, and he was very worried about her because she was close to death and the words of Elohim (God) to her were being fulfilled: "In suffering shall you bear a child, and in sorrow shall you bring forth a child."* (1-adam-eve 74:3). It ain't new — the sentence was passed already: *Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.* (Genesis 3:16). Yet the same Yahuah who pronounced the sorrow hears Adam's cry and delivers her — mercy travels with the curse. *And Elohim (God) looked at His maid-servant Eve, and delivered her, and she gave birth to her first-born son, and with him a daughter.* (1-adam-eve 74:5).$n$,$n$Eve's first labour, far from the cave of treasures, fulfils to the letter the word spoken at the gate of Eden. *When the time came for her to give birth, she strained a lot. Adam felt sorry, and he was very worried about her because she was close to death and the words of Elohim (God) to her were being fulfilled: "In suffering shall you bear a child, and in sorrow shall you bring forth a child."* (1 Adam and Eve 74:3). It ain't new — the sentence was passed already: *Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.* (Genesis 3:16). Yet the same Yahuah who pronounced the sorrow hears Adam's cry and delivers her — mercy travels with the curse. *And Elohim (God) looked at His maid-servant Eve, and delivered her, and she gave birth to her first-born son, and with him a daughter.* (1 Adam and Eve 74:5).$n$),
(11126,$n$The first child born outside Eden is named for the hatred already in him. *The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.* (1-adam-eve 74:7). The enmity put between the seeds at the gate of the garden is not a thing of the future — it is in the womb. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The other primeval witnesses keep the same order — Cain first, then Abel, then a daughter: *And in the third week in the second jubilee she gave birth to Cain, and in the fourth she gave birth to Abel, and in the fifth she gave birth to her daughter 'Âwân.* (Jubilees 4:1). And the apostle reads Cain back to its true father: *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* (1 John 3:12).$n$,$n$The first child born outside Eden is named for the hatred already in him. *The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.* (1 Adam and Eve 74:7). The enmity put between the seeds at the gate of the garden is not a thing of the future — it is in the womb. *And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* (Genesis 3:15). The other primeval witnesses keep the same order — Cain first, then Abel, then a daughter: *And in the third week in the second jubilee she gave birth to Cain, and in the fourth she gave birth to Abel, and in the fifth she gave birth to her daughter 'Âwân.* (Jubilees 4:1). And the apostle reads Cain back to its true father: *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother's righteous.* (1 John 3:12).$n$),
(11127,$n$Cain named "hater" before he draws a second breath foreshadows the first murder and the parting of the two seed-lines. *The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.* (1-adam-eve 74:7). Scripture later sets his works against his brother's: *Woe unto them! for they have gone in the way of Cain, and ran greedily after the error of Balaam for reward, and perished in the gainsaying of Core.* (Jude 1:11) — "the way of Cain" is a road, a lineage of works. Over against it stands the witness of faith: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, Elohim (God) testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.* (Hebrews 11:4). The serpent's striker and the woman's seed are present in the cradle.$n$,$n$Cain named "hater" before he draws a second breath foreshadows the first murder and the parting of the two seed-lines. *The meaning of Cain is "hater," because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adam named him Cain.* (1 Adam and Eve 74:7). Scripture later sets his works against his brother's: *Woe unto them! for they have gone in the way of Cain, and ran greedily after the error of Balaam for reward, and perished in the gainsaying of Core.* (Jude 1:11) — "the way of Cain" is a road, a lineage of works. Over against it stands the witness of faith: *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, Elohim (God) testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.* (Hebrews 11:4). The serpent's striker and the woman's seed are present in the cradle.$n$),
(11128,$n$Forty days after the birth, Adam sets an offering for his children — the sacrifices of the covenant line, kept generations before the mountain. *Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."* (1-adam-eve 74:9). This is the same Adam who, leaving Eden, kept the sweet savour: *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* (Jubilees 3:27). The children he offers for will themselves bring offerings — *And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:3) — and the Name kept by this line is the same Name men called upon from the beginning: *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26).$n$,$n$Forty days after the birth, Adam sets an offering for his children — the sacrifices of the covenant line, kept generations before the mountain. *Then Adam and Eve waited until Cain and his sister were forty days old, when Adam said to Eve, "We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children."* (1 Adam and Eve 74:9). This is the same Adam who, leaving Eden, kept the sweet savour: *And on that day on which Adam went forth from the garden, he offered as a sweet savour an offering, frankincense, galbanum, and stacte, and spices in the morning with the rising of the sun from the day when he covered his shame.* (Jubilees 3:27). The children he offers for will themselves bring offerings — *And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:3) — and the Name kept by this line is the same Name men called upon from the beginning: *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* (Genesis 4:26).$n$),
(11198,$n$Dying Seth adjures his sons by the blood of Abel to keep the holy mountain and never mingle with Cain's line: *I beg of you my children, not to let one of you go down from this Holy and pure Mountain. Make no fellowship with the children of Cain the murderer and the sinner, who killed his brother; for ye know, 0 my children, that we flee from him, and from all his sin with all our might because he killed his brother Abel.* (2-adam-eve 12:10-11). This is the two-seed war set in the genealogy: Seth himself was given as the appointed seed in Abel's room — *Adam knew his wife again; and she bare a son, and called his name Seth: For Elohim (God), said she, hath appointed me another seed instead of Abel, whom Cain slew* (Genesis 4:25). The line below is the serpent's: *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother* (1 John 3:12); they who follow it *have gone in the way of Cain* (Jude 1:11). Jubilees carries the same two houses — *Elohim (God) has raised up a second seed to us on the earth instead of Abel; for Cain slew him* (Jubilees 4:7) — while Cain built his city below.$n$,$n$Dying Seth adjures his sons by the blood of Abel to keep the holy mountain and never mingle with Cain's line: *I beg of you my children, not to let one of you go down from this Holy and pure Mountain. Make no fellowship with the children of Cain the murderer and the sinner, who killed his brother; for ye know, 0 my children, that we flee from him, and from all his sin with all our might because he killed his brother Abel.* (2 Adam and Eve 12:10-11). This is the two-seed war set in the genealogy: Seth himself was given as the appointed seed in Abel's room — *Adam knew his wife again; and she bare a son, and called his name Seth: For Elohim (God), said she, hath appointed me another seed instead of Abel, whom Cain slew* (Genesis 4:25). The line below is the serpent's: *Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother* (1 John 3:12); they who follow it *have gone in the way of Cain* (Jude 1:11). Jubilees carries the same two houses — *Elohim (God) has raised up a second seed to us on the earth instead of Abel; for Cain slew him* (Jubilees 4:7) — while Cain built his city below.$n$);
